// 短文閱讀題庫（Part 6、7 風格，原創）：id, lv, p=6/7, k=類型, ti, tx, zh, w=用到的單字 id, qs=[{q,o,a,ex}]
window.QUIZ_READ = [{"id":"r400-01","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Your order is on the way","tx":"To: Kevin Wu\nFrom: Bright Home Store\nSubject: Your order is on the way\n\nDear Mr. Wu,\n\nThank you for shopping with us. We sent your desk lamp this morning. We will deliver it to your home on Thursday. The receipt is attached to this e-mail.\n\nIf the item is damaged, please contact us within seven days. We will replace it or give you a full refund.\n\nBright Home Store","zh":"收件人：Kevin Wu\n寄件人：Bright Home Store\n主旨：您的訂單已在配送途中\n\nWu 先生您好：\n\n感謝您的購買。我們今天早上已經寄出您的檯燈，會在星期四送到您家。收據已附在這封電子郵件裡。\n\n如果商品有損壞，請在七天內與我們聯絡。我們會為您更換，或是全額退款。\n\nBright Home Store","w":[179,15,219,34,242,230,212,119,2],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the e-mail?","o":["To say that an order has been sent","To advertise a new lamp","To cancel an order","To ask for a payment"],"a":0,"ex":"信中寫 We sent your desk lamp this morning（我們今天早上寄出了您的檯燈），目的是通知訂單已經寄出。文中沒有要求付款、沒有推銷新的檯燈，也沒有取消訂單。"},{"q":"When will the lamp arrive at Mr. Wu's home?","o":["This morning","On Tuesday","On Thursday","In seven days"],"a":2,"ex":"We will deliver it to your home on Thursday，星期四會送到家。this morning 是商店寄出的時間，seven days 是商品損壞時要聯絡商店的期限，文中沒有提到星期二。"},{"q":"What will the store do if the lamp is damaged?","o":["Repair it at Mr. Wu's home","Give a discount on the next order","Send another receipt","Send a new one or give the money back"],"a":3,"ex":"We will replace it or give you a full refund，replace 是「更換」，full refund 是「全額退款」，也就是換一個新的或把錢退回。文中沒有提到到府修理、下次購物折扣或再寄一張收據。"}]},
{"id":"r400-02","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"Third floor printer is not working","tx":"NOTICE: Third Floor Printer\n\nThe printer on the third floor is not working. A repair person will come on Wednesday morning. Until then, please use the printer on the second floor, next to the elevator.\n\nPlease do not try to repair the printer yourself. If you need to print many pages, contact Ms. Park in the IT department.\n\nThank you.","zh":"公告：三樓印表機\n\n三樓的印表機故障了。維修人員會在星期三早上過來。在那之前，請使用二樓電梯旁邊的印表機。\n\n請不要自己動手修理印表機。如果需要列印很多頁，請聯絡資訊部門的 Park 小姐。\n\n謝謝。","w":[16,232,230,35],"qs":[{"q":"What is the notice mainly about?","o":["A new elevator in the building","A meeting with Ms. Park","A change in office hours","A printer that is broken"],"a":3,"ex":"第一句 The printer on the third floor is not working（三樓的印表機故障了），整篇公告都在講這台壞掉的印表機。電梯只是用來說明二樓印表機的位置，文中沒有提到上班時間或會議。"},{"q":"Where is the printer that people should use now?","o":["On the third floor","On the second floor","In the IT department","In Ms. Park's office"],"a":1,"ex":"please use the printer on the second floor，請大家先用二樓的印表機。三樓的那台壞了；IT department 的 Ms. Park 是要印很多頁時的聯絡對象，不是印表機的位置。"},{"q":"The word \"repair\" in the notice is closest in meaning to","o":["clean","fix","buy","move"],"a":1,"ex":"repair 是「修理」，和 fix 意思最接近。印表機 is not working（故障），所以需要有人來修。move 是搬動、buy 是購買、clean 是清潔。"}]},
{"id":"r400-03","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Annual Summer Sale at Sunny Shoes","tx":"Sunny Shoes — Annual Summer Sale!\n\nFrom July 1 to July 7, all shoes are 30% off. We have a wide selection of popular brands for men, women, and children. Bags are also on sale at a 10% discount.\n\nThe quantity is limited, so come early! The store is open from 10 A.M. to 9 P.M. every day. Sorry, we cannot give refunds on sale items.","zh":"Sunny Shoes——年度夏季特賣！\n\n7 月 1 日到 7 月 7 日，全部鞋款打七折。我們有多種熱門品牌可以挑選，男鞋、女鞋、童鞋都有。包包也有九折優惠。\n\n數量有限，請早點來！本店每天從上午 10 點營業到晚上 9 點。很抱歉，特賣商品無法退款。","w":[146,57,25,111,60,144,119,34],"qs":[{"q":"What is being advertised?","o":["A shoe repair service","A job at a shoe store","The opening of a new store","A sale at a shoe store"],"a":3,"ex":"標題 Annual Summer Sale，內文說 all shoes are 30% off，是鞋店的特賣活動廣告。文中沒有提到新店開幕、徵人或修鞋服務。"},{"q":"How much is the discount on bags?","o":["30%","10%","50%","7%"],"a":1,"ex":"Bags are also on sale at a 10% discount，包包的折扣是 10%（九折）。30% 是鞋子的折扣，7 是特賣結束的日期 July 7，文中沒有出現 50%。"},{"q":"Why are customers told to come early?","o":["The store closes at noon","Early shoppers get a free bag","The number of sale items is limited","The sale is only for one day"],"a":2,"ex":"The quantity is limited, so come early!，quantity is limited 是「數量有限」，所以要早點來。商店開到晚上 9 點，不是中午就關；特賣從 July 1 到 July 7 共七天；文中沒有說早來可以拿到免費的包包。"}]},
{"id":"r400-04","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"message","ti":"My flight is late","tx":"Dana Kim (9:12 A.M.): Hi, Tom. My flight is late because of bad weather. I will reach the office at about 2 P.M.\n\nTom Reyes (9:15 A.M.): OK. The client meeting is at 1 P.M. Should I cancel it?\n\nDana Kim (9:17 A.M.): No, please don't. Can you move it to 3 P.M.? Our client, Ms. Ito, said she is available all afternoon.\n\nTom Reyes (9:18 A.M.): Sure. I will call her now.","zh":"Dana Kim（上午 9:12）：嗨，Tom。因為天氣不好，我的班機延誤了。我大約下午 2 點才會到辦公室。\n\nTom Reyes（上午 9:15）：好的。和客戶的會議是下午 1 點。要我取消嗎？\n\nDana Kim（上午 9:17）：不，請不要取消。可以幫我改到下午 3 點嗎？我們的客戶 Ito 小姐說她整個下午都有空。\n\nTom Reyes（上午 9:18）：沒問題。我現在就打電話給她。","w":[24,216,38,176,139],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Ms. Kim write to Mr. Reyes?","o":["To ask about the weather","To say that she will arrive late","To book a flight","To invite him to lunch"],"a":1,"ex":"Ms. Kim 一開始就說 My flight is late（我的班機延誤了），而且 I will reach the office at about 2 P.M.，所以是通知對方她會晚到。她沒有要訂機票、沒有邀請對方吃午餐，也不是在問天氣。"},{"q":"What time will the client meeting most likely start?","o":["2 P.M.","9 A.M.","1 P.M.","3 P.M."],"a":3,"ex":"Ms. Kim 問 Can you move it to 3 P.M.?，Mr. Reyes 回答 Sure，所以會議最可能改到下午 3 點。1 P.M. 是原本的時間，2 P.M. 是 Ms. Kim 到辦公室的時間，早上 9 點多是他們傳訊息的時間。"},{"q":"What will Mr. Reyes probably do next?","o":["Go to the airport","Call Ms. Ito","Book a new flight","Cancel the meeting"],"a":1,"ex":"最後一句 I will call her now，her 指的是客戶 Ms. Ito，所以他接下來會打電話給她。Ms. Kim 說 No, please don't，所以不會取消會議；文中也沒有提到去機場或訂新的班機。"}]},
{"id":"r400-05","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"form","ti":"Order confirmation: Maple Office Supplies","tx":"Maple Office Supplies\nOrder Confirmation\n\nOrder number: 4521\nCustomer: Ms. Lisa Chang\nOrder date: May 3\n\nItems:\nPrinter paper, 5 boxes: $40\nBlue pens, 20: $10\nDelivery fee: $5\nTotal amount: $55\n\nPayment: Paid by credit card\nDelivery date: May 6\n\nQuestions? Contact us at 555-0142. Please keep this page as your receipt.","zh":"Maple Office Supplies\n訂單確認單\n\n訂單編號：4521\n顧客：Lisa Chang 小姐\n訂購日期：5 月 3 日\n\n品項：\n印表機用紙，5 箱：40 美元\n藍色原子筆，20 支：10 美元\n運費：5 美元\n總金額：55 美元\n\n付款：已用信用卡付款\n送貨日期：5 月 6 日\n\n有問題嗎？請撥 555-0142 與我們聯絡。請保留此頁作為收據。","w":[34,16,7,5,29,230,15],"qs":[{"q":"What did Ms. Chang order?","o":["A printer and pens","Pens and notebooks","Boxes and a desk","Paper and pens"],"a":3,"ex":"Items 底下列了 Printer paper（印表機用紙）和 Blue pens（藍色原子筆），所以她訂的是紙和筆。Printer paper 是「印表機用的紙」，不是印表機；表單上也沒有書桌或筆記本。"},{"q":"How much is the delivery fee?","o":["$55","$40","$5","$10"],"a":2,"ex":"Delivery fee: $5，運費是 5 美元。$10 是筆的價錢，$40 是紙的價錢，$55 是 Total amount（總金額）。"},{"q":"What is NOT shown on the form?","o":["The order number","The delivery date","The total amount","The customer's address"],"a":3,"ex":"表單上有 Order number: 4521（訂單編號）、Delivery date: May 6（送貨日期）和 Total amount: $55（總金額），但是沒有寫顧客的地址。"}]},
{"id":"r400-06","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"review","ti":"A good stay at Lakeside Hotel","tx":"Lakeside Hotel — Review by Mark T.\nRating: 4 out of 5\n\nI stayed at the Lakeside Hotel for three nights on a business trip. My room was clean and quiet, and the staff was very friendly. The receptionist helped me book a taxi to the airport. The hotel is also near the train station.\n\nMy only complaint is the breakfast. There was not much variety. Still, I recommend this hotel.","zh":"Lakeside Hotel——Mark T. 的評論\n評分：4 分（滿分 5 分）\n\n我因為出差，在 Lakeside Hotel 住了三個晚上。房間乾淨又安靜，員工也非常親切。接待人員幫我預訂了去機場的計程車。飯店離火車站也很近。\n\n我唯一的抱怨是早餐，菜色變化不多。不過，我還是推薦這家飯店。","w":[40,32,185,95,82,208],"qs":[{"q":"What is the review about?","o":["A taxi company","A stay at a hotel","A train trip","A meal at a restaurant"],"a":1,"ex":"I stayed at the Lakeside Hotel for three nights，整篇在評論住飯店的經驗。計程車和火車站只是順帶提到；早餐是飯店的早餐，不是在評論餐廳。"},{"q":"What did the receptionist do for the writer?","o":["Booked a taxi","Made breakfast","Cleaned the room","Carried the bags"],"a":0,"ex":"The receptionist helped me book a taxi to the airport，接待人員幫他預訂了去機場的計程車。文中沒有說接待人員打掃房間、提行李或做早餐。"},{"q":"What did the writer NOT like about the hotel?","o":["The staff","The breakfast","The room","The location"],"a":1,"ex":"My only complaint is the breakfast，complaint 是「抱怨」，他唯一不滿意的是早餐。房間 clean and quiet、員工 very friendly、飯店 near the train station，這些他都覺得很好。"}]},
{"id":"r400-07","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"announcement","ti":"Flight 208: new time and gate","tx":"Attention, passengers on Flight 208 to Tokyo.\n\nBecause of heavy rain, the departure time has changed. The flight will now leave at 4:30 P.M., not 3:00 P.M. The gate has also changed from Gate 12 to Gate 5 in the same terminal.\n\nPassengers can get a free beverage at the café near Gate 5. Please show your ticket to the cashier. We apologize for the delay.","zh":"搭乘 208 號班機前往東京的旅客請注意。\n\n由於大雨，起飛時間已經更改。班機將改在下午 4:30 起飛，而不是下午 3:00。登機門也從 12 號改為同一航廈的 5 號登機門。\n\n旅客可以在 5 號登機門附近的咖啡店免費領取一杯飲料。請向收銀員出示您的機票。造成延誤，我們深感抱歉。","w":[1,24,67,99,86,4,180],"qs":[{"q":"What is the announcement mainly about?","o":["A lost ticket","A new café at the airport","A change to a flight","A cheaper flight to Tokyo"],"a":2,"ex":"the departure time has changed 和 The gate has also changed，公告主要在說班機的起飛時間和登機門改了。咖啡店只是領免費飲料的地方，文中沒有提到遺失機票或比較便宜的班機。"},{"q":"Which gate should passengers go to now?","o":["Gate 5","Gate 12","Gate 3","Gate 4"],"a":0,"ex":"The gate has also changed from Gate 12 to Gate 5，登機門從 12 號改成 5 號，所以現在要去 5 號登機門。Gate 12 是原本的登機門；3 和 4 只是時間 3:00、4:30 裡的數字，不是登機門。"},{"q":"What can passengers get for free?","o":["A drink","A taxi ride","A new ticket","A meal"],"a":0,"ex":"Passengers can get a free beverage，beverage 是「飲料」，也就是 a drink。文中沒有提到免費的餐點、新機票或計程車。"}]},
{"id":"r400-08","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"memo","ti":"Sales meeting moves to Tuesday","tx":"MEMO\nTo: All sales staff\nFrom: Helen Brooks, Sales Manager\nDate: March 4\n\nNext week, our regular Monday sales meeting will move to Tuesday because Monday is a holiday. The meeting will start at 10 A.M. in Meeting Room B.\n\nAll staff must attend. Please bring your sales figures for February. We will also talk about our targets for April. If you cannot come, tell me by Friday.","zh":"備忘錄\n收件人：全體業務人員\n寄件人：業務經理 Helen Brooks\n日期：3 月 4 日\n\n下星期，我們固定在星期一舉行的業務會議將改到星期二，因為星期一是假日。會議將於上午 10 點在 B 會議室開始。\n\n全體人員都必須出席。請帶二月份的銷售數字。我們也會討論四月份的目標。如果無法出席，請在星期五之前告訴我。","w":[40,137,175,69,112],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the memo?","o":["To ask about holiday plans","To welcome new staff","To report February sales","To announce a change of meeting day"],"a":3,"ex":"our regular Monday sales meeting will move to Tuesday，目的是通知會議從星期一改到星期二。二月的銷售數字是開會要帶的資料，不是這份備忘錄在報告的內容；文中沒有歡迎新人，也沒有詢問假期計畫。"},{"q":"When is next week's sales meeting?","o":["Tuesday at 10 A.M.","Monday at 10 A.M.","Tuesday at 2 P.M.","Friday at 10 A.M."],"a":0,"ex":"will move to Tuesday 加上 The meeting will start at 10 A.M.，所以是星期二上午 10 點。星期一是假日，所以才改期；星期五是告知無法出席的期限。"},{"q":"The word \"figures\" in the memo is closest in meaning to","o":["pictures","people","numbers","shapes"],"a":2,"ex":"sales figures 是「銷售數字」，所以這裡的 figures 意思最接近 numbers（數字）。figure 也可以指人物或形狀，但是和 sales 一起用時指的是業績數字；pictures 是圖片。"}]},
{"id":"r400-09","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"New bakery opens on Lake Street","tx":"New Bakery Opens Downtown\n\nSweet Morning Bakery opened last Saturday on Lake Street. The owner, Ms. Rosa Diaz, has ten years of experience as a hotel baker. Now she has her own shop.\n\nThe bakery sells bread, cakes, and various beverages. Ms. Diaz buys her fruit and milk from local farms. \"I want to support local farmers,\" she said. The shop is open every day except Monday.","zh":"市中心新麵包店開幕\n\nSweet Morning Bakery 上星期六在 Lake Street 開幕。老闆 Rosa Diaz 小姐有十年在飯店當麵包師傅的經驗，現在她有了自己的店。\n\n這家麵包店販售麵包、蛋糕和各種飲料。Diaz 小姐的水果和牛奶都是向當地農場買的。她說：「我想支持當地的農民。」這家店除了星期一以外，每天都營業。","w":[106,148,86,164,235],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article about?","o":["A new shop in town","A hotel restaurant","A baking class","A farm that sells fruit"],"a":0,"ex":"標題 New Bakery Opens Downtown 和第一句 Sweet Morning Bakery opened last Saturday，都在說一家新開的麵包店。飯店是老闆以前工作的地方，農場是她買水果和牛奶的地方，文中沒有提到烘焙課。"},{"q":"When is the bakery closed?","o":["On Sundays","On holidays","On Mondays","On Saturdays"],"a":2,"ex":"The shop is open every day except Monday，except 是「除了…以外」，所以只有星期一不營業。Saturday 是開幕的那一天，文中沒有說星期日或假日休息。"},{"q":"What is suggested about Ms. Diaz?","o":["She is new to baking","She grows her own fruit","She wants to help farmers in her area","She plans to open a hotel"],"a":2,"ex":"她說 I want to support local farmers，support 是「支持」、local 是「當地的」，所以她想幫助當地的農民。她的水果是向農場買的，不是自己種的；她有 ten years of experience，不是新手；文中沒有說她要開飯店。"}]},
{"id":"r400-10","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"letter","ti":"Your new savings account","tx":"Stone Bridge Bank\n\nDear Mr. Allen,\n\nThank you for opening a savings account at Stone Bridge Bank. Your bank card will arrive by mail within five days.\n\nBefore you use the card, please call 555-0177 to create a personal password. To keep your account secure, do not tell anyone your password.\n\nIf you have any questions, please visit your local Stone Bridge Bank or contact us by phone.\n\nSincerely,\nNina Ford\nCustomer Service","zh":"Stone Bridge Bank\n\nAllen 先生您好：\n\n感謝您在 Stone Bridge Bank 開立儲蓄帳戶。您的金融卡將在五天內郵寄送達。\n\n使用卡片之前，請先撥打 555-0177 設定個人密碼。為了保護帳戶安全，請不要把密碼告訴任何人。\n\n如果有任何問題，請到您當地的 Stone Bridge Bank，或是打電話與我們聯絡。\n\n敬上\nNina Ford\n客戶服務部","w":[30,183,135,168,164,230],"qs":[{"q":"Why did the bank write to Mr. Allen?","o":["To say that his card was lost","To offer him a loan","To give information about his new account","To ask him to pay a fee"],"a":2,"ex":"信的開頭 Thank you for opening a savings account，接著說明金融卡和密碼的事，所以是提供新帳戶的相關資訊。文中沒有要他付費、沒有提供貸款，也沒有說卡片遺失。"},{"q":"How will Mr. Allen get his bank card?","o":["By e-mail","By mail","From a bank machine","From Ms. Ford in person"],"a":1,"ex":"Your bank card will arrive by mail within five days，by mail 是「用郵寄的」。文中沒有說用電子郵件寄、由 Ms. Ford 親自交給他，或是從機器領取。"},{"q":"The word \"secure\" in the letter is closest in meaning to","o":["busy","new","open","safe"],"a":3,"ex":"To keep your account secure 是「為了讓帳戶保持安全」，secure 和 safe 意思最接近，所以後面才說不要把密碼告訴別人。open 是開著的、new 是新的、busy 是忙碌的。"}]},
{"id":"r400-11","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Now hiring: receptionist","tx":"Now Hiring: Receptionist\n\nPine Street Clinic is seeking a full-time receptionist. The job starts on June 1.\n\nTasks: answer the phone, welcome visitors, and arrange appointments.\nYou need: one year of office experience and basic computer skills.\nHours: Monday to Friday, 9 A.M. to 6 P.M.\n\nTo apply, send your résumé to Ms. Gomez by May 15. We will contact you for an interview.","zh":"徵才：接待人員\n\nPine Street Clinic 誠徵全職接待人員。工作從 6 月 1 日開始。\n\n工作內容：接聽電話、接待訪客、安排預約。\n條件：一年辦公室工作經驗及基本電腦能力。\n上班時間：星期一到星期五，上午 9 點到下午 6 點。\n\n想應徵的人，請在 5 月 15 日前把履歷寄給 Gomez 小姐。我們會與您聯絡安排面試。","w":[202,32,6,221,11,205,8,106,197,230,231],"qs":[{"q":"What job is being advertised?","o":["A nurse","A cleaner","A computer teacher","A receptionist"],"a":3,"ex":"標題 Now Hiring: Receptionist，而且第一句說 is seeking a full-time receptionist，徵的是接待人員。雖然地點是診所，但徵的不是護理師；computer skills 只是應徵條件，不是要找電腦老師；文中也沒有提到清潔人員。"},{"q":"What is NOT a task of the job?","o":["Welcoming visitors","Answering the phone","Arranging appointments","Cleaning the office"],"a":3,"ex":"Tasks 列出 answer the phone, welcome visitors, and arrange appointments 三項工作，沒有提到打掃辦公室。"},{"q":"What must people who want the job do by May 15?","o":["Call the clinic","Start the job","Come for an interview","Send a résumé"],"a":3,"ex":"To apply, send your résumé to Ms. Gomez by May 15，想應徵的人必須在 5 月 15 日前寄出履歷。June 1 才開始上班；面試要等診所聯絡之後才安排；文中沒有要求打電話。"}]},
{"id":"r400-12","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"East elevator closed on Friday","tx":"Oak Tower Apartments — Notice\n\nThe east elevator will be closed on Friday, April 12, from 9 A.M. to 3 P.M. Workers will replace some old parts.\n\nDuring this period, please use the west elevator or the stairs. If you need help with heavy items, contact the front desk in the lobby. We apologize for the trouble.\n\nBuilding Management","zh":"Oak Tower Apartments——公告\n\n東側電梯將於 4 月 12 日星期五上午 9 點到下午 3 點暫停使用。工人要更換一些老舊的零件。\n\n在這段期間，請使用西側電梯或樓梯。如果您需要有人幫忙搬重物，請聯絡大廳的櫃台。造成不便，我們深感抱歉。\n\n大樓管理處","w":[212,43,34,230,13,180],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the notice?","o":["To say that an elevator will be closed","To announce new stairs","To welcome new neighbors","To ask people to move out"],"a":0,"ex":"The east elevator will be closed on Friday, April 12，公告是要通知大家東側電梯會暫停使用。樓梯只是替代的方式，文中沒有歡迎新鄰居，也沒有要大家搬走。"},{"q":"How long will the east elevator be closed?","o":["Two days","Three hours","Six hours","Nine hours"],"a":2,"ex":"from 9 A.M. to 3 P.M.，從上午 9 點到下午 3 點一共是六個小時。3 和 9 只是時間裡的數字；電梯只在星期五這一天關閉，不是兩天。"},{"q":"The word \"period\" in the notice is closest in meaning to","o":["place","rule","time","price"],"a":2,"ex":"During this period 是「在這段期間」，指電梯關閉的那六個小時，所以 period 和 time 意思最接近。place 是地方、price 是價格、rule 是規定。"}]},
{"id":"r400-13","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Your reservation at Garden View Hotel","tx":"To: Jason Lee\nFrom: Garden View Hotel\nSubject: Your reservation\n\nDear Mr. Lee,\n\nThis e-mail is to confirm your reservation. You booked a single room for two nights, from October 8 to October 10. The price is $90 per night, and breakfast is included.\n\nYou can check in after 3 P.M. If you need to cancel, please tell us at least 24 hours in advance.\n\nWe look forward to your visit.","zh":"收件人：Jason Lee\n寄件人：Garden View Hotel\n主旨：您的訂房\n\nLee 先生您好：\n\n這封電子郵件是要確認您的訂房。您預訂了一間單人房，共兩晚，從 10 月 8 日到 10 月 10 日。房價是每晚 90 美元，含早餐。\n\n您可以在下午 3 點以後辦理入住。如果需要取消，請至少提前 24 小時告訴我們。\n\n期待您的光臨。","w":[196,9,185,176,246,2],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the e-mail?","o":["To advertise a new hotel","To ask for a payment","To confirm a hotel booking","To cancel a reservation"],"a":2,"ex":"This e-mail is to confirm your reservation，confirm 是「確認」，目的是確認訂房。cancel 那一句只是說明想取消時該怎麼做；文中沒有推銷新飯店，也沒有要求付款。"},{"q":"How many nights will Mr. Lee stay?","o":["One","Two","Three","Eight"],"a":1,"ex":"You booked a single room for two nights，他訂了兩晚。single room 是「單人房」，不是住一晚；3 是可以入住的時間 3 P.M.；8 是入住日期 October 8 裡的數字。"},{"q":"What should Mr. Lee do if he needs to cancel?","o":["Send a letter","Call after 3 P.M.","Pay $90","Tell the hotel at least one day before"],"a":3,"ex":"please tell us at least 24 hours in advance，in advance 是「事先」，24 小時就是一天，所以要至少提前一天通知飯店。$90 是每晚的房價，3 P.M. 是可以入住的時間，文中沒有說要寄信。"}]},
{"id":"r400-14","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"message","ti":"Wrong ink from the supplier","tx":"Amy (10:02): Hi, Ben. We have a problem. The supplier sent the wrong ink for our printer.\n\nBen (10:05): Oh no. Did you contact them?\n\nAmy (10:06): Yes. They apologized and will deliver the right ink tomorrow morning.\n\nBen (10:08): But I need to print my sales report today.\n\nAmy (10:09): You can use the printer in the marketing department. I already got permission.\n\nBen (10:10): Great. Thanks!","zh":"Amy（10:02）：嗨，Ben。我們有個問題。供應商寄錯了我們印表機要用的墨水。\n\nBen（10:05）：糟糕。妳聯絡他們了嗎？\n\nAmy（10:06）：聯絡了。他們道了歉，明天早上會把正確的墨水送來。\n\nBen（10:08）：可是我今天就要列印我的業務報告。\n\nAmy（10:09）：你可以用行銷部門的印表機。我已經得到許可了。\n\nBen（10:10）：太好了，謝謝！","w":[97,16,230,180,179,35,41],"qs":[{"q":"What problem does Amy mention?","o":["A report is missing","The printer is broken","The supplier is closed","The wrong ink was sent"],"a":3,"ex":"Amy 說 The supplier sent the wrong ink for our printer，供應商寄錯了墨水。印表機本身沒有壞，報告也沒有不見；供應商有道歉並答應補寄，並沒有關門。"},{"q":"When will the right ink arrive?","o":["This afternoon","Tomorrow morning","Next week","Tomorrow night"],"a":1,"ex":"They apologized and will deliver the right ink tomorrow morning，正確的墨水明天早上會送到。文中沒有提到今天下午、明天晚上或下星期。"},{"q":"What will Ben most likely do today?","o":["Wait for the delivery","Print his report in another department","Buy ink at a store","Call the supplier"],"a":1,"ex":"Ben 說 I need to print my sales report today，Amy 回答 You can use the printer in the marketing department，Ben 說 Great，所以他今天會去行銷部門列印。墨水明天才到，他等不了；Amy 已經聯絡過供應商；文中沒有提到去商店買墨水。"}]},
{"id":"r400-15","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"form","ti":"City Museum: Saturday schedule","tx":"City Museum — Saturday Schedule\n\n10:00 A.M. Museum opens\n10:30 A.M. Guided tour (meet in the lobby)\n12:00 P.M. Lunch break — café on the second floor\n2:00 P.M. Talk by the author Paul Grant, Room 3\n4:00 P.M. Children's art class\n5:30 P.M. Museum closes\n\nAdmission: $8 for adults, free for children under 12.\nThe guided tour is free, but please reserve a place online.","zh":"City Museum——星期六行程表\n\n上午 10:00 博物館開館\n上午 10:30 導覽（在大廳集合）\n中午 12:00 午休——二樓咖啡廳\n下午 2:00 作家 Paul Grant 演講，3 號室\n下午 4:00 兒童美術課\n下午 5:30 博物館閉館\n\n門票：成人 8 美元，12 歲以下兒童免費。\n導覽免費，但請先在網路上預約名額。","w":[108,13,20,84,234],"qs":[{"q":"How much is admission for an adult?","o":["$8","$12","$3","It is free"],"a":0,"ex":"Admission: $8 for adults，admission 是「入場費」，成人是 8 美元。12 是兒童免費的年齡（under 12），3 是演講的地點 Room 3，免費入場的是 12 歲以下的兒童。"},{"q":"Who is Paul Grant?","o":["An art teacher","A museum cashier","A writer","A tour guide"],"a":2,"ex":"Talk by the author Paul Grant，author 是「作者、作家」，也就是 a writer。導覽和兒童美術課都沒有寫是誰負責，文中也沒有提到收銀員。"},{"q":"What must visitors do to join the guided tour?","o":["Come after lunch","Go to Room 3","Reserve a place online","Buy a tour ticket"],"a":2,"ex":"The guided tour is free, but please reserve a place online，導覽免費，但是要先在網路上預約。因為免費，所以不用買導覽票；導覽是 10:30，在午休之前；集合地點是 the lobby，不是 Room 3。"}]},
{"id":"r400-16","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"review","ti":"Blue Wave speaker: small and clear","tx":"Blue Wave Speaker — Review by Sara P.\nRating: 5 out of 5\n\nI bought this speaker last month for $35. It is small and portable, so I carry it in my bag every day. The sound is clear, even at high volume. The battery lasts about ten hours.\n\nThe only negative point is the manual. It is not detailed, so I watched a video to learn how to use the speaker. For this price, it is a real bargain.","zh":"Blue Wave 喇叭——Sara P. 的評論\n評分：5 分（滿分 5 分）\n\n我上個月用 35 美元買了這個喇叭。它體積小、方便攜帶，所以我每天都放在包包裡帶著走。即使音量開得很大，聲音還是很清楚。電池大約可以用十個小時。\n\n唯一的缺點是使用手冊。內容不夠詳細，所以我看了影片才學會怎麼使用這個喇叭。以這個價格來說，真的非常划算。","w":[154,33,140,104,161,129],"qs":[{"q":"What is the review about?","o":["A mobile phone","A music video","A small speaker","A travel bag"],"a":2,"ex":"I bought this speaker last month，而且說 It is small and portable，評論的是一個小喇叭。bag 只是她放喇叭的地方，video 是她用來學習使用方法的影片，文中沒有提到手機。"},{"q":"What does the writer say about the manual?","o":["It is easy to understand","It was not in the box","It does not give enough information","It is too long"],"a":2,"ex":"The only negative point is the manual. It is not detailed，detailed 是「詳細的」，手冊不夠詳細，也就是資訊不夠。她還要另外看影片才學會使用，所以手冊並不好懂；文中沒有說手冊太長，也沒有說盒子裡沒有手冊。"},{"q":"The word \"portable\" in the review is closest in meaning to","o":["hard to find","nice to look at","easy to break","easy to carry"],"a":3,"ex":"It is small and portable, so I carry it in my bag every day，因為 portable，所以可以每天放在包包裡帶著走，意思是 easy to carry（方便攜帶）。easy to break 是容易壞、hard to find 是很難找、nice to look at 是好看。"}]},
{"id":"r400-17","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"announcement","ti":"Sunrise Foods anniversary party","tx":"Sunrise Foods: Anniversary Party\n\nDear colleagues,\n\nNext month, Sunrise Foods will be 20 years old! To celebrate our anniversary, we will have a party on Friday, September 18, at 6 P.M. The venue is the Rose Garden Restaurant, next to our office.\n\nAll employees are invited. Dinner and beverages are free. Please respond to Ms. Ortiz in the HR department by September 10 so that we can reserve enough tables.","zh":"Sunrise Foods：周年慶祝派對\n\n各位同事：\n\n下個月，Sunrise Foods 就要滿 20 歲了！為了慶祝周年，我們將在 9 月 18 日星期五下午 6 點舉辦派對。場地是辦公室隔壁的 Rose Garden Restaurant。\n\n我們邀請所有員工參加。晚餐和飲料都免費。請在 9 月 10 日前回覆人資部門的 Ortiz 小姐，這樣我們才能預訂足夠的桌子。","w":[87,90,96,10,173,86,186,35,234],"qs":[{"q":"Why will the company have a party?","o":["A new manager is coming","Sales were good this year","A new restaurant is opening","It will be 20 years old"],"a":3,"ex":"Sunrise Foods will be 20 years old! To celebrate our anniversary, we will have a party，anniversary 是「周年紀念日」，派對是為了慶祝公司成立 20 年。文中沒有提到新經理、新餐廳開幕或業績。"},{"q":"What is indicated about the party?","o":["Only managers can go","Employees do not need to pay for food","It will be held in the morning","It is far from the office"],"a":1,"ex":"Dinner and beverages are free，晚餐和飲料免費，所以員工不用付餐費。派對在 6 P.M.，是晚上；All employees are invited，所有員工都受邀；餐廳 next to our office，就在辦公室隔壁。"},{"q":"What should employees do by September 10?","o":["Pay for dinner","Buy a ticket","Bring beverages","Reply to Ms. Ortiz"],"a":3,"ex":"Please respond to Ms. Ortiz in the HR department by September 10，respond 是「回覆」，也就是 reply。晚餐和飲料都是免費的，所以不用付錢、買票或自己帶飲料。"}]},
{"id":"r400-18","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Software update on Saturday","tx":"To: All employees\nFrom: IT Department\nSubject: Software update on Saturday\n\nDear all,\n\nWe will install new software on all office computers this Saturday. The work will start at 8 A.M. and take about four hours. During this time, you cannot use your e-mail account or the company network.\n\nBefore you leave on Friday, please save your files and turn off your computer. If you have a problem on Monday, contact the IT help desk.","zh":"收件人：全體員工\n寄件人：資訊部門\n主旨：星期六軟體更新\n\n大家好：\n\n這個星期六，我們會在辦公室所有的電腦上安裝新軟體。作業將從上午 8 點開始，大約需要四個小時。這段時間內，各位無法使用電子郵件帳號或公司網路。\n\n星期五下班前，請儲存您的檔案並把電腦關機。如果星期一有問題，請聯絡資訊服務台。","w":[10,35,46,233,189,30,0,125,172,230,2],"qs":[{"q":"What is the e-mail mainly about?","o":["A change in office hours","A new employee","A software update","A lost computer"],"a":2,"ex":"主旨 Software update on Saturday，內文說 We will install new software on all office computers，主要在通知軟體更新。文中沒有提到新員工、遺失的電腦或上班時間改變。"},{"q":"When will the work most likely finish?","o":["On Monday morning","At 8 A.M. on Saturday","On Friday evening","Around noon on Saturday"],"a":3,"ex":"The work will start at 8 A.M. and take about four hours，星期六上午 8 點開始、大約四個小時，所以大約中午結束。8 A.M. 是開始的時間；Friday 是要先存檔關機的日子；Monday 是有問題時聯絡服務台的日子。"},{"q":"What should employees do before they leave on Friday?","o":["Turn off their computers","Change their e-mail password","Install the software","Call the help desk"],"a":0,"ex":"Before you leave on Friday, please save your files and turn off your computer，星期五下班前要存檔並把電腦關機。安裝軟體是資訊部門的工作；星期一有問題才聯絡 help desk；文中沒有提到改密碼。"}]},
{"id":"r400-19","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"New bus route to the airport","tx":"New Bus Route to the Airport\n\nStarting May 1, a new bus route will run between the city center and the airport. Bus 88 will depart from Central Station every 20 minutes. The trip takes about 40 minutes.\n\nThe fare is $3 for adults and $1 for children. Passengers can pay with cash or a bus card. The city hopes the new route will reduce traffic on the airport road.","zh":"通往機場的新公車路線\n\n從 5 月 1 日起，將有一條新的公車路線往返市中心和機場。88 號公車每 20 分鐘從 Central Station 發車，車程大約 40 分鐘。\n\n票價是成人 3 美元、兒童 1 美元。乘客可以用現金或公車卡付費。市政府希望這條新路線能減少機場道路的車流量。","w":[48,222,39,1,198],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article about?","o":["A new airport","A train station closing","Higher parking fees","A new bus service"],"a":3,"ex":"標題 New Bus Route to the Airport，內文說 a new bus route will run between the city center and the airport，主題是新的公車路線。機場不是新的，Central Station 是發車地點而不是要關閉，文中也沒有提到停車費。"},{"q":"How often will Bus 88 leave Central Station?","o":["Every hour","Every 20 minutes","Every 10 minutes","Every 40 minutes"],"a":1,"ex":"Bus 88 will depart from Central Station every 20 minutes，depart 是「出發」，每 20 分鐘一班。40 minutes 是車程的時間，不是發車的間隔。"},{"q":"What does the city hope the new route will do?","o":["Give drivers more jobs","Lower the amount of traffic","Make bus fares cheaper","Bring more visitors to the city"],"a":1,"ex":"The city hopes the new route will reduce traffic on the airport road，reduce 是「減少」，也就是讓車流量變少。文中沒有提到吸引遊客、降低票價或增加司機的工作。"}]},
{"id":"r400-20","lv":400,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"New parking rules at Riverside Mall","tx":"Riverside Mall — New Parking Rules\n\nThese rules start on August 1.\n\nCustomers with a shopping receipt can park free for two hours. Please show the receipt to the cashier at the exit. After two hours, the fee is $2 per hour.\n\nMotorcycles must use the separate section near Gate B. Vehicles cannot stay in the parking lot overnight. The lot is open from 8 A.M. to 11 P.M.","zh":"Riverside Mall——停車新規定\n\n這些規定從 8 月 1 日開始實施。\n\n持有購物收據的顧客可以免費停車兩小時。請在出口把收據拿給收銀員看。超過兩小時後，費用是每小時 2 美元。\n\n機車必須停在 B 入口附近的獨立區域。車輛不可以在停車場過夜。停車場的開放時間是上午 8 點到晚上 11 點。","w":[15,4,7,249,55,26],"qs":[{"q":"What is the notice about?","o":["New rules for parking","A new store at the mall","A sale at the mall","A job for cashiers"],"a":0,"ex":"標題 New Parking Rules，內容都在說停車的費用和規定。文中沒有提到新商店、特賣活動或徵收銀員。"},{"q":"How can customers park free for two hours?","o":["By paying $2","By parking near Gate B","By arriving before 8 A.M.","By showing a shopping receipt"],"a":3,"ex":"Customers with a shopping receipt can park free for two hours. Please show the receipt to the cashier，把購物收據拿給收銀員看，就能免費停兩小時。$2 是超過兩小時後每小時的費用，Gate B 附近是機車的停車區，8 A.M. 是停車場開門的時間。"},{"q":"What are drivers NOT allowed to do?","o":["Leave a vehicle in the lot all night","Park a motorcycle","Pay the cashier at the exit","Park for more than two hours"],"a":0,"ex":"Vehicles cannot stay in the parking lot overnight，overnight 是「過夜」，車子不可以整晚停在停車場。停超過兩小時只要付費就可以；機車可以停在 separate section；文中也沒有禁止在出口付費。"}]},
{"id":"r400-21","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"email","ti":"Your interview on May 14","tx":"To: Maria Santos\nFrom: Daniel Cho, Human Resources\nSubject: Your interview\n\nDear Ms. Santos,\n\nThank you for applying for the sales job at Brightway Electronics. We would like to [1] ------- you to an interview on Tuesday, May 14, at 10 A.M.\n\nThe interview [2] ------- about 30 minutes. Please bring a copy of your résumé. When you arrive, please give your name to the receptionist in the lobby.\n\n[3] ------- We look forward to meeting you.","zh":"收件人：Maria Santos\n寄件人：Daniel Cho（人力資源部）\n主旨：您的面試\n\nSantos 小姐您好：\n\n感謝您應徵 Brightway Electronics 的業務工作。我們想邀請您在 5 月 14 日星期二上午 10 點來面試。\n\n面試大約需要 30 分鐘。請帶一份履歷。抵達時，請把您的名字告訴大廳的接待人員。\n\n請回覆這封電子郵件確認時間。我們期待與您見面。","w":[197,173,231,32,13,196,2],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["attend","invite","deliver","remind"],"a":1,"ex":"invite someone to an interview 是「邀請某人來面試」。attend 是參加（後面接活動，不接人）、remind 是提醒、deliver 是遞送，放進去意思都不通。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["took","has taken","will take","taking"],"a":2,"ex":"面試在 May 14，是還沒發生的事，所以用未來式 will take（將花費…時間）。took 是過去式、has taken 是現在完成式，時間不對；taking 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能當句子的動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Your first day of work is May 14.","Please reply to this e-mail to confirm the time.","The sales job is no longer open.","We were happy to meet you last week."],"a":1,"ex":"前面已經告訴她面試的日期和時間，所以最後請她回信確認時間（confirm the time），再接 We look forward to meeting you 最自然。面試還沒舉行，不可能上星期已經見過面；May 14 是面試的日子，不是第一天上班；公司正在邀請她面試，職缺不可能已經關閉。"}]},
{"id":"r400-22","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"notice","ti":"Power off on Sunday","tx":"NOTICE: Power Off on Sunday\n\nThe power in the Green Tower office building will be turned off on Sunday, June 9, from 7 A.M. to 1 P.M. Workers need to [1] ------- some old equipment.\n\nDuring this time, the lights, elevators, and air conditioners will not work. [2] -------, please do not come to the office on Sunday morning.\n\nBefore you leave on Friday, turn off your computer and printer. This will [3] ------- damage to your devices.","zh":"公告：星期日停電\n\nGreen Tower 辦公大樓將在 6 月 9 日星期日上午 7 點到下午 1 點停電。工人需要更換一些老舊的設備。\n\n這段時間內，電燈、電梯和冷氣都無法使用。所以，星期日早上請不要到辦公室來。\n\n星期五下班前，請把電腦和印表機關機。這樣可以防止您的裝置受損。","w":[117,212,44,16,215,242,71],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["replace","remain","respond","participate"],"a":0,"ex":"replace old equipment 是「更換老舊的設備」，所以大樓才需要停電。participate 是參加、respond 是回應、remain 是保持，這三個字後面都不能直接接 equipment，意思也不通。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["Or","So","Because","But"],"a":1,"ex":"前一句說電燈、電梯、冷氣都不能用，後一句是結果：請不要來辦公室，所以用表示結果的 So（所以）。But 是但是、Or 是或者，邏輯不對；Because 是因為，後面要接原因的句子，不能加逗號單獨使用。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["prevent","perform","present","propose"],"a":0,"ex":"prevent damage 是「防止損壞」，先把電腦和印表機關機，就能避免裝置受損。perform 是執行、propose 是提議、present 是提出或贈送，和 damage 搭配意思都不通。"}]},
{"id":"r400-23","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"memo","ti":"New employee starts Monday","tx":"MEMO\nTo: All staff\nFrom: Grace Liu, Office Manager\nSubject: New employee\n\nA new employee, Mr. Ryan Scott, will join the sales department on Monday. Before this, he [1] ------- at a bank for five years.\n\nOn his first day, Ms. Tan will give him a [2] ------- of the office and introduce him to everyone. His desk is next to the printer on the second floor.\n\nPlease [3] ------- him if he has any questions.","zh":"備忘錄\n收件人：全體員工\n寄件人：辦公室經理 Grace Liu\n主旨：新進員工\n\n新員工 Ryan Scott 先生將於星期一加入業務部門。在這之前，他在銀行工作了五年。\n\n第一天上班時，Tan 小姐會帶他參觀辦公室，並把他介紹給大家。他的座位在二樓的印表機旁邊。\n\n如果他有任何問題，請大家協助他。","w":[40,10,35,108,214,16,193,2],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["will work","working","worked","works"],"a":2,"ex":"Before this（在這之前）指的是過去的事，所以用過去式 worked。works 是現在式、will work 是未來式，時間不對；working 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能當句子的動詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["tour","fare","sample","loan"],"a":0,"ex":"give someone a tour of the office 是「帶某人參觀辦公室」，新人第一天上班常會這樣安排。fare 是車資、loan 是貸款、sample 是樣品，放進去意思都不通。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["assistant","assisted","assistance","assist"],"a":3,"ex":"Please 後面接原形動詞，assist him 是「協助他」。assistant 是名詞（助理）、assistance 是名詞（協助）、assisted 是過去式或過去分詞。"}]},
{"id":"r400-24","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Happy Road Car Rental","tx":"Happy Road Car Rental\n\nDo you need a car for your next trip? At Happy Road, you can [1] ------- a car for only $40 a day. We have a wide range of vehicles, from small cars to large vans.\n\nEvery car is [2] ------- by our staff before you drive it. You do not need to pay extra for insurance [3] ------- it is included in the price.\n\nBook online today and save 10%!","zh":"Happy Road Car Rental\n\n下一趟旅行需要用車嗎？在 Happy Road，您每天只要 40 美元就可以租到一輛車。我們有各式各樣的車輛，從小型車到大型廂型車都有。\n\n每一輛車在您開走之前，都由我們的員工檢查過。您不需要為保險額外付費，因為保險已經包含在價格裡。\n\n今天就上網預訂，可以省下 10%！","w":[228,127,26,40,78,185,172],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["retire","attend","depart","rent"],"a":3,"ex":"rent a car 是「租車」，後面的 for only $40 a day 是每天的租金，而且這是租車公司（Car Rental）的廣告。depart 是出發、attend 是參加、retire 是退休，和 a car 搭配都不通。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["checks","checking","checked","check"],"a":2,"ex":"be 動詞 + 過去分詞是被動語態，後面有 by our staff（由我們的員工），車子是「被檢查」，所以用過去分詞 checked。checking 是現在分詞、check 是原形動詞、checks 是第三人稱單數，都不能放在 is 和 by 中間表示被動。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["so","or","but","because"],"a":3,"ex":"「保險已經包含在價格裡」是「不需要額外付費」的原因，所以用 because（因為）。but 是但是、or 是或者，意思不對；so 是所以，放在這裡因果順序會顛倒。"}]},
{"id":"r400-25","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"letter","ti":"About your coffee maker","tx":"Dear Ms. Howard,\n\nThank you for your letter of March 3. We are sorry that the coffee maker you bought at our store [1] ------- working after only one week. We would like to [2] ------- for this problem.\n\nYou have two options. We can send you a new coffee maker, [3] ------- we can give you a full refund. Please call us at 555-0199 and tell us your decision.\n\nSincerely,\nTom Berg\nCustomer Service, Kitchen Corner","zh":"Howard 小姐您好：\n\n感謝您 3 月 3 日的來信。很抱歉，您在本店購買的咖啡機才用了一個星期就故障了。我們想為這個問題向您道歉。\n\n您有兩個選擇。我們可以寄一台新的咖啡機給您，或是全額退款給您。請撥打 555-0199，告訴我們您的決定。\n\n敬上\nTom Berg\nKitchen Corner 客戶服務部","w":[180,14,119,53],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["stopped","stops","will stop","stopping"],"a":0,"ex":"咖啡機故障是已經發生的事（Ms. Howard 在 3 月 3 日的信裡提到的），前面的 bought 也是過去式，所以用過去式 stopped，stopped working 是「停止運作」。stops 是現在式、will stop 是未來式，時間不對；stopping 不能單獨當動詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["apply","apologize","subscribe","participate"],"a":1,"ex":"apologize for 是「為…道歉」，前一句說 We are sorry，這裡是為咖啡機的問題道歉。apply for 是申請、participate 是參加、subscribe 是訂閱，放進去意思都不通。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["or","until","because","so"],"a":0,"ex":"前面說 You have two options（您有兩個選擇），「寄新的咖啡機」和「全額退款」是二選一，所以用 or（或者）。so 是所以、because 是因為、until 是直到，都不能表示選擇。"}]},
{"id":"r400-26","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"announcement","ti":"Holiday hours at Green Basket Market","tx":"Holiday Hours at Green Basket Market\n\nDear customers,\n\nGreen Basket Market will be closed on Thursday, January 1, for the New Year holiday. We will open again on Friday at our [1] ------- time, 8 A.M.\n\nOn Wednesday, December 31, the store will close early at 6 P.M. [2] -------\n\nThis week, all beverages are sold at a 20% discount. Thank you for your [3] ------- this year. We wish you a happy New Year!","zh":"Green Basket Market 假期營業時間\n\n各位顧客您好：\n\nGreen Basket Market 將於 1 月 1 日星期四元旦假期休息一天。我們會在星期五照平常的時間上午 8 點恢復營業。\n\n12 月 31 日星期三，本店將提早在下午 6 點打烊。請在那之前完成購物。\n\n本週所有飲料一律八折。感謝您這一年來的支持。祝您新年快樂！","w":[137,86,111,235],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["annual","frequent","entire","regular"],"a":3,"ex":"our regular time 是「我們平常的（開門）時間」，後面的 8 A.M. 就是平常開門的時間。annual 是一年一次的、entire 是整個的、frequent 是頻繁的，都不能用來形容開門的時間。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["We will stay open until midnight that day.","Please finish your shopping before then.","The meeting will be in Room 2.","Thank you for returning the item."],"a":1,"ex":"前一句說 12 月 31 日會提早在下午 6 點打烊，所以接著提醒顧客 before then（在那之前）把東西買完。「營業到午夜」和提早打烊互相矛盾；文中沒有提到退回商品，也沒有提到任何會議。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["damage","pollution","support","complaint"],"a":2,"ex":"Thank you for your support 是「感謝您的支持」，是商店在年底感謝顧客的常見說法。complaint 是客訴、damage 是損害、pollution 是污染，不會拿來感謝顧客。"}]},
{"id":"r400-27","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"message","ti":"Price list for Mr. Baker","tx":"Hi Jenny,\n\nI am sorry to [1] ------- you on your day off. I looked in every folder on my computer, but I cannot find the price list for our client, Mr. Baker. He [2] ------- it by 3 P.M. today.\n\nCould you tell me where the file is? [3] ------- you have a copy, please attach it to an e-mail and send it to me. Then I can give it to Mr. Baker immediately.\n\nThank you!\nCarla","zh":"嗨，Jenny：\n\n很抱歉在妳休假的時候打擾妳。我找遍了電腦裡的每一個資料夾，還是找不到要給客戶 Baker 先生的價目表。他今天下午 3 點以前就需要這份資料。\n\n可以告訴我檔案放在哪裡嗎？如果妳有備份，請把它附在電子郵件裡寄給我。這樣我就可以立刻交給 Baker 先生。\n\n謝謝！\nCarla","w":[223,38,219,170],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["disturb","develop","deliver","display"],"a":0,"ex":"sorry to disturb you 是「抱歉打擾你」，在對方休假（day off）時聯絡常這樣說。deliver 是遞送、develop 是開發、display 是展示，後面接 you 意思都不通。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["need","needs","to need","needing"],"a":1,"ex":"主詞 He 是第三人稱單數，現在式動詞要加 s，所以用 needs。need 沒有加 s；needing 和 to need 都不能單獨當句子的動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["But","So","Or","If"],"a":3,"ex":"Carla 不確定 Jenny 有沒有備份，所以用 If（如果）：「如果妳有備份，請寄給我」。So 是所以、But 是但是、Or 是或者，都不能用來表示「條件」。"}]},
{"id":"r400-28","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"article","ti":"Survey: workers like short meetings","tx":"Survey: Workers Like Short Meetings\n\nA new survey asked 500 office workers about meetings. The [1] ------- show that most workers do not like long meetings. Nearly 70% said that a meeting should be 30 minutes or less.\n\nMany workers also said that they [2] ------- too many meetings each week. Experts recommend that managers send the topics to staff before each meeting. This can [3] ------- the time that workers spend in meetings.","zh":"調查：上班族喜歡簡短的會議\n\n一項新的調查詢問了 500 位上班族對會議的看法。結果顯示，大多數上班族不喜歡冗長的會議。將近 70% 的人說，一場會議應該在 30 分鐘以內。\n\n許多上班族也說，他們每星期參加太多會議。專家建議主管在每次開會前，先把討論的主題寄給員工。這樣可以減少員工花在會議上的時間。","w":[126,105,171,175,88,208,40,198],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["results","fares","wages","goods"],"a":0,"ex":"The results show that... 是「（調查）結果顯示…」，survey 和 result 常一起出現。fares 是車資、goods 是商品、wages 是工資，都不能「顯示」調查的內容。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["to attend","attends","attending","attend"],"a":3,"ex":"主詞 they 是複數，現在式用原形動詞 attend，attend meetings 是「參加會議」。attends 要搭配第三人稱單數的主詞；attending 和 to attend 都不能單獨當子句的動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["remind","reduce","respond","retire"],"a":1,"ex":"reduce the time 是「減少時間」，先把主題寄給員工，開會就能更快結束。remind 是提醒、respond 是回應、retire 是退休，和 the time 搭配都不通。"}]},
{"id":"r400-29","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"email","ti":"Welcome to Bayside Business Weekly","tx":"To: Paul Green\nFrom: Bayside Business Weekly\nSubject: Welcome!\n\nDear Mr. Green,\n\nThank you for [1] ------- to Bayside Business Weekly. You can now read all of our articles online. The week's top news [2] ------- to your e-mail address every Monday morning.\n\nYour first month is free. After that, the [3] ------- is $5 per month. You can cancel at any time. If you have any questions, please contact us.","zh":"收件人：Paul Green\n寄件人：Bayside Business Weekly\n主旨：歡迎！\n\nGreen 先生您好：\n\n感謝您訂閱 Bayside Business Weekly。您現在可以在網路上閱讀我們所有的文章。每星期一早上，當週的重點新聞會寄到您的電子郵件信箱。\n\n第一個月免費。之後的費用是每個月 5 美元。您隨時可以取消。如果有任何問題，請與我們聯絡。","w":[211,64,7,176,230,2],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["subscribing","subscribe","subscribed","subscribes"],"a":0,"ex":"介系詞 for 後面要接動名詞（V-ing），Thank you for subscribing to... 是「感謝您訂閱…」。subscribe 是原形動詞、subscribed 是過去式或過去分詞、subscribes 是第三人稱單數，都不能放在 for 後面。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["is sent","sent","is sending","sends"],"a":0,"ex":"新聞是「被寄到」信箱，要用被動語態（be 動詞 + 過去分詞）；every Monday morning 是固定發生的事，用現在式，所以是 is sent。sends 和 is sending 是主動語態，新聞不會自己寄東西；只寫 sent 少了 be 動詞，不是被動語態。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["fare","loan","fee","wage"],"a":2,"ex":"fee 是「（服務的）費用」，訂閱每個月要付的錢用 fee。fare 是車資、wage 是工資、loan 是貸款，都不是訂閱要付的錢。"}]},
{"id":"r400-30","lv":400,"p":6,"k":"review","ti":"Lunch at Corner Table Café","tx":"Corner Table Café — Review by Tina R.\n\nI had lunch at Corner Table Café with two colleagues last Friday. We did not have a [1] -------, but we got a table in five minutes.\n\nThe menu is small, but there is a good selection of beverages. Our food [2] ------- only ten minutes after we ordered. The prices are a little high. [3] -------, I will go back again because the service was so good.","zh":"Corner Table Café——Tina R. 的評論\n\n上星期五我和兩位同事在 Corner Table Café 吃午餐。我們沒有訂位，但是五分鐘就有位子了。\n\n菜單上的選擇不多，不過飲料的種類很豐富。我們點餐後才十分鐘，餐點就送來了。價格有一點高。不過，因為服務非常好，我還會再去。","w":[90,9,57,86],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["reservation","description","departure","destination"],"a":0,"ex":"have a reservation 是「有訂位」，沒有訂位卻五分鐘就有桌子，前後用 but 連接很合理。destination 是目的地、description 是描述、departure 是出發，都和餐廳的座位無關。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["arrived","will arrive","arriving","arrives"],"a":0,"ex":"這是上星期五（last Friday）發生的事，後面的 after we ordered 也是過去式，所以用過去式 arrived。arrives 是現在式、will arrive 是未來式，時間不對；arriving 不能單獨當動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["For example","Therefore","However","Because"],"a":2,"ex":"前一句說價格有點高（缺點），後一句卻說還會再去，前後意思相反，所以用 However（然而）。Therefore 是因此、For example 是例如，邏輯不對；Because 是連接詞，後面不能加逗號單獨使用。"}]},
{"id":"r600-01","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Your shipment is delayed","tx":"To: Kevin Wu\nFrom: Customer Service, Maple Home Store\nSubject: Your shipment is delayed\n\nDear Mr. Wu,\n\nThank you for your recent purchase. We are sorry to tell you that your shipment has been delayed. The desk lamp you ordered is in stock, but heavy snow has stopped our courier from leaving the warehouse. We now expect your order to arrive on Friday, March 14, instead of Tuesday.\n\nYou can track your package on our website at any time. Because of this delay, we will not charge you for shipping. The $8 fee will be returned to your credit card within approximately five days.\n\nIf you have any questions, please do not hesitate to contact us.\n\nSincerely,\nNina Ross","zh":"收件人：Kevin Wu\n寄件人：Maple Home Store 客服部\n主旨：您的貨件延遲了\n\n吳先生您好：\n\n感謝您最近的購買。很抱歉通知您，您的貨件延遲了。您訂購的檯燈有現貨，但大雪讓我們的快遞員無法離開倉庫。我們現在預計您的訂單會在 3 月 14 日星期五送達，而不是星期二。\n\n您可以隨時在我們的網站上追蹤包裹。由於這次延遲，我們不會向您收取運費。8 美元的費用將在大約五天內退回您的信用卡。\n\n如果您有任何問題，請不要猶豫，隨時與我們聯絡。\n\nNina Ross 敬上","w":[492,316,345,341,485,486,366,420,430],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the e-mail?","o":["To advertise a new desk lamp","To say that an item is out of stock","To explain that an order will arrive late","To ask a customer to pay a fee"],"a":2,"ex":"信中說 your shipment has been delayed，並告知新的到貨日期，所以目的是通知訂單會晚到。文中說檯燈 is in stock（有現貨），運費是要退還而不是加收，也沒有推銷新產品。"},{"q":"Why has the order been delayed?","o":["The customer's address was wrong","Bad weather stopped the courier","The payment was not received","The lamp is not in stock"],"a":1,"ex":"文中說 heavy snow has stopped our courier from leaving the warehouse，大雪讓快遞員無法出發，所以是天氣不好造成的。檯燈有現貨，文中也沒有提到地址或付款有問題。"},{"q":"The word \"track\" in the passage is closest in meaning to","o":["follow","weigh","wrap","cancel"],"a":0,"ex":"track your package 是「追蹤包裹」，也就是持續查看包裹送到哪裡了，意思最接近 follow（跟著、追蹤）。cancel 是取消、weigh 是秤重、wrap 是包裝。"}]},
{"id":"r600-02","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Interview for sales assistant position","tx":"To: Grace Liu\nFrom: Daniel Ortiz, Human Resources\nSubject: Interview for sales assistant position\n\nDear Ms. Liu,\n\nThank you for your application for the sales assistant position at Bright Office Supplies. We were pleased with your résumé and would like to invite you to an interview on Thursday, May 8, at 10:00 A.M. The interview will be held at our main office and will take approximately 40 minutes.\n\nPlease bring photo identification and a copy of your computer skills certificate. You will meet Ms. Park, the supervisor of the sales team.\n\nIf this time is not possible for you, please reply by Monday so that we can reschedule.\n\nBest regards,\nDaniel Ortiz","zh":"收件人：Grace Liu\n寄件人：人力資源部 Daniel Ortiz\n主旨：業務助理職位面試\n\n劉小姐您好：\n\n感謝您應徵 Bright Office Supplies 的業務助理職位。我們對您的履歷很滿意，想邀請您在 5 月 8 日星期四上午 10 點來面試。面試將在我們的總公司進行，大約需要 40 分鐘。\n\n請攜帶附照片的身分證明文件，以及您的電腦技能證書影本。您將會見到業務團隊的主管 Park 小姐。\n\n如果這個時間您不方便，請在星期一之前回覆，以便我們改期。\n\nDaniel Ortiz 敬上","w":[276,338,291,420,269,256,319,424],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Mr. Ortiz write to Ms. Liu?","o":["To invite her to a job interview","To tell her she got the job","To cancel an appointment","To ask her to send a résumé"],"a":0,"ex":"信中說 would like to invite you to an interview，是邀請她來面試。她還沒有被錄取；履歷已經收到了（We were pleased with your résumé）；文中也沒有取消任何約定。"},{"q":"What is Ms. Liu asked to bring?","o":["A letter from her supervisor","Her university transcript","A printed résumé","Photo identification"],"a":3,"ex":"文中說 Please bring photo identification and a copy of your computer skills certificate，要帶附照片的身分證明和證書影本。履歷、成績單和主管的信都沒有被要求。"},{"q":"The word \"position\" in the passage is closest in meaning to","o":["order","opinion","place","job"],"a":3,"ex":"the sales assistant position 是「業務助理這個職位」，position 在這裡指工作、職位，最接近 job。place 是地點、opinion 是意見、order 是訂單或順序，都不是這裡的意思。"}]},
{"id":"r600-03","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"email","ti":"Conference registration confirmed","tx":"To: Peter Yang\nFrom: Events Team, National Marketing Conference\nSubject: Registration confirmed\n\nDear Mr. Yang,\n\nThank you for registering for the National Marketing Conference on September 19. We have received your payment of $120.\n\nThe conference will be held at the Lakeside Convention Center. Each [1] ------- lasts one hour, and the full schedule [2] ------- to this e-mail. Please arrive by 8:30 A.M. to pick up your name badge at the reception desk.\n\nLunch is included in the fee. [3] -------, parking is not, so we suggest using public transportation.\n\nWe look forward to seeing you.\n\nEvents Team","zh":"收件人：Peter Yang\n寄件人：National Marketing Conference 活動小組\n主旨：報名已確認\n\n楊先生您好：\n\n感謝您報名 9 月 19 日的 National Marketing Conference。我們已收到您 120 美元的款項。\n\n研討會將在 Lakeside Convention Center 舉行。每一場活動進行一小時，完整的時程表已附在這封電子郵件中。請在上午 8 點 30 分前抵達，到接待櫃台領取您的名牌。\n\n費用包含午餐。不過，停車費不包含在內，所以我們建議您搭乘大眾運輸工具。\n\n期待與您見面。\n\n活動小組","w":[262,278,494,320,325,451,279],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["shipment","division","pension","session"],"a":3,"ex":"Each session lasts one hour 是「每一場活動進行一小時」，研討會裡一場一場的活動就叫 session，後面也提到 schedule（時程表）。shipment 是貨件、pension 是退休金、division 是部門，都不會「進行一小時」。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["attaching","is attached","attaches","has attached"],"a":1,"ex":"主詞 the full schedule（完整時程表）是「被附上」的東西，要用被動語態 is attached to this e-mail。attaches 和 has attached 是主動，變成時程表自己去附加別的東西；attaching 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能當句子的動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Therefore","For example","In addition","However"],"a":3,"ex":"前一句說午餐包含在費用內，這一句說停車不包含，前後意思相反，要用表示轉折的 However（然而）。Therefore 是因此、For example 是例如、In addition 是此外，都接不上相反的內容。"}]},
{"id":"r600-04","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"Elevator maintenance in the east wing","tx":"NOTICE TO ALL TENANTS\n\nThe elevator in the east wing of Lakeview Tower will be closed for maintenance on Wednesday, June 4, from 9:00 A.M. to 3:00 P.M. Technicians will replace several old parts so that the elevator continues to operate safely.\n\nDuring this time, please use the elevator in the west wing or the stairs adjacent to the lobby. Tenants who need help carrying heavy items may call the front desk at extension 105.\n\nWe apologize for the trouble and thank you for your patience. The work will be finished in one day, and no additional closures are planned this month.\n\nBuilding Management Office","zh":"致全體承租戶的公告\n\nLakeview Tower 東側的電梯將於 6 月 4 日星期三上午 9 點至下午 3 點關閉，進行維護保養。技術人員會更換幾個老舊零件，讓電梯能繼續安全運作。\n\n在這段時間，請使用西側的電梯，或大廳旁邊的樓梯。需要協助搬運重物的承租戶，可以撥分機 105 聯絡櫃台。\n\n造成不便，我們深感抱歉，也感謝您的耐心配合。工程將在一天內完成，本月沒有安排其他的關閉時間。\n\n大樓管理室","w":[339,292,333,443,389,283,405],"qs":[{"q":"What is the notice mainly about?","o":["The opening of a new lobby","A change in front desk hours","A temporary elevator closure","A new parking rule"],"a":2,"ex":"公告說 The elevator in the east wing ... will be closed for maintenance，而且只有 6 月 4 日一天，所以是電梯暫時關閉。文中沒有提到停車規定、櫃台時間或新大廳。"},{"q":"What should tenants do if they need help with heavy items?","o":["Visit the management office","Call the front desk","Wait for a technician","Use the east wing elevator"],"a":1,"ex":"文中說 Tenants who need help carrying heavy items may call the front desk at extension 105，要撥分機 105 給櫃台。東側電梯當天關閉不能用，文中也沒有說要等技術人員或去管理室。"},{"q":"What is suggested about Lakeview Tower?","o":["It is closed on Wednesdays","It has more than one elevator","It was built this year","It has no stairs"],"a":1,"ex":"文中提到 the elevator in the east wing 和 the elevator in the west wing，東側、西側各有電梯，可見這棟大樓不只一部電梯。文中有提到 stairs（樓梯），電梯已經有 old parts（老舊零件），也沒有說星期三不開放。"}]},
{"id":"r600-05","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"Customer database update this Saturday","tx":"IT Department Notice: Customer Database Update\n\nThe customer database will not be available this Saturday, October 18, from 8:00 P.M. to midnight. During these hours, our technicians will install new hardware and add a search function that many employees have requested.\n\nPlease save your work and log out before 8:00 P.M. Any data entered after that time may be lost. Access will return on Sunday morning, and you will not need a new password.\n\nIf the database does not function correctly on Monday, do not attempt to fix the problem yourself. Call the help desk at extension 220, and a technician will assist you.","zh":"資訊部公告：客戶資料庫更新\n\n客戶資料庫將於本週六 10 月 18 日晚上 8 點至午夜暫停使用。在這段時間，我們的技術人員會安裝新的硬體設備，並加入許多員工要求的搜尋功能。\n\n請在晚上 8 點前儲存您的工作並登出。在那之後輸入的資料可能會遺失。星期日早上就可以恢復使用，您不需要新的密碼。\n\n如果星期一資料庫無法正常運作，請不要試著自己修理。請撥分機 220 聯絡服務台，會有技術人員協助您。","w":[302,333,323,491,371,487,283],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the notice?","o":["To ask employees to change their passwords","To report that customer data was lost","To introduce a new technician","To tell staff when a system will be unavailable"],"a":3,"ex":"公告一開始就說 The customer database will not be available this Saturday ... from 8:00 P.M. to midnight，目的是通知系統暫停使用的時間。文中說 you will not need a new password，不用換密碼；也沒有介紹新的技術人員或說資料已經遺失。"},{"q":"What should employees do before 8:00 P.M. on Saturday?","o":["Create a new password","Save their work and log out","Call the help desk","Install new hardware"],"a":1,"ex":"文中說 Please save your work and log out before 8:00 P.M.。不需要新密碼；打電話給服務台是星期一資料庫有問題時才要做的事；安裝硬體是技術人員的工作。"},{"q":"The word \"attempt\" in the passage is closest in meaning to","o":["forget","refuse","try","agree"],"a":2,"ex":"do not attempt to fix the problem yourself 是「不要試著自己解決問題」，attempt 是嘗試，最接近 try。forget 是忘記、refuse 是拒絕、agree 是同意。"}]},
{"id":"r600-06","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"email","ti":"Replacement for your coffee maker","tx":"To: Olivia Grant\nFrom: Tom Reed, Customer Service\nSubject: Your coffee maker\n\nDear Ms. Grant,\n\nThank you for contacting us about the coffee maker that you [1] ------- from our online store last month. We are sorry to hear that it has stopped working.\n\nAll of our appliances come with a one-year [2] -------, so we will be happy to replace yours at no charge. Please put the machine back in its original box. A courier will pick it up from your home on a day that you choose.\n\n[3] ------- we receive the machine, a new one will be shipped to you within three business days.\n\nSincerely,\nTom Reed","zh":"收件人：Olivia Grant\n寄件人：客服部 Tom Reed\n主旨：您的咖啡機\n\nGrant 小姐您好：\n\n感謝您來信告知上個月在我們網路商店購買的咖啡機的狀況。很遺憾聽到它已經不能運作了。\n\n我們所有的家電都附有一年保固，所以我們很樂意免費為您更換。請把機器放回原本的箱子裡。快遞員會在您選擇的日期到府收件。\n\n我們收到機器之後，會在三個工作天內把新的咖啡機寄給您。\n\nTom Reed 敬上","w":[492,252,493,486,341],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["purchased","purchase","purchasing","will purchase"],"a":0,"ex":"句尾有 last month（上個月），是過去的時間，動詞要用過去式 purchased。purchase 是現在式、will purchase 是未來式，時間不對；purchasing 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能單獨當動詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["deadline","agenda","guarantee","proposal"],"a":2,"ex":"come with a one-year guarantee 是「附有一年保固」，後面說 replace yours at no charge（免費更換）正是保固的內容。deadline 是截止日、proposal 是提案、agenda 是議程。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["After","Unless","Although","During"],"a":0,"ex":"意思是「我們收到機器之後，就會寄出新的」，要用表示時間先後的 After。Although 是雖然、Unless 是除非，邏輯不通；During 是介系詞，後面要接名詞，不能接 we receive the machine 這樣的句子。"}]},
{"id":"r600-07","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"memo","ti":"New travel expense policy","tx":"MEMO\n\nTo: All sales staff\nFrom: Helen Brooks, Accounting\nDate: August 25\nSubject: New travel expense policy\n\nA new policy for travel expenses will be effective on September 1. All expense reports must be submitted within ten days after your trip ends. Reports sent after this deadline will not be paid until the following month.\n\nPlease attach receipts for every expense over $20. Your supervisor must approve the report before it goes to Accounting. Meals with clients are still covered, but hotel rates may not exceed $150 per night.\n\nA summary of the policy is on the company website. If you have a specific question, call me at extension 314.","zh":"備忘錄\n\n收件人：全體業務人員\n寄件人：會計部 Helen Brooks\n日期：8 月 25 日\n主旨：新的差旅費用政策\n\n新的差旅費用政策將於 9 月 1 日生效。所有費用報告必須在出差結束後十天內提交。超過這個截止日才送出的報告，要到下個月才會付款。\n\n每一筆超過 20 美元的費用都請附上收據。報告送到會計部之前，必須先由您的主管批准。與客戶用餐的費用仍然可以報帳，但飯店費用每晚不得超過 150 美元。\n\n政策摘要已放在公司網站上。如果您有具體的問題，請撥分機 314 與我聯絡。","w":[329,286,288,384,455,260,319,450,368,474,259,379,283],"qs":[{"q":"What is the memo mainly about?","o":["Training for the accounting team","A change in sales targets","A list of hotels for business trips","New rules for reporting travel costs"],"a":3,"ex":"主旨是 New travel expense policy，內容說明費用報告的提交期限、收據和批准規定，所以是在講申報差旅費用的新規定。文中沒有提到業績目標、飯店名單或會計部的訓練。"},{"q":"What will happen if a report is sent in late?","o":["It must be approved by Ms. Brooks","It will be paid the following month","It will not be paid at all","The employee must pay a $20 fee"],"a":1,"ex":"文中說 Reports sent after this deadline will not be paid until the following month，晚交的報告要到下個月才付款，不是完全不付。批准報告的是 supervisor（主管）；20 美元是需要附收據的金額，不是罰款。"},{"q":"What is suggested about meals with clients?","o":["The company paid for them under the old policy","They will not be paid for anymore","They no longer need receipts","They are limited to $20 each"],"a":0,"ex":"文中說 Meals with clients are still covered，still（仍然）表示以前就可以報帳，新政策也一樣。20 美元是要附收據的門檻，不是餐費上限；文中也沒有說不用收據或不再給付。"}]},
{"id":"r600-08","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"memo","ti":"Move to the third floor","tx":"MEMO\n\nTo: Marketing Division\nFrom: Paul Chen, Office Administration\nSubject: Move to the third floor\n\nNext Friday, June 13, the marketing division will move to the third floor. The new area is more spacious and has two meeting rooms. Each employee has been assigned a desk, and the new layout is attached to this memo.\n\nPlease pack your personal items in the boxes provided by Thursday at 5:00 P.M. A moving company will carry the boxes and computers, so you do not need to move anything yourself.\n\nIf your assigned desk is not appropriate for your work, please tell me by Wednesday so that I can revise the layout.","zh":"備忘錄\n\n收件人：行銷部\n寄件人：辦公室行政組 Paul Chen\n主旨：搬到三樓\n\n下週五 6 月 13 日，行銷部將搬到三樓。新的區域比較寬敞，還有兩間會議室。每位員工都已經分配好座位，新的座位配置圖附在這份備忘錄後面。\n\n請在星期四下午 5 點前，把您的個人物品裝進公司提供的箱子裡。搬家公司會負責搬運箱子和電腦，所以您不需要自己搬任何東西。\n\n如果分配給您的座位不適合您的工作，請在星期三之前告訴我，讓我可以修改配置圖。","w":[287,318,397,449,336,334,407,463],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main purpose of the memo?","o":["To announce a new division manager","To explain plans for an office move","To ask staff to order new computers","To invite employees to a meeting"],"a":1,"ex":"備忘錄說 the marketing division will move to the third floor，接著說明座位分配和打包方式，所以目的是說明辦公室搬遷的安排。文中沒有提到新主管、訂購電腦或開會。"},{"q":"What must employees do by Thursday at 5:00 P.M.?","o":["Call the moving company","Choose a new desk","Pack their personal items","Carry their computers upstairs"],"a":2,"ex":"文中說 Please pack your personal items in the boxes provided by Thursday at 5:00 P.M.。電腦由搬家公司搬；座位已經分配好（has been assigned a desk），不用自己選；也不需要打電話給搬家公司。"},{"q":"What is NOT mentioned about the new area?","o":["It has more space","It has two meeting rooms","It has a kitchen","It is on the third floor"],"a":2,"ex":"文中有 move to the third floor（在三樓）、more spacious（比較寬敞）、has two meeting rooms（有兩間會議室），只有廚房沒有提到。"}]},
{"id":"r600-09","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"notice","ti":"Parking Lot B closed for construction","tx":"NOTICE: Parking Lot B Closed\n\nBecause of construction work, Parking Lot B will be closed from Monday, April 7, to Friday, April 18. During this period, workers [1] ------- new lights and security cameras.\n\nEmployees who usually park in Lot B may use Lot D, which is [2] ------- to the main gate. A parking pass is not required there during these two weeks. Please note that Lot D is smaller, so spaces may fill up early. [3] -------\n\nWe thank you for your patience. If you have any concerns, please contact the facilities office at extension 410.","zh":"公告：B 停車場關閉\n\n由於施工，B 停車場將於 4 月 7 日星期一至 4 月 18 日星期五關閉。在這段期間，工人將安裝新的照明燈和監視器。\n\n平常停在 B 停車場的員工可以使用 D 停車場，它就在大門旁邊。這兩週在那裡停車不需要停車證。請注意，D 停車場比較小，車位可能很早就停滿。因此，我們建議您在上午 8 點 30 分前抵達。\n\n感謝您的耐心配合。如果您有任何疑慮，請撥分機 410 聯絡總務處。","w":[251,389,451,490,283],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["will install","have installed","installed","installing"],"a":0,"ex":"前一句說停車場 will be closed，是未來的事，During this period 指的也是未來那段時間，所以要用未來式 will install。installed 是過去式、have installed 是現在完成式，時間不對；installing 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能當動詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["flexible","adjacent","essential","relevant"],"a":1,"ex":"be adjacent to 是「緊鄰、在…旁邊」，D 停車場就在大門旁邊。relevant 是相關的、essential 是必要的、flexible 是有彈性的，都不能用來說明停車場的位置。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["The new lights were installed last year.","Lot B will open again on April 7.","We therefore suggest arriving before 8:30 A.M.","Please show your receipt to the cashier."],"a":2,"ex":"前一句說 D 停車場比較小、車位可能很早就停滿，接著建議「因此請在上午 8 點 30 分前抵達」最合理。新的燈是這次施工才要裝的，不是去年；4 月 7 日是 B 停車場開始關閉的日子，不是重新開放；文中沒有提到收據或收銀員。"}]},
{"id":"r600-10","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Kitchen Corner summer appliance sale","tx":"Kitchen Corner Summer Appliance Sale\n\nFrom July 1 to July 15, save up to 30 percent on kitchen appliances at all Kitchen Corner outlets. Choose from a wide range of affordable ovens, coffee makers, and rice cookers.\n\nEvery purchase over $200 comes with complimentary delivery inside the city. All appliances have a two-year guarantee, and our technicians will install large items at no additional charge.\n\nNot sure which model is right for you? Our staff will be happy to demonstrate any product in the store. Visit us soon, because stock is limited!\n\nAll outlets are open daily from 10:00 A.M. to 9:00 P.M.","zh":"Kitchen Corner 夏季家電特賣\n\n7 月 1 日至 7 月 15 日，Kitchen Corner 所有門市的廚房家電最高可省 30%。多款價格實惠的烤箱、咖啡機和電鍋任您挑選。\n\n每筆消費超過 200 美元，即可享有市區內免費配送。所有家電都有兩年保固，大型商品由我們的技術人員安裝，不另外收費。\n\n不確定哪一款適合您嗎？我們的店員很樂意在店內為您示範任何產品。存貨有限，請盡快來店選購！\n\n所有門市每天上午 10 點至晚上 9 點營業。","w":[252,300,381,492,393,493,333,405,486,466,345],"qs":[{"q":"What is being advertised?","o":["A sale on kitchen appliances","A repair service for ovens","A cooking class","A new restaurant"],"a":0,"ex":"標題是 Summer Appliance Sale，內文說 save up to 30 percent on kitchen appliances，是廚房家電的特賣活動。文中沒有提到烹飪課、餐廳或維修服務。"},{"q":"How can customers get free delivery?","o":["By ordering online","By buying two appliances","By spending more than $200","By shopping on July 1"],"a":2,"ex":"文中說 Every purchase over $200 comes with complimentary delivery，complimentary 是免費的，所以消費超過 200 美元就能免費配送。文中沒有說要在 7 月 1 日購買、買兩件或在網路上訂購。"},{"q":"What is NOT offered by Kitchen Corner?","o":["Product demonstrations in the store","A monthly payment plan","A two-year guarantee","Installation of large items"],"a":1,"ex":"文中有 a two-year guarantee（兩年保固）、technicians will install large items（安裝大型商品）、staff will be happy to demonstrate any product in the store（在店內示範產品），只有每月分期付款沒有提到。"}]},
{"id":"r600-11","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Now hiring: store assistants at Sunny Mart","tx":"Now Hiring: Store Assistants at Sunny Mart\n\nSunny Mart, a growing retail company, is looking for store assistants for its new outlet on Pine Street. The position involves helping customers, putting merchandise on the shelves, and using the cash register.\n\nInexperienced candidates are welcome because we provide one week of paid training. Work hours are flexible, with morning, evening, and weekend shifts available. Employees also receive a 15 percent discount on all purchases.\n\nTo apply, please submit your résumé on our website. The deadline is April 30, and interviews will begin the following week.","zh":"徵才：Sunny Mart 門市助理\n\nSunny Mart 是一家成長中的零售公司，正在為位於 Pine Street 的新門市招募門市助理。這份工作的內容包括協助顧客、把商品上架，以及操作收銀機。\n\n歡迎沒有經驗的求職者，因為我們會提供一週的有薪訓練。工作時間有彈性，有早班、晚班和週末班可以選擇。員工購買任何商品還可享有 85 折優惠。\n\n如要應徵，請在我們的網站上提交履歷。截止日是 4 月 30 日，面試將在隔週開始。","w":[364,300,338,429,331,494,388,315,382,369,492,455,291,260],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the advertisement?","o":["To find new workers for a store","To advertise a training school","To announce a store sale","To introduce a new product"],"a":0,"ex":"標題是 Now Hiring（徵才），內文說 is looking for store assistants for its new outlet，是在為新門市找員工。文中沒有提到特賣、訓練學校或新產品。"},{"q":"What do Sunny Mart employees receive?","o":["Free meals during shifts","Two weeks of paid training","A free uniform","A discount on things they buy"],"a":3,"ex":"文中說 Employees also receive a 15 percent discount on all purchases，員工買東西有折扣。訓練是 one week（一週）不是兩週，文中也沒有提到免費餐點或制服。"},{"q":"What is suggested about the position?","o":["It requires working every weekend","It lasts for only one week","It is at the company's head office","Past work experience is not necessary"],"a":3,"ex":"文中說 Inexperienced candidates are welcome，歡迎沒有經驗的人，所以不需要工作經驗。班別是 flexible（有彈性），不是每個週末都要上班；一週指的是訓練時間；工作地點是 Pine Street 的新門市，不是總公司。"}]},
{"id":"r600-12","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"memo","ti":"Training for new software","tx":"MEMO\n\nTo: All employees\nFrom: Sandra Lopez, Human Resources\nSubject: Training for new software\n\nNext month, the company will begin using new software to manage work hours and pay. To help everyone learn the system, an [1] ------- from the software company will teach two training sessions: one on Tuesday, May 6, and one on Thursday, May 8.\n\nEach session will last [2] ------- two hours and will be held in Meeting Room 3. You only need to attend one of them. Please [3] ------- on the company website by April 30 so that we can prepare enough seats.\n\nIf neither date is possible for you, please speak to your supervisor.","zh":"備忘錄\n\n收件人：全體員工\n寄件人：人力資源部 Sandra Lopez\n主旨：新軟體訓練\n\n下個月起，公司將開始使用新軟體來管理工時和薪資。為了幫助大家學會這套系統，軟體公司的一位講師會來上兩場訓練課程：一場在 5 月 6 日星期二，另一場在 5 月 8 日星期四。\n\n每場課程大約兩小時，地點在第 3 會議室。您只需要參加其中一場。請在 4 月 30 日前到公司網站報名，好讓我們準備足夠的座位。\n\n如果這兩個日期您都無法參加，請告訴您的主管。","w":[267,320,420,494,319],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["instructive","instructor","instruction","instruct"],"a":1,"ex":"冠詞 an 後面要接名詞，而且這個人要 teach two training sessions（教兩場訓練課程），所以要用表示「人」的名詞 instructor（講師）。instruction 是名詞「指示」，不是人；instruct 是動詞；instructive 是形容詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["approximately","particularly","immediately","frequently"],"a":0,"ex":"approximately two hours 是「大約兩小時」，數字前面用 approximately 表示大約。particularly 是尤其、immediately 是立刻、frequently 是經常，都不能放在數字前面表示大概的時間長度。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["hesitate","register","commute","operate"],"a":1,"ex":"register on the company website 是「在公司網站上報名」，後面說 so that we can prepare enough seats（好讓我們準備足夠的座位），所以是請大家先報名。commute 是通勤、operate 是操作或運作、hesitate 是猶豫。"}]},
{"id":"r600-13","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"message","ti":"Presentation moved to 2:00","tx":"Maria Santos (9:12 A.M.): Hi, Tom. My train is delayed because of a problem on the line. I won't reach the office until about 10:30.\n\nTom Becker (9:14 A.M.): Thanks for telling me. Our presentation to Mr. Hill is at 10:00, isn't it?\n\nMaria Santos (9:15 A.M.): Yes. Could you ask him to postpone it until 11:00? The slides are on my laptop.\n\nTom Becker (9:21 A.M.): I just called him. He has another meeting at 11:00, but he is free at 2:00 this afternoon.\n\nMaria Santos (9:22 A.M.): Perfect. Please reschedule it for 2:00 and book Conference Room B.\n\nTom Becker (9:24 A.M.): Done. I'll also forward the new agenda to the team.","zh":"Maria Santos（上午 9:12）：嗨，Tom。因為路線出了問題，我的火車誤點了。我大概要到 10:30 才會到辦公室。\n\nTom Becker（上午 9:14）：謝謝妳告訴我。我們對 Hill 先生的簡報是 10 點，對吧？\n\nMaria Santos（上午 9:15）：對。你可以請他延到 11 點嗎？投影片在我的筆電裡。\n\nTom Becker（上午 9:21）：我剛剛打給他了。他 11 點有另一個會議，但今天下午 2 點有空。\n\nMaria Santos（上午 9:22）：太好了。請把簡報改到 2 點，並預訂 B 會議室。\n\nTom Becker（上午 9:24）：辦好了。我也會把新的議程轉寄給團隊。","w":[322,423,424,262,432,348],"qs":[{"q":"Why does Ms. Santos contact Mr. Becker?","o":["To borrow his laptop","To say she will arrive late","To ask for a ride to the office","To cancel a presentation"],"a":1,"ex":"她說 My train is delayed ... I won't reach the office until about 10:30，是通知自己會晚到。她是要把簡報延後而不是取消，也沒有要求接送或借筆電。"},{"q":"When will the presentation take place?","o":["At 2:00 P.M.","At 10:30 A.M.","At 10:00 A.M.","At 11:00 A.M."],"a":0,"ex":"Hill 先生 is free at 2:00 this afternoon，Santos 小姐說 Please reschedule it for 2:00，所以簡報改到下午 2 點。10:00 是原本的時間，10:30 是她到辦公室的時間，11:00 Hill 先生有別的會議。"},{"q":"At 9:24 A.M., what does Mr. Becker mean when he writes, \"Done\"?","o":["He has finished making the slides","He has arrived at the office","He has done what Ms. Santos asked","He does not want to talk anymore"],"a":2,"ex":"Santos 小姐前一句說 Please reschedule it for 2:00 and book Conference Room B，Becker 先生回 Done，意思是「辦好了」，也就是已經照她說的改好時間、訂好會議室。投影片在她的筆電裡，不是他做的；他也沒有說自己剛到辦公室或不想再聊。"}]},
{"id":"r600-14","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"message","ti":"Photocopier problem on the fourth floor","tx":"Jenny Wang (1:05 P.M.): Hi, Mark. The photocopier on the fourth floor has malfunctioned again. Paper keeps getting stuck inside.\n\nMark Davis (1:07 P.M.): Oh no. I need 50 copies of the sales summary for the 3:00 meeting.\n\nJenny Wang (1:08 P.M.): I already called the maintenance company. A technician will come tomorrow morning.\n\nMark Davis (1:10 P.M.): That's too late for me. Is there another machine I can use?\n\nJenny Wang (1:11 P.M.): The accounting division on the second floor has one. Just ask Ms. Ito for permission first.\n\nMark Davis (1:12 P.M.): Great. I'll go down there right now. Thanks!","zh":"Jenny Wang（下午 1:05）：嗨，Mark。四樓的影印機又故障了，紙一直卡在裡面。\n\nMark Davis（下午 1:07）：糟糕。我需要印 50 份業績摘要，3 點開會要用。\n\nJenny Wang（下午 1:08）：我已經打電話給維修公司了。技術人員明天早上會來。\n\nMark Davis（下午 1:10）：那對我來說太晚了。有其他機器可以用嗎？\n\nJenny Wang（下午 1:11）：二樓的會計部有一台。只是要先徵求 Ito 小姐的同意。\n\nMark Davis（下午 1:12）：太好了，我現在就下去。謝謝！","w":[277,499,259,292,333,329,287],"qs":[{"q":"What problem are the writers discussing?","o":["A meeting has been canceled","A technician arrived late","A report contains mistakes","A machine is not working properly"],"a":3,"ex":"Wang 小姐說 The photocopier on the fourth floor has malfunctioned again，影印機又故障了，所以是機器無法正常運作。會議沒有取消，文中也沒有說報告有錯或技術人員遲到。"},{"q":"When will the technician come?","o":["Tomorrow morning","In one hour","At 3:00 P.M. today","Tomorrow afternoon"],"a":0,"ex":"Wang 小姐說 A technician will come tomorrow morning，技術人員明天早上才會來。3:00 是 Davis 先生開會的時間，不是技術人員來的時間。"},{"q":"What will Mr. Davis most likely do next?","o":["Call the maintenance company","Wait for the technician","Cancel the 3:00 meeting","Go to the second floor"],"a":3,"ex":"Wang 小姐說 The accounting division on the second floor has one，Davis 先生回 I'll go down there right now，所以他接下來會去二樓用會計部的影印機。維修公司已經聯絡過了；他說等到明天太晚（too late for me），也沒有要取消會議。"}]},
{"id":"r600-15","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Business English at Summit Language Center","tx":"Improve Your Business English at Summit Language Center!\n\nDo you need better English for your career? Summit Language Center offers evening and weekend courses for busy professionals. Our class times are [1] -------, so you can study around your work schedule.\n\nAll courses are taught by experienced instructors in small groups of eight students or fewer. Students who complete a twelve-week course [2] ------- an official certificate.\n\nOur prices are affordable, and new students can try one lesson for free. To [3] -------, visit our website or call us before the next term begins on March 3.","zh":"到 Summit Language Center 提升您的商務英語！\n\n您的職涯需要更好的英語能力嗎？Summit Language Center 為忙碌的專業人士提供晚間和週末課程。我們的上課時間很有彈性，您可以配合自己的工作時間來學習。\n\n所有課程都由經驗豐富的講師以八人以下的小班方式授課。完成十二週課程的學員會拿到一張正式的證書。\n\n我們的價格實惠，新學員還可以免費試上一堂課。如要註冊，請在 3 月 3 日下一期開課前上我們的網站或來電。","w":[415,382,267,256,381,427,297],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["medical","domestic","anonymous","flexible"],"a":3,"ex":"後面說 so you can study around your work schedule（可以配合工作時間來上課），所以上課時間是 flexible（有彈性的）。anonymous 是匿名的、domestic 是國內的、medical 是醫療的。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["to receive","receives","receive","receiving"],"a":2,"ex":"這句的主詞是複數的 Students（who complete a twelve-week course 只是修飾語），動詞要用複數的現在式 receive。receives 要配單數主詞；receiving 和 to receive 不能當句子的主要動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["enroll","occur","shrink","commute"],"a":0,"ex":"To enroll 是「如要註冊（報名課程）」，後面接著說上網站或打電話，就是報名的方法。shrink 是縮小、occur 是發生、commute 是通勤。"}]},
{"id":"r600-16","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"New express bus to serve Riverside commuters","tx":"New Express Bus to Serve Riverside Commuters\n\nRIVERSIDE — The city's transportation office announced on Monday that a new express bus will begin service on September 2. The bus will run between Riverside Station and the downtown business district, with only three stops along the way.\n\nOfficials predict that the trip will take approximately 25 minutes, about half the time of the current route. The fare will be $2.50, the same as on regular buses.\n\n\"Many people in our community commute downtown every day,\" said office director Laura Kim. \"We hope this service will persuade more of them to leave their cars at home.\"","zh":"新快捷公車將服務 Riverside 通勤族\n\n【Riverside 訊】市政府交通局星期一宣布，新的快捷公車將於 9 月 2 日開始營運。這班公車行駛於 Riverside 車站和市中心商業區之間，沿途只停靠三站。\n\n官員預測車程大約 25 分鐘，約為現有路線所需時間的一半。票價為 2.5 美元，和一般公車相同。\n\n交通局局長 Laura Kim 表示：「我們社區有很多人每天通勤到市中心。希望這項服務能說服更多人把車子留在家裡。」","w":[343,279,426,420,378,271,428,441],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article mainly about?","o":["The closing of a train station","A new parking area downtown","An increase in bus fares","A new bus service"],"a":3,"ex":"標題和第一段都說 a new express bus will begin service on September 2，主題是新的公車服務。票價 the same as on regular buses，沒有調漲；文中也沒有提到車站關閉或新的停車場。"},{"q":"About how long does the current route take?","o":["12 minutes","25 minutes","75 minutes","50 minutes"],"a":3,"ex":"文中說新公車 will take approximately 25 minutes, about half the time of the current route，25 分鐘大約是現有路線的一半，所以現有路線大約要 50 分鐘。25 分鐘是新公車的車程。"},{"q":"What does Ms. Kim hope the new bus will do?","o":["Get more people to travel without their cars","Lower the price of parking","Create jobs for bus drivers","Bring more tourists to Riverside"],"a":0,"ex":"Kim 局長說 We hope this service will persuade more of them to leave their cars at home，希望說服更多人把車留在家裡、改搭公車。文中沒有提到觀光客、司機的工作機會或停車費。"}]},
{"id":"r600-17","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"Harlow Foods to build new plant in Easton","tx":"Harlow Foods to Build New Plant in Easton\n\nEASTON — Harlow Foods, a firm known for its frozen meals, plans to build a new plant in Easton. Construction will begin in March and is expected to take about one year.\n\nThe company will invest $20 million in the project and employ approximately 300 local workers when the plant opens. \"Demand for our products has grown every quarter,\" said company president Rosa Diaz. \"We need more space to keep up.\"\n\nCity leaders welcomed the news. They believe the plant will have a positive impact on the local economy, particularly on small shops and restaurants near the site.","zh":"Harlow Foods 將在 Easton 興建新工廠\n\n【Easton 訊】以冷凍餐點聞名的 Harlow Foods 公司，計劃在 Easton 興建一座新工廠。工程將於三月動工，預計需要大約一年。\n\n該公司將在這項計畫中投資 2,000 萬美元，工廠啟用時將雇用大約 300 名當地員工。公司總裁 Rosa Diaz 表示：「我們產品的需求每一季都在成長。我們需要更多空間才能跟上。」\n\n市府官員對這個消息表示歡迎。他們相信這座工廠會對當地經濟帶來正面影響，尤其是工廠附近的小商店和餐廳。","w":[305,299,251,464,447,420,344,375,328,419],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article mainly about?","o":["A food company's new building project","A change of company president","A drop in sales of frozen meals","A new restaurant opening in Easton"],"a":0,"ex":"標題和第一段說 Harlow Foods ... plans to build a new plant in Easton，主題是食品公司的興建計畫。文中說產品需求一直成長，不是銷售下滑；也沒有提到新餐廳開幕或更換總裁。"},{"q":"According to Ms. Diaz, why does the company need the new plant?","o":["Workers asked for a new site","Costs are lower in Easton","Demand for its products keeps growing","Its old plant was damaged"],"a":2,"ex":"Diaz 總裁說 Demand for our products has grown every quarter ... We need more space to keep up，因為需求每一季都在成長，需要更多空間。文中沒有提到舊工廠受損、員工的要求或成本比較低。"},{"q":"The word \"plant\" in the passage is closest in meaning to","o":["market","office","factory","flower"],"a":2,"ex":"plant 在這裡是「工廠」：公司要 build a new plant，啟用後雇用約 300 名員工來生產產品，最接近 factory。flower 是花（plant 另一個意思是植物，但這裡不是）、office 是辦公室、market 是市場。"}]},
{"id":"r600-18","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"letter","ti":"Thank you for your donation","tx":"Riverton Youth Sports Club\n12 Park Road\n\nJune 20\n\nDear Mr. Walker,\n\nOn behalf of the Riverton Youth Sports Club, I would like to express our [1] ------- for your kind donation of $2,000. Your company has sponsored our summer program for three years, and your support makes a real difference in our community.\n\nLast month, the money [2] ------- to buy new soccer balls and uniforms for more than 60 children. We have enclosed some photos from our first practice.\n\nWe would be pleased if you could join us at our closing ceremony on August 15. [3] -------\n\nSincerely,\nAngela Price\nClub Director","zh":"Riverton Youth Sports Club\n12 Park Road\n\n6 月 20 日\n\nWalker 先生您好：\n\n我謹代表 Riverton Youth Sports Club，對您善心捐贈的 2,000 美元表達我們的感謝。貴公司已經贊助我們的夏季活動三年了，您的支持為我們的社區帶來了實質的改變。\n\n上個月，這筆錢被用來為 60 多名孩子購買新的足球和制服。隨信附上幾張我們第一次練習時的照片。\n\n如果您能來參加我們 8 月 15 日的閉幕典禮，我們會非常高興。正式的邀請函將在下個月寄給您。\n\n社長\nAngela Price 敬上","w":[330,268,498,271,273],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["appreciated","appreciation","appreciative","appreciate"],"a":1,"ex":"所有格 our 後面要接名詞，express our appreciation for 是「對…表達我們的感謝」。appreciate 是動詞、appreciated 是過去式或過去分詞、appreciative 是形容詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["has used","is using","was used","uses"],"a":2,"ex":"主詞 the money（這筆錢）是「被用來」買東西的，要用被動語態；Last month 是過去的時間，所以是 was used。is using、uses、has used 都是主動，變成錢自己去使用別的東西，意思不通。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Your application for the position has been received.","A formal invitation will be mailed to you next month.","The program was canceled because of low interest.","Please pay the balance by the end of the week."],"a":1,"ex":"前一句邀請 Walker 先生參加 8 月 15 日的閉幕典禮，接著說「正式的邀請函下個月會寄給您」最自然。這是一封感謝函，沒有要他付款；活動正在進行，並沒有取消；他是贊助人，不是來應徵工作的。"}]},
{"id":"r600-19","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"letter","ti":"A change to your savings account","tx":"Harbor Bank\n45 Dock Street\n\nMarch 3\n\nDear Mr. Tanaka,\n\nThank you for being a customer of Harbor Bank. I am writing regarding your savings account.\n\nBeginning April 1, the interest rate on your account will rise from 1.2 percent to 1.5 percent. To receive the new rate, you must maintain a balance of at least $1,000. If your balance falls below this amount, the current rate will apply.\n\nYou do not need to do anything to accept this change. Your monthly statement will show the new rate starting in April. As always, you may withdraw or deposit money at any time without a charge.\n\nSincerely,\nEmily Stone\nCustomer Service Manager","zh":"Harbor Bank\n45 Dock Street\n\n3 月 3 日\n\nTanaka 先生您好：\n\n感謝您成為 Harbor Bank 的客戶。這封信是關於您的儲蓄帳戶。\n\n自 4 月 1 日起，您帳戶的利率將從 1.2% 調升為 1.5%。若要享有新利率，您的帳戶餘額必須維持在至少 1,000 美元。如果餘額低於這個金額，將適用目前的利率。\n\n您不需要做任何事就能接受這項變更。從四月開始，您每月的對帳單上會顯示新利率。和以往一樣，您可以隨時提款或存款，不收任何費用。\n\n客戶服務經理\nEmily Stone 敬上","w":[250,270,368,446,258,378,337,469,373,486],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the letter?","o":["To tell a customer about a higher interest rate","To report a problem with an account","To announce a new bank fee","To ask a customer to open an account"],"a":0,"ex":"信中說 the interest rate on your account will rise from 1.2 percent to 1.5 percent，目的是通知利率調升。文中沒有說帳戶有問題；Tanaka 先生已經有帳戶；存提款 without a charge（不收費），也沒有新的手續費。"},{"q":"What must Mr. Tanaka do to receive the new rate?","o":["Have at least $1,000 in his account","Sign and return a form","Open a second savings account","Visit the bank before April 1"],"a":0,"ex":"文中說 To receive the new rate, you must maintain a balance of at least $1,000，帳戶餘額至少要有 1,000 美元。信中也說 You do not need to do anything to accept this change，所以不用去銀行、簽表格或另外開戶。"},{"q":"The word \"regarding\" in the passage is closest in meaning to","o":["about","without","against","after"],"a":0,"ex":"I am writing regarding your savings account 是「我寫這封信是關於您的儲蓄帳戶」，regarding 是「關於」，最接近 about。after 是在…之後、without 是沒有、against 是反對。"}]},
{"id":"r600-20","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"letter","ti":"Your lease for Apartment 5C","tx":"Greenfield Apartments\nManagement Office\n\nNovember 10\n\nDear Ms. Novak,\n\nYour lease for Apartment 5C will end on December 31. We would be happy to have you stay as our tenant. If you wish to extend your lease for another year, please sign the attached contract and return it to our office by December 1.\n\nThe monthly rent will remain $900. However, starting in January, utilities will no longer be included, so tenants will pay for their own water and electricity. Your current deposit will be kept for the new term, and no additional payment is required now.\n\nPlease call me if you have any concerns.\n\nSincerely,\nRobert Hayes\nProperty Manager","zh":"Greenfield Apartments\n管理室\n\n11 月 10 日\n\nNovak 小姐您好：\n\n您 5C 公寓的租約將於 12 月 31 日到期。我們很樂意您繼續當我們的房客。如果您想把租約再延長一年，請在隨信附上的合約上簽名，並在 12 月 1 日前交回我們的辦公室。\n\n每月租金維持 900 美元不變。不過，從一月開始，租金將不再包含水電費，所以房客要自行支付水費和電費。您目前的押金會保留到新的租期，現在不需要另外付款。\n\n如果您有任何疑慮，請打電話給我。\n\n物業經理\nRobert Hayes 敬上","w":[495,339,435,367,346,378,373,297,405,490],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Mr. Hayes write to Ms. Novak?","o":["To return her deposit","To announce a rent increase","To invite her to extend her lease","To ask her to move out"],"a":2,"ex":"信中說 If you wish to extend your lease for another year, please sign the attached contract，是請她考慮續約。信中歡迎她繼續住；租金 will remain $900（不變）；押金會保留到新租期，不是退還。"},{"q":"What will change in January?","o":["Tenants will pay for water and electricity","The rent will go up","The management office will move","A new deposit will be required"],"a":0,"ex":"文中說 starting in January, utilities will no longer be included, so tenants will pay for their own water and electricity。租金不變；押金沿用（no additional payment is required now）；文中也沒有提到管理室搬家。"},{"q":"The word \"term\" in the passage is closest in meaning to","o":["price","period","rule","word"],"a":1,"ex":"the new term 指的是「新的租期」，term 在這裡是一段期間，最接近 period。word 是字詞（term 也有「術語」的意思，但這裡不是）、rule 是規則、price 是價格。"}]},
{"id":"r600-21","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"announcement","ti":"Bella Home opens its third outlet","tx":"Grand Opening: Bella Home Opens Its Third Outlet\n\nBella Home is pleased to announce the opening of its newest outlet in the Westgate Shopping Center on Saturday, November 8. The store will [1] ------- furniture, kitchen goods, and a wide selection of home decorations.\n\nTo celebrate, the first 100 customers will receive a [2] ------- gift bag. In addition, all merchandise will be 20 percent off during the opening weekend.\n\nThe new store is easily [3] ------- by bus and subway, and free parking is available for shoppers. Store hours are 10:00 A.M. to 9:00 P.M. every day. We hope to see you there!","zh":"盛大開幕：Bella Home 第三家門市開張\n\nBella Home 很高興宣布，位於 Westgate Shopping Center 的最新門市將於 11 月 8 日星期六開幕。這家店主打家具、廚房用品，以及種類豐富的居家裝飾品。\n\n為了慶祝開幕，前 100 位顧客將獲得一個免費的禮物袋。此外，開幕週末期間全店商品一律八折。\n\n新門市搭公車和地鐵都很容易到達，也為購物的顧客提供免費停車位。營業時間為每天上午 10 點至晚上 9 點。期待您的光臨！","w":[300,496,393,331,404],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["postpone","feature","persuade","predict"],"a":1,"ex":"feature 當動詞是「以…為特色、主打」，The store will feature furniture, kitchen goods... 是說這家店主打家具、廚房用品等商品。predict 是預測、persuade 是說服、postpone 是延後，後面都不能接這些商品。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["punctual","verbal","cautious","complimentary"],"a":3,"ex":"a complimentary gift bag 是「免費贈送的禮物袋」，為了慶祝開幕送給前 100 位顧客。punctual 是準時的、cautious 是謹慎的、verbal 是口頭的，都不能形容禮物袋。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["access","accessible","accessibility","accessibly"],"a":1,"ex":"be 動詞 is 後面要接形容詞，前面的副詞 easily 用來修飾它，is easily accessible by bus and subway 是「搭公車和地鐵都很容易到達」。access 是名詞或動詞、accessibly 是副詞、accessibility 是名詞。"}]},
{"id":"r600-22","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"announcement","ti":"Employee of the Year award ceremony","tx":"Employee of the Year Award Ceremony\n\nWestbrook Electronics is pleased to announce that this year's award ceremony will be held on Friday, December 12, at 6:00 P.M. in the Grand Hall of the Parkside Hotel.\n\nThe committee has nominated three employees for their excellent performance. The winner will receive a reward of $1,000 and two additional days of paid vacation. A reception with food and drinks will follow the ceremony.\n\nAll employees are invited. To help us plan, please register on the company website by December 5. Transportation from the office to the hotel will be provided at 5:15 P.M.","zh":"年度最佳員工頒獎典禮\n\nWestbrook Electronics 很高興宣布，今年的頒獎典禮將於 12 月 12 日星期五下午 6 點，在 Parkside Hotel 的 Grand Hall 舉行。\n\n委員會已提名三位表現優異的員工。得獎者將獲得 1,000 美元獎金，以及額外兩天的有薪假。典禮結束後會有提供餐點和飲料的招待會。\n\n歡迎所有員工參加。為了方便我們安排，請在 12 月 5 日前到公司網站報名。下午 5 點 15 分將提供從辦公室到飯店的交通接送。","w":[273,298,481,263,359,405,325,494,279],"qs":[{"q":"What event is being announced?","o":["A retirement party","A company award ceremony","A staff training day","A hotel opening"],"a":1,"ex":"公告說 this year's award ceremony will be held on Friday, December 12，是公司的頒獎典禮。飯店只是舉辦地點，文中沒有提到訓練或退休派對。"},{"q":"What will the winner receive?","o":["A free hotel stay","Dinner for two","Money and extra vacation days","A promotion to manager"],"a":2,"ex":"文中說 The winner will receive a reward of $1,000 and two additional days of paid vacation，是獎金加上額外兩天有薪假。文中沒有提到升遷、免費住宿或雙人晚餐。"},{"q":"What is NOT mentioned in the announcement?","o":["The names of the nominated employees","The way employees can get to the hotel","The place where the event will be held","The deadline for signing up"],"a":0,"ex":"地點有寫 in the Grand Hall of the Parkside Hotel，報名期限有寫 register ... by December 5，交通有寫 Transportation from the office to the hotel will be provided。文中只說提名了 three employees，沒有寫出他們的名字。"}]},
{"id":"r600-23","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"announcement","ti":"Book donation week at Oakdale Shopping Center","tx":"Help Us Support the Oakdale Community Library\n\nOakdale Shopping Center will host a book donation event from May 5 to May 11. We invite everyone in the community to donate used books in good condition. All books will go to the Oakdale Community Library, which is opening a new reading room for children.\n\nDonation boxes will be located near the main entrance and beside the food court. Every person who contributes five or more books will receive a complimentary drink ticket as a sign of our appreciation.\n\nThe event is sponsored by Page One Bookstore. For details, please visit the information desk on the first floor.","zh":"一起支持 Oakdale 社區圖書館\n\nOakdale Shopping Center 將於 5 月 5 日至 5 月 11 日舉辦捐書活動。我們邀請社區的每一位朋友捐出狀況良好的二手書。所有書籍都會送到 Oakdale 社區圖書館，圖書館即將啟用一間新的兒童閱覽室。\n\n捐書箱將設在正門附近和美食街旁邊。每位捐出五本以上書籍的民眾，都可以得到一張免費飲料券，以表達我們的感謝。\n\n本活動由 Page One Bookstore 贊助。詳情請洽一樓的服務台。","w":[271,363,268,431,465,434,393,330,498],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the announcement?","o":["To advertise a bookstore sale","To invite people to a food festival","To announce new library hours","To ask people to give books"],"a":3,"ex":"公告說 We invite everyone in the community to donate used books，是請大家捐書。Page One Bookstore 只是贊助商，文中沒有提到特賣、圖書館開放時間或美食活動。"},{"q":"Where can people leave their books?","o":["Near the main entrance","At the community library","At Page One Bookstore","At the information desk"],"a":0,"ex":"文中說 Donation boxes will be located near the main entrance and beside the food court，捐書箱在正門附近和美食街旁邊。書最後會送到圖書館，但不是在那裡收；Page One Bookstore 是贊助商；服務台是詢問詳情的地方。"},{"q":"The word \"host\" in the passage is closest in meaning to","o":["watch","attend","cancel","hold"],"a":3,"ex":"will host a book donation event 是「將舉辦捐書活動」，host 是主辦，最接近 hold（舉行）。attend 是參加、cancel 是取消、watch 是觀看。"}]},
{"id":"r600-24","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"article","ti":"Norvale Motors reports strong third quarter","tx":"Norvale Motors Reports Strong Third Quarter\n\nNorvale Motors announced on Tuesday that its profit for the third quarter rose 12 percent compared with the same period last year. The result [1] ------- the company's own forecast of 8 percent.\n\nCompany president Alan Pierce said that sales of small cars were [2] ------- strong in overseas markets. \"Consumers want vehicles that use less fuel, and we are ready to meet that demand,\" he said.\n\n[3] ------- the good news, Mr. Pierce remains cautious. He noted that competitors plan to launch several new models next year, which could affect the firm's future sales.","zh":"Norvale Motors 第三季表現亮眼\n\nNorvale Motors 星期二宣布，第三季的獲利比去年同期成長了 12%。這個結果超過了公司自己預測的 8%。\n\n公司總裁 Alan Pierce 表示，小型車在海外市場的銷售特別強勁。他說：「消費者想要更省油的車輛，而我們已經準備好滿足這個需求。」\n\n儘管有這個好消息，Pierce 先生仍然保持謹慎。他指出，競爭對手計劃明年推出幾款新車，這可能會影響公司未來的銷售。","w":[370,344,376,474,419,417,313,398,255,425,305],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["enrolled","exceeded","persuaded","postponed"],"a":1,"ex":"獲利成長 12%，比公司自己預測的 8% 還高，所以是 exceeded the company's own forecast（超過公司自己的預測）。postponed 是延後、persuaded 是說服、enrolled 是註冊，放進去意思都不通。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["particularly","approximately","verbally","punctually"],"a":0,"ex":"particularly strong 是「特別強勁」，說明小型車在海外市場賣得特別好。approximately 是大約（後面通常接數字）、punctually 是準時地、verbally 是口頭上，都不能修飾 strong。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Although","Instead","Despite","Because of"],"a":2,"ex":"前面是好消息，後面卻說他 remains cautious（仍然謹慎），是轉折；空格後面接的是名詞 the good news，要用介系詞 Despite（儘管）。Although 也是「雖然」，但後面要接完整的句子；Because of 是因為，邏輯相反；Instead 是副詞，後面不能直接接名詞。"}]},
{"id":"r600-25","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"review","ti":"Review of Seaside Garden Hotel","tx":"Seaside Garden Hotel\nRating: 4 out of 5\nReviewed by Linda Moore\n\nI stayed at the Seaside Garden Hotel for three nights during a business conference. My room was spacious and very clean, and the rate was reasonable for a hotel so close to the beach. I particularly liked the complimentary breakfast, which had a wide variety of fresh food.\n\nThe staff at the reception desk were friendly and gave me useful advice about local transportation. My only complaint is that the Internet was slow in the evenings, so it was hard to send large files.\n\nMy overall experience was good, and I would recommend this hotel to other business travelers.","zh":"Seaside Garden Hotel\n評分：4 分（滿分 5 分）\n評論者：Linda Moore\n\n我在參加商務研討會期間，在 Seaside Garden Hotel 住了三晚。我的房間寬敞又非常乾淨，而且以離海灘這麼近的飯店來說，房價很合理。我特別喜歡免費的早餐，有各式各樣的新鮮食物。\n\n接待櫃台的員工很親切，還給了我關於當地交通的實用建議。我唯一的抱怨是晚上的網路很慢，很難傳送大型檔案。\n\n我的整體體驗很好，我會把這家飯店推薦給其他商務旅客。","w":[262,397,368,406,419,393,325,279,489,400],"qs":[{"q":"Why was Ms. Moore staying at the hotel?","o":["She was visiting relatives","She was attending a conference","She was interviewing for a job","She was on a family vacation"],"a":1,"ex":"她說 I stayed ... for three nights during a business conference，是在參加商務研討會期間入住的。文中沒有提到家庭旅遊、面試或探親。"},{"q":"What problem does Ms. Moore mention?","o":["The Internet was slow at night","The staff were unfriendly","The room was too small","The breakfast was expensive"],"a":0,"ex":"她說 My only complaint is that the Internet was slow in the evenings，唯一的抱怨是晚上網路很慢。房間是 spacious（寬敞），早餐是 complimentary（免費），員工是 friendly（親切）。"},{"q":"What is suggested about the hotel?","o":["It has no reception desk","It is only for business travelers","It is located near the beach","It charges extra for breakfast"],"a":2,"ex":"文中說 a hotel so close to the beach，可見飯店離海灘很近。早餐是 complimentary（免費），不另外收費；文中有提到 reception desk；她推薦給商務旅客，但沒有說只有商務旅客才能入住。"}]},
{"id":"r600-26","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"review","ti":"Review of the TaskPilot app","tx":"Product Review: TaskPilot\nRating: 4 out of 5\nBy Sam Carter, small business owner\n\nI started using TaskPilot three months ago to track my team's assignments. The interface is simple, and it took me only a few minutes to learn. My favorite feature is the dashboard, which shows every project deadline on one screen. You can also customize the colors and categories.\n\nThe 30-day trial is free. After that, the subscription costs $9 a month, which is affordable for a small firm like mine. However, the phone application sometimes closes without warning. I hope the company fixes this soon.\n\nIn conclusion, TaskPilot is a useful tool, and I recommend it.","zh":"產品評論：TaskPilot\n評分：4 分（滿分 5 分）\n評論者：小型企業老闆 Sam Carter\n\n三個月前，我開始用 TaskPilot 來追蹤團隊的工作任務。它的介面很簡單，我只花了幾分鐘就學會了。我最喜歡的功能是儀表板，它可以在一個畫面上顯示每個專案的截止日。你還可以自訂顏色和類別。\n\n30 天的試用是免費的。之後訂閱費是每月 9 美元，對我這種小公司來說負擔得起。不過，手機版的應用程式有時候會無預警關閉。希望公司能盡快修正。\n\n總而言之，TaskPilot 是很實用的工具，我推薦它。","w":[485,264,355,496,310,260,476,274,327,253,381,305,276,272],"qs":[{"q":"What is Mr. Carter reviewing?","o":["A new mobile phone","A computer repair service","A tool for managing team tasks","An online business course"],"a":2,"ex":"他說用 TaskPilot to track my team's assignments，還提到 interface、dashboard、phone application，可見這是一個管理團隊工作的軟體工具。他評論的不是手機、維修服務或課程。"},{"q":"How much does TaskPilot cost after the trial?","o":["$9 a year","$3 a month","$30 a month","$9 a month"],"a":3,"ex":"文中說 After that, the subscription costs $9 a month，試用結束後每月 9 美元。30 是試用的天數，three months 是他已經使用的時間，都不是價格。"},{"q":"What is NOT mentioned as a feature of TaskPilot?","o":["Colors that users can change","A chat tool for team members","An interface that is easy to learn","A screen that shows deadlines"],"a":1,"ex":"文中有 the dashboard, which shows every project deadline on one screen（顯示截止日的畫面）、customize the colors（可以自訂顏色）、The interface is simple ... only a few minutes to learn（介面好學）。只有團隊聊天工具沒有提到。"}]},
{"id":"r600-27","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"message","ti":"Reminder from Harbor View Hotel","tx":"Message from Harbor View Hotel\n\nHello, Ms. Kim. This is a reminder that your reservation at Harbor View Hotel begins tomorrow, July 22. Check-in starts at 3:00 P.M. [1] ------- you plan to arrive after 10:00 P.M., please let us know in advance.\n\nYour room rate includes breakfast and [2] ------- to the fitness center. Our airport shuttle bus runs every 30 minutes and is complimentary for hotel guests.\n\nAt check-in, please show [3] ------- photo identification and the credit card used for your booking. We look forward to welcoming you!","zh":"Harbor View Hotel 的訊息\n\nKim 小姐您好。提醒您，您在 Harbor View Hotel 的訂房從明天 7 月 22 日開始。下午 3 點開始辦理入住。如果您打算晚上 10 點以後才抵達，請事先告訴我們。\n\n您的房價包含早餐和健身中心的使用權。我們的機場接駁車每 30 分鐘一班，飯店房客可免費搭乘。\n\n辦理入住時，請出示有效的附照片身分證明，以及訂房時使用的信用卡。期待您的光臨！","w":[368,371,393,401,269,366],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["Although","If","Unless","Until"],"a":1,"ex":"意思是「如果您打算晚上 10 點以後才抵達，請事先告訴我們」，表示條件要用 If。Unless 是除非，意思會變成相反；Although 是雖然、Until 是直到，放進去句意都不通。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["evidence","priority","access","balance"],"a":2,"ex":"access to 是「使用…的權利」，房價包含早餐和 access to the fitness center（健身中心的使用權）。balance 是餘額、evidence 是證據、priority 是優先事項，都不能和 to the fitness center 搭配。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["spacious","valid","verbal","punctual"],"a":1,"ex":"valid photo identification 是「有效的附照片身分證明」，辦理入住時要出示有效的證件。spacious 是寬敞的、punctual 是準時的、verbal 是口頭的，都不能形容身分證明文件。"}]},
{"id":"r600-28","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"form","ti":"Order confirmation 58213","tx":"ORDER CONFIRMATION\nBrightway Office Supplies\n\nOrder number: 58213\nOrder date: June 3\nCustomer: Ms. Karen Hsu, Delta Accounting Firm\n\nItems purchased:\n2 office chairs (black), $90 each\n1 standing desk, $240\n5 boxes of copy paper, $6 each\n\nMerchandise total: $450\nShipping charge: $0 (complimentary for orders over $300)\nTotal paid by credit card: $450\n\nEstimated delivery: June 7 by Swift Courier\n\nNotes: The chairs must be assembled by the customer. Instructions are in the box. Unused items may be returned within 14 days. To track your shipment, enter your order number on our website.","zh":"訂單確認\nBrightway Office Supplies\n\n訂單編號：58213\n訂購日期：6 月 3 日\n顧客：Delta Accounting Firm 的 Karen Hsu 小姐\n\n購買品項：\n辦公椅（黑色）2 張，每張 90 美元\n站立式辦公桌 1 張，240 美元\n影印紙 5 箱，每箱 6 美元\n\n商品總計：450 美元\n運費：0 美元（訂單超過 300 美元免運費）\n信用卡付款總額：450 美元\n\n預計送達：6 月 7 日，由 Swift Courier 配送\n\n備註：椅子須由顧客自行組裝，說明書在箱子裡。未使用的商品可在 14 天內退貨。如要追蹤貨件，請在我們的網站上輸入訂單編號。","w":[329,305,492,331,486,393,366,341,448,485,316],"qs":[{"q":"Why was Ms. Hsu not charged for shipping?","o":["She picked up the items herself","She is a new customer","She used a discount coupon","Her order was over $300"],"a":3,"ex":"表單上寫 Shipping charge: $0 (complimentary for orders over $300)，訂單超過 300 美元就免運費，而她的商品總計是 450 美元。商品是由快遞送達的，文中也沒有提到折價券或新顧客優惠。"},{"q":"What must Ms. Hsu do with the chairs?","o":["Pick them up at a store","Pay for them on delivery","Return them within 7 days","Put them together"],"a":3,"ex":"備註寫 The chairs must be assembled by the customer，assemble 是組裝，所以她要自己把椅子組起來。退貨期限是 14 天，而且不是一定要退；商品由快遞送達；款項已經用信用卡付清。"},{"q":"What information is NOT included in the form?","o":["The date of the order","The price of each item","The name of the delivery company","The customer's street address"],"a":3,"ex":"表單有 Order date: June 3（訂購日期）、每項商品的價格、Swift Courier（配送公司），但沒有寫顧客的地址。"}]},
{"id":"r600-29","lv":600,"p":7,"k":"form","ti":"Travel itinerary for Mr. Reyes","tx":"TRAVEL ITINERARY\nPrepared for: Mr. David Reyes, Sales Division\n\nMonday, October 6\n8:40 A.M. Depart Dallas on Flight 302\n11:05 A.M. Arrive in Chicago (layover: 1 hour 30 minutes)\n12:35 P.M. Depart Chicago on Flight 518\n2:05 P.M. Arrive in Minneapolis\nTransportation to hotel: complimentary shuttle bus\nHotel: Pinecrest Inn (two nights)\n\nTuesday, October 7\n9:00 A.M. to 4:00 P.M. Retail Industry Conference, City Convention Center\n6:30 P.M. Evening reception\n\nWednesday, October 8\n10:05 A.M. Depart Minneapolis on Flight 177 (direct flight to Dallas)\n\nNote: Please bring your conference registration number and photo identification.","zh":"出差行程表\n出差人：業務部 David Reyes 先生\n\n10 月 6 日星期一\n上午 8:40　搭乘 302 號班機從達拉斯出發\n上午 11:05　抵達芝加哥（轉機停留：1 小時 30 分鐘）\n下午 12:35　搭乘 518 號班機從芝加哥出發\n下午 2:05　抵達明尼亞波利斯\n前往飯店的交通：免費接駁車\n飯店：Pinecrest Inn（兩晚）\n\n10 月 7 日星期二\n上午 9:00 至下午 4:00　零售產業研討會，City Convention Center\n下午 6:30　晚間招待會\n\n10 月 8 日星期三\n上午 10:05　搭乘 177 號班機從明尼亞波利斯出發（直飛達拉斯）\n\n備註：請攜帶您的研討會報名編號和附照片的身分證明文件。","w":[352,287,347,279,393,364,266,262,325,278,269],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main reason for Mr. Reyes's trip?","o":["To attend a conference","To open a new store","To interview job applicants","To take a vacation"],"a":0,"ex":"行程表上星期二整天是 Retail Industry Conference，備註也要他帶 conference registration number，可見這趟出差主要是參加研討會。文中沒有提到開店、面試或度假。"},{"q":"Where will Mr. Reyes wait between flights on Monday?","o":["At the Pinecrest Inn","In Minneapolis","In Chicago","In Dallas"],"a":2,"ex":"行程寫 Arrive in Chicago (layover: 1 hour 30 minutes)，layover 是轉機停留，所以他星期一在芝加哥等下一班飛機。達拉斯是出發地，明尼亞波利斯是目的地，Pinecrest Inn 是抵達後住的飯店。"},{"q":"What is indicated about the shuttle bus to the hotel?","o":["It is free of charge","It goes to the convention center","It must be booked in advance","It leaves at 2:05 P.M."],"a":0,"ex":"行程寫 Transportation to hotel: complimentary shuttle bus，complimentary 是「免費的」。2:05 是飛機抵達的時間；接駁車是開往飯店的；文中也沒有說要事先預約。"}]},
{"id":"r600-30","lv":600,"p":6,"k":"review","ti":"Review of Olive Tree Kitchen","tx":"Olive Tree Kitchen\nRating: 5 out of 5\nReviewed by Hannah Fisher\n\nLast Saturday, my family and I had dinner at Olive Tree Kitchen, a small restaurant that opened in March. The chef uses fresh [1] ------- from local farms, and you can really taste the difference. I ordered the grilled fish, which [2] ------- with rice and vegetables.\n\nThe prices were [3] ------- for the quality. Our meal for four people cost only $70. The servers were particularly friendly and brought our food quickly.\n\nThe restaurant already has a strong reputation, so I suggest booking a table in advance. We will certainly go back.","zh":"Olive Tree Kitchen\n評分：5 分（滿分 5 分）\n評論者：Hannah Fisher\n\n上週六，我和家人到 Olive Tree Kitchen 吃晚餐，這是一家三月才開幕的小餐廳。主廚使用來自當地農場的新鮮食材，真的吃得出差別。我點了烤魚，搭配白飯和蔬菜一起上桌。\n\n以這樣的品質來說，價格很合理。我們四個人這一餐只花了 70 美元。服務生特別親切，上菜也很快。\n\n這家餐廳已經有很好的名聲，所以我建議事先訂位。我們一定會再去。","w":[254,406,419,351,451],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["ingredients","statements","appliances","utilities"],"a":0,"ex":"主廚用來自當地農場的 fresh ingredients（新鮮食材）做菜，所以吃得出差別。appliances 是家電、statements 是對帳單、utilities 是水電費，都不是農場生產、可以拿來做菜的東西。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["serving","has served","was served","serves"],"a":2,"ex":"which 指的是 the grilled fish（烤魚），魚是「被端上桌」的，要用被動語態；事情發生在 Last Saturday，所以是過去式 was served。has served 和 serves 是主動，變成魚自己去上菜；serving 前面沒有 be 動詞，不能當動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["reasonable","spacious","punctual","anonymous"],"a":0,"ex":"後面說四個人只花了 70 美元，所以價格是 reasonable（合理的）。spacious 是寬敞的（形容空間）、punctual 是準時的、anonymous 是匿名的，都不能形容價格。"}]},
{"id":"r800-01","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Delay in your office chair order","tx":"To: Karen Wu\nFrom: Daniel Ortiz, Brightline Office Supply\nSubject: Delay in your office chair order\n\nDear Ms. Wu,\n\nThank you for your recent order of 40 office chairs (invoice #5821). I am writing to notify you that the shipment will not arrive on March 4 as scheduled. During a routine inspection at our warehouse, we detected a defect in the wheels of several chairs. To ensure that every chair you receive is reliable, we have asked the manufacturer to replace the entire batch.\n\nOur current estimate is that the chairs will be delivered on March 18. To compensate you for the inconvenience, we will deduct 10 percent from your invoice, and you will not be charged for delivery.\n\nIf the new date does not suit you, an alternative model is in stock and can be shipped within two days. Please let me know by Friday how you would like to proceed.\n\nSincerely,\nDaniel Ortiz\nCustomer Representative","zh":"收件人：Karen Wu\n寄件人：Daniel Ortiz，Brightline Office Supply\n主旨：您的辦公椅訂單延遲\n\n吳小姐您好：\n\n感謝您最近訂購 40 張辦公椅（發票號碼 5821）。來信是要通知您，這批貨無法如期在 3 月 4 日送達。我們在倉庫進行例行檢查時，發現其中幾張椅子的輪子有瑕疵。為了確保您收到的每一張椅子都可靠耐用，我們已請製造商更換整批貨。\n\n我們目前估計椅子會在 3 月 18 日送達。為了補償造成您的不便，我們會從您的發票金額中扣除 10%，而且不收運費。\n\n如果新的日期對您不方便，我們另有一款替代型號有現貨，可以在兩天內出貨。請在星期五之前告訴我您希望如何處理。\n\n敬上\nDaniel Ortiz\n客戶服務代表","w":[725,531,685,514,702,674,580,691],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main purpose of the e-mail?","o":["To request payment of an overdue invoice","To confirm that an order has arrived","To advertise a new chair model","To explain why a delivery will be late"],"a":3,"ex":"信中說 the shipment will not arrive on March 4 as scheduled，接著說明原因是 detected a defect in the wheels，所以目的是解釋交貨為什麼會延遲。訂單還沒送到，信中也沒有催繳款項；替代型號只是延遲時的另一個選擇，不是這封信的主要目的。"},{"q":"What was found during the inspection?","o":["An error in the invoice total","Damage to the delivery truck","A shortage of warehouse staff","A problem with some chair wheels"],"a":3,"ex":"關鍵句是 we detected a defect in the wheels of several chairs，defect 是「瑕疵」，也就是部分椅子的輪子有問題。發票金額錯誤、倉庫人手不足、貨車受損，文中都沒有提到。"},{"q":"What is NOT offered to Ms. Wu?","o":["A lower price on her order","Free delivery","A different chair model","A full refund"],"a":3,"ex":"deduct 10 percent from your invoice 是降價，you will not be charged for delivery 是免運費，an alternative model is in stock 是可以改訂另一款型號，這三項都有提供。只有全額退款在信中完全沒有出現。"}]},
{"id":"r800-02","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"Elevator inspection on Thursday","tx":"NOTICE TO ALL TENANTS\nElevator Inspection: Thursday, June 12\n\nThe annual safety inspection of the elevators in Parkview Tower is mandatory under city regulations. It will be conducted this Thursday from 9:00 A.M. to 1:00 P.M.\n\nOnly one passenger elevator will be taken out of operation at a time, so the other two will remain available. However, waiting times may be longer than usual. As a precaution, use of the freight elevator will be restricted to building personnel during the inspection. Tenants who are expecting large deliveries should reschedule them for the afternoon.\n\nAnyone who needs assistance while the elevators are being checked may ask at the security desk in the lobby.\n\nWe apologize for any inconvenience. For further information, please contact the management office at extension 204.\n\nParkview Tower Management","zh":"致全體承租戶公告\n電梯檢查：6 月 12 日星期四\n\n依照市政法規，Parkview Tower 的電梯每年都必須進行安全檢查。這次檢查將於本週四上午 9 點至下午 1 點進行。\n\n每次只會停用一部客用電梯，其他兩部仍可正常使用，不過等候時間可能會比平常久。為了預防萬一，檢查期間貨梯僅限大樓工作人員使用。預計有大型貨物送達的承租戶，請將送貨時間改到下午。\n\n電梯檢查期間如需協助，可洽大廳的保全櫃檯。\n\n造成不便，敬請見諒。如需進一步資訊，請撥分機 204 與管理室聯絡。\n\nParkview Tower 管理處","w":[531,639,710,533,532,670,528,580],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the inspection being carried out?","o":["New elevators are being installed","An elevator broke down last week","Tenants complained about long waits","It is required by city rules"],"a":3,"ex":"文中說 The annual safety inspection ... is mandatory under city regulations，mandatory 是「強制的、依規定必須做的」，所以這是市政法規要求的年度檢查。電梯故障、承租戶抱怨、安裝新電梯都沒有提到。"},{"q":"What are tenants expecting large deliveries advised to do?","o":["Pay a fee to use the freight elevator","Have them left in the lobby","Cancel them until next week","Move them to the afternoon"],"a":3,"ex":"Tenants who are expecting large deliveries should reschedule them for the afternoon，reschedule 是「改時間」。檢查到下午 1 點結束，所以建議把送貨改到下午。取消、放在大廳、付費使用貨梯都不是文中的建議。"},{"q":"The word \"restricted\" in the notice is closest in meaning to","o":["extended","limited","repaired","offered"],"a":1,"ex":"use of the freight elevator will be restricted to building personnel 意思是貨梯「只限」大樓人員使用，restricted 就是 limited（受限制的）。extended 是延長、repaired 是修理、offered 是提供，意思都不一樣。"}]},
{"id":"r800-03","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"memo","ti":"New procedure for travel expenses","tx":"MEMO\nTo: All sales personnel\nFrom: Linda Park, Finance Department\nDate: September 2\nSubject: New procedure for travel expenses\n\nBeginning October 1, the company will implement a new procedure for travel expense claims. The objective is to streamline the process and reduce the time employees wait for payment.\n\nInstead of filling out paper forms, you will upload a photo of each receipt or invoice to the online expense system. Your supervisor will then validate the claim, and the amount will be transferred to your bank account. Claims that follow the guidelines should be paid within five working days, rather than the current three weeks.\n\nPlease note that claims submitted more than 30 days after a trip will be declined.\n\nA 20-minute webinar outlining the new system will be held on September 15 and again on September 17. Attendance at one of these sessions is compulsory.","zh":"備忘錄\n收件人：全體業務人員\n寄件人：Linda Park，財務部\n日期：9 月 2 日\n主旨：差旅費申請新流程\n\n自 10 月 1 日起，公司將實施新的差旅費申請流程，目的是簡化作業，縮短員工等待款項的時間。\n\n以後不必再填寫紙本表單，只要把每張收據或發票拍照，上傳到線上費用系統即可。接著由您的主管審核確認，款項就會匯入您的銀行帳戶。符合規範的申請應可在五個工作天內付款，不必像現在要等三個星期。\n\n請注意，出差結束超過 30 天才提出的申請將不予受理。\n\n說明新系統的 20 分鐘網路研討會將於 9 月 15 日舉行，9 月 17 日再辦一場。兩場之中必須參加一場。","w":[564,676,541,732,694,544,746,610],"qs":[{"q":"What is the memo mainly about?","o":["A new schedule for paychecks","A change in how expenses are claimed","A training course for supervisors","A reduction in the travel budget"],"a":1,"ex":"第一句 the company will implement a new procedure for travel expense claims 點出主題：申請差旅費的方式要改了。文中沒有說要刪減差旅預算或更改發薪日；網路研討會是全體業務人員都要參加，不是專為主管開的課。"},{"q":"How quickly should claims be paid under the new procedure?","o":["Within 30 days of the trip","Within three weeks","Within five working days","On the same day"],"a":2,"ex":"Claims that follow the guidelines should be paid within five working days, rather than the current three weeks。新制是五個工作天內付款；three weeks 是目前的情況，30 days 是出差後提出申請的期限，不是付款時間。"},{"q":"What is indicated about the webinar?","o":["It lasts for one hour","It is only for supervisors","It will be held once, on October 1","Attending one session is required"],"a":3,"ex":"Attendance at one of these sessions is compulsory，compulsory 是「強制的、必須的」，所以兩場之中一定要參加一場。研討會長度是 20 分鐘，日期是 9 月 15 日和 17 日，對象是全體業務人員。"}]},
{"id":"r800-04","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Harbor Crest Hotel: Made for Business Travelers","tx":"Harbor Crest Hotel: Made for Business Travelers\n\nLocated five minutes from Lakeside Convention Center, the newly renovated Harbor Crest Hotel offers everything a business traveler needs. Every room has a large desk, reliable high-speed Internet, and a coffee machine. Our amenities include a 24-hour fitness center, an indoor pool, and a business lounge with free printing.\n\nPlanning an event? Our three meeting rooms can accommodate groups of 10 to 120 people, and our onsite catering team will prepare a menu to suit your budget.\n\nExclusive corporate offer: Companies that book ten or more nights before November 30 qualify for a 15 percent discount and a free shuttle service to the airport.\n\nTo obtain an estimate for your group, call our sales representative at 555-0142.","zh":"Harbor Crest Hotel：專為商務旅客打造\n\n全新整修的 Harbor Crest Hotel 距離 Lakeside 會議中心只要五分鐘，商務旅客需要的一切這裡都有。每間客房都有大書桌、穩定的高速網路和咖啡機。飯店設施包括 24 小時健身中心、室內游泳池，以及可免費列印的商務交誼廳。\n\n要辦活動嗎？我們的三間會議室可容納 10 到 120 人的團體，飯店內的外燴團隊也會依照您的預算設計菜單。\n\n企業專屬優惠：凡在 11 月 30 日前預訂十晚以上的公司，即可享有八五折優惠及免費機場接駁服務。\n\n如需為您的團體索取報價，請撥 555-0142 與我們的業務代表聯絡。","w":[686,617,539,711,576,630,631,659],"qs":[{"q":"Who is the advertisement mainly intended for?","o":["Families on vacation","People traveling for work","Hotel employees seeking jobs","Students looking for cheap rooms"],"a":1,"ex":"標題 Made for Business Travelers 和內文 offers everything a business traveler needs 都指出對象是出差的商務旅客，後面還有給公司的 corporate offer。文中沒有提到家庭度假、學生或徵才。"},{"q":"How can a company get the 15 percent discount?","o":["By booking ten or more nights","By joining the fitness center","By paying for the airport shuttle","By holding an event for 120 people"],"a":0,"ex":"Companies that book ten or more nights before November 30 qualify for a 15 percent discount，qualify for 是「符合…的資格」，條件是在 11 月 30 日前訂十晚以上。辦活動、使用健身中心都不是條件；機場接駁是免費贈送的，不用付費。"},{"q":"What is NOT mentioned as a feature of the hotel?","o":["A rooftop restaurant","Meeting rooms","An indoor pool","A fitness center"],"a":0,"ex":"文中提到 a 24-hour fitness center、an indoor pool 和 three meeting rooms，這三項都有。屋頂餐廳完全沒有出現，所以是沒有提到的設施。"}]},
{"id":"r800-05","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"message","ti":"Lunch order for Thursday's seminar","tx":"Mei Tanaka (10:12 A.M.): Hi Robert. I just received the final headcount for Thursday's seminar. It's 64, not 50.\nRobert Diaz (10:14 A.M.): That's a significant increase. Our catering order only covers 50 lunches.\nMei Tanaka (10:15 A.M.): Can the vendor handle 14 more?\nRobert Diaz (10:21 A.M.): I just called them. They can, but they have run out of the chicken dish. They suggested vegetable pasta as a substitute for the additional meals.\nMei Tanaka (10:22 A.M.): That's fine. What about the cost?\nRobert Diaz (10:24 A.M.): The revised estimate is $896, which is still within our budget of $950.\nMei Tanaka (10:25 A.M.): Great. Please go ahead and confirm it. I'll notify the venue that we need more tables.\nRobert Diaz (10:26 A.M.): Will do. I'll forward you the new invoice this afternoon.","zh":"Mei Tanaka（上午 10:12）：嗨，Robert。我剛收到星期四研討會的最終人數，是 64 人，不是 50 人。\nRobert Diaz（上午 10:14）：增加得不少。我們訂的外燴只有 50 份午餐。\nMei Tanaka（上午 10:15）：廠商有辦法多做 14 份嗎？\nRobert Diaz（上午 10:21）：我剛打電話問過了。可以，但雞肉餐點已經沒有了。他們建議多出來的餐點改用蔬菜義大利麵代替。\nMei Tanaka（上午 10:22）：沒問題。費用呢？\nRobert Diaz（上午 10:24）：修改後的報價是 896 美元，還在我們 950 美元的預算內。\nMei Tanaka（上午 10:25）：太好了，請直接跟他們確認。我會通知場地我們需要更多桌子。\nRobert Diaz（上午 10:26）：好的。我下午把新的發票轉寄給你。","w":[569,538,576,540,743,740,725,573],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Ms. Tanaka contact Mr. Diaz?","o":["To report a new number of attendees","To cancel a catering order","To ask for a larger budget","To complain about a vendor's poor service"],"a":0,"ex":"她一開始就說 I just received the final headcount ... It's 64, not 50，headcount 是「人數」，也就是出席人數從 50 變成 64。她沒有取消訂單、沒有抱怨廠商；費用還在預算內，也不需要增加預算。"},{"q":"What will the vendor provide for the additional meals?","o":["A beef sandwich","Vegetable pasta","A chicken dish","A fruit dessert"],"a":1,"ex":"They suggested vegetable pasta as a substitute for the additional meals，substitute 是「替代品」。雞肉餐點已經 run out（沒有了），牛肉三明治和水果甜點文中沒有提到。"},{"q":"What will Ms. Tanaka most likely do next?","o":["Reduce the number of attendees","Send an invoice to Mr. Diaz","Call the catering vendor","Contact the seminar venue"],"a":3,"ex":"她說 I'll notify the venue that we need more tables，notify 是「通知」，所以她接下來會聯絡研討會的場地。向廠商確認訂單和轉寄發票都是 Mr. Diaz 要做的事，文中也沒有要減少人數。"}]},
{"id":"r800-06","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"Maple & Rye to Open Three New Branches","tx":"Maple & Rye to Open Three New Branches\n\nRIVERTON — Maple & Rye, the bakery chain founded in Riverton twelve years ago, announced an ambitious expansion plan on Monday. The company will open three new branches in the neighboring cities of Dalton and Westfield by the end of next year.\n\nFounder Helen Brooks said that revenue has grown for five consecutive years, primarily because of strong demand for the company's whole-grain bread. \"Our customers have been very loyal,\" she remarked. \"This is the right moment to broaden our reach.\"\n\nTo support the new stores, Maple & Rye intends to recruit about 60 employees and relocate its headquarters to a larger building on Canal Street. The current headquarters will be transformed into a training center for new bakers.\n\nThe first of the new branches, in Dalton, is scheduled to open in March.","zh":"Maple & Rye 將新開三家分店\n\nRIVERTON 訊 — 十二年前在 Riverton 創立的連鎖麵包店 Maple & Rye，星期一宣布了一項企圖心十足的擴張計畫。該公司將在明年年底前，於鄰近的 Dalton 和 Westfield 兩個城市新開三家分店。\n\n創辦人 Helen Brooks 表示，公司營收已連續五年成長，主要是因為全穀麵包的需求強勁。她說：「我們的顧客一直非常忠實，現在正是擴大版圖的好時機。」\n\n為了支援新門市，Maple & Rye 打算招募約 60 名員工，並把總部遷到 Canal Street 上一棟更大的建築。現在的總部將改造成新進麵包師傅的訓練中心。\n\n第一家新分店位於 Dalton，預定三月開幕。","w":[623,560,590,625,664,717,566,690],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article mainly about?","o":["A company's plan to grow","A bakery that is closing","A new type of bread","The retirement of a company founder"],"a":0,"ex":"標題 to Open Three New Branches 和第一段 announced an ambitious expansion plan 說明主題是這家公司的擴張計畫，expansion 是「擴張」。全穀麵包只是營收成長的原因，文中沒有提到創辦人退休或關店。"},{"q":"What will happen to the current headquarters?","o":["It will be closed in March","It will become a training center","It will be sold to another company","It will be turned into a new branch"],"a":1,"ex":"The current headquarters will be transformed into a training center for new bakers，transform 是「改造、轉變」，所以現在的總部會變成訓練中心。文中沒有說要賣掉或改成分店，March 是 Dalton 新分店開幕的時間。"},{"q":"What is suggested about Maple & Rye?","o":["Its revenue fell last year","It will stop selling whole-grain bread","It plans to reduce its staff","It has operated for over ten years"],"a":3,"ex":"founded in Riverton twelve years ago 表示公司是十二年前創立的，所以已經營業超過十年。營收是 grown for five consecutive years（連續五年成長），公司要 recruit about 60 employees（招募約 60 人），全穀麵包的需求也很強，其他三項都和文意相反。"}]},
{"id":"r800-07","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"letter","ti":"Your mortgage application","tx":"Northgate Bank\n18 Fulton Street\n\nApril 9\n\nMr. Samuel Reyes\n52 Orchard Lane\n\nDear Mr. Reyes,\n\nWe are pleased to inform you that your mortgage application has been approved. Based on our analysis of your financial records, Northgate Bank can offer you a loan of $240,000 over a span of 20 years.\n\nBefore we can proceed, we need two further documents: a copy of your most recent tax statement and a signed copy of the enclosed agreement. Please read clause 7 carefully, as it specifies the fee for late payments. Monthly installments will be taken automatically from your Northgate checking account on the fifth day of each month.\n\nThis offer is valid until May 9. To clarify any details, please visit your local branch or call our mortgage representative, Ms. Julia Novak, at 555-0178.\n\nSincerely,\nPeter Lang\nLoan Department","zh":"Northgate Bank\nFulton Street 18 號\n\n4 月 9 日\n\nSamuel Reyes 先生\nOrchard Lane 52 號\n\nReyes 先生您好：\n\n很高興通知您，您的房屋貸款申請已經核准。根據我們對您財務紀錄的分析，Northgate Bank 可以提供您 24 萬美元的貸款，還款期間為 20 年。\n\n在進行下一步之前，我們還需要兩份文件：您最近一期的報稅單影本，以及隨信附上的合約簽名本。請仔細閱讀第 7 條，其中載明了逾期付款的費用。每月的分期款項將於每月 5 日自動從您的 Northgate 支票存款帳戶扣款。\n\n本貸款方案的有效期限至 5 月 9 日。如需釐清任何細節，請親臨您附近的分行，或撥 555-0178 與我們的房貸專員 Julia Novak 小姐聯絡。\n\n敬上\nPeter Lang\n貸款部","w":[519,543,644,601,672,586,680,542],"qs":[{"q":"Why was the letter sent?","o":["To report a late payment","To advertise a new branch","To close a checking account","To announce that a loan was approved"],"a":3,"ex":"第一句 your mortgage application has been approved 就是重點，mortgage 是「房屋貸款」，approved 是「核准」。late payments 只是合約第 7 條規定的內容，並不是 Mr. Reyes 遲繳；文中也沒有要關閉帳戶或宣傳新分行。"},{"q":"What must Mr. Reyes provide before the bank can proceed?","o":["A tax statement and a signed agreement","A list of his monthly expenses","A copy of his passport and a recent photo","A letter from his employer"],"a":0,"ex":"we need two further documents: a copy of your most recent tax statement and a signed copy of the enclosed agreement。銀行要的是最近的報稅單和簽好名的合約；護照、每月支出清單、雇主信函都沒有提到。"},{"q":"The word \"span\" in the letter is closest in meaning to","o":["rate","amount","distance","period"],"a":3,"ex":"a loan of $240,000 over a span of 20 years 是指「在 20 年的期間內」還款，這裡的 span 就是 period（一段時間）。distance 是距離、amount 是金額、rate 是利率或比率，在這裡都不通。"}]},
{"id":"r800-08","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"announcement","ti":"Leadership Workshop for New Supervisors","tx":"Leadership Workshop for New Supervisors\n\nThe Personnel Department is pleased to announce a two-day workshop, \"Leading Your Team,\" on May 21 and 22 in Training Room 2 at headquarters.\n\nThe workshop is designed for employees who have been promoted to a supervisory position within the past twelve months. For this group, attendance is compulsory. Other staff members who wish to pursue a management career are also eligible, provided that their manager gives written approval.\n\nTopics include how to delegate tasks, evaluate performance fairly, and resolve disputes between team members. The sessions will be conducted by Angela Moreno, an external consultant who specializes in workplace communication.\n\nBecause the room has a capacity of 24, the remaining places will be allocated in the order that requests are received. To register, e-mail the Personnel Department by May 9.","zh":"新任主管領導力工作坊\n\n人事部很高興宣布，將於 5 月 21 日和 22 日在總部第 2 訓練室舉辦為期兩天的工作坊「帶領你的團隊」。\n\n本工作坊是為過去十二個月內升任主管職的員工所設計，這些人員一律必須參加。其他有志往管理職發展的同仁，只要取得主管的書面同意，也有資格報名。\n\n課程主題包括如何分派工作、公平地評估績效，以及化解團隊成員之間的爭執。課程將由專攻職場溝通的外部顧問 Angela Moreno 主講。\n\n由於教室只能容納 24 人，剩餘名額將依照收到申請的先後順序分配。報名請在 5 月 9 日前寄電子郵件給人事部。","w":[524,610,608,749,679,678,598,729],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the announcement?","o":["To advertise a job opening for a supervisor","To report the results of a staff survey","To introduce a new department head","To give details of a training event"],"a":3,"ex":"開頭 is pleased to announce a two-day workshop，後面說明對象、主題、講師和報名方式，所以目的是公布一場訓練活動的細節。文中沒有介紹新主管、問卷結果或職缺。"},{"q":"What do staff members who are not new supervisors need in order to attend?","o":["An invitation from Ms. Moreno","Written approval from their manager","Twelve months of experience","A certificate in communication"],"a":1,"ex":"Other staff members ... are also eligible, provided that their manager gives written approval，provided that 是「只要、前提是」，所以需要主管的書面同意。twelve months 是指新主管升職的時間；Ms. Moreno 是講師，並不負責邀請；文中沒有提到證書。"},{"q":"What is NOT listed as a workshop topic?","o":["Settling disagreements","Assigning work to others","Judging employees' performance","Preparing a department budget"],"a":3,"ex":"主題是 delegate tasks（分派工作）、evaluate performance fairly（公平評估績效）和 resolve disputes（化解爭執），這三項都有列出。編列部門預算文中沒有提到。"}]},
{"id":"r800-09","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"review","ti":"A durable bag with one weak point","tx":"Product: Trekline Pro 15 Laptop Backpack\nReviewer: Marcus Hall\nRating: 4 out of 5 stars\n\nA durable bag with one weak point\n\nI travel by train every day, so I need a bag that can bear a heavy load. After six months of daily use, my Trekline Pro still looks almost new. The fabric is very strong, and the padded pocket has protected my laptop on numerous crowded journeys. The bag is also compatible with most suitcase handles, which is a tremendous help at airports.\n\nMy only complaint concerns the zipper on the front pocket, which broke after about three months. Because the bag comes with a two-year warranty, I contacted the company. A representative acknowledged the defect immediately and sent me a new bag within a week at no charge.\n\nAt $89, it is not the most economical choice, but the quality and the service justify the price.","zh":"產品：Trekline Pro 15 筆電後背包\n評論者：Marcus Hall\n評分：5 顆星中的 4 顆星\n\n耐用的包包，但有一個弱點\n\n我每天都搭火車，所以需要一個能承受重物的包包。每天使用了六個月之後，我的 Trekline Pro 看起來還是幾乎全新。布料非常堅固，有襯墊的夾層在無數次擁擠的路程中保護了我的筆電。這個包包還能套在大多數行李箱的拉桿上，在機場時幫了大忙。\n\n我唯一不滿意的地方是前袋的拉鍊，用了大約三個月就壞了。因為包包有兩年保固，我就聯絡了公司。客服代表馬上承認這是瑕疵，並在一週內免費寄了一個新包包給我。\n\n售價 89 美元，不算是最划算的選擇，但以它的品質和服務來說，這個價錢很合理。","w":[646,695,571,620,522,703,629,684],"qs":[{"q":"What is the reviewer's overall opinion of the backpack?","o":["It is too heavy to carry on a train every day","It is the cheapest bag available","It is worth the price despite a flaw","It does not protect a laptop well"],"a":2,"ex":"最後一句 the quality and the service justify the price 表示品質和服務讓這個價錢很值得；前面說唯一的缺點（My only complaint）是拉鍊壞掉。他每天搭火車都在用，並沒有嫌它太重；他說這不是 the most economical choice，所以不是最便宜的；包包也 has protected my laptop，有好好保護筆電。"},{"q":"What happened after the reviewer reported the broken zipper?","o":["He paid to have the zipper repaired","He was told the warranty had ended","He received a new bag for free","He was given a refund of $89"],"a":2,"ex":"A representative acknowledged the defect immediately and sent me a new bag within a week at no charge。at no charge 是「免費」，公司在一週內免費寄了新包包給他。不是退款，也不用自費修理，而且包包還在兩年保固期內。"},{"q":"The word \"bear\" in the review is closest in meaning to","o":["avoid","support","measure","reduce"],"a":1,"ex":"a bag that can bear a heavy load 是「能承受很重的東西的包包」，bear 在這裡是「承受、支撐」，意思最接近 support。avoid 是避免、reduce 是減少、measure 是測量。"}]},
{"id":"r800-10","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"form","ti":"Order confirmation CK-30977","tx":"Corwin Kitchen Supply\nORDER CONFIRMATION\n\nOrder number: CK-30977\nOrder date: August 14\nCustomer: Sunrise Café (wholesale account)\nContact: Ms. Priya Nair\n\nItems:\n1 commercial dishwasher, model D-400: $2,150\n2 steel work tables at $190 each: $380\nInstallation service: $120\nTotal: $2,650\n\nPayment: An invoice will be sent after delivery and is due within 30 days.\nEstimated delivery: August 21, between 8:00 A.M. and noon\n\nNotes:\nThe dishwasher is covered by a three-year warranty on all components. Installation will be carried out on the day of delivery by one of our technicians and takes about two hours. Please ensure that a staff member is onsite to sign for the goods. To modify this order, notify us at least 48 hours prior to delivery.","zh":"Corwin Kitchen Supply\n訂單確認單\n\n訂單編號：CK-30977\n訂購日期：8 月 14 日\n客戶：Sunrise Café（批發帳戶）\n聯絡人：Priya Nair 小姐\n\n品項：\n商用洗碗機 D-400 型 1 台：2,150 美元\n鋼製工作桌 2 張，每張 190 美元：380 美元\n安裝服務：120 美元\n合計：2,650 美元\n\n付款方式：發票將於送貨後寄出，請於 30 天內付款。\n預計送貨時間：8 月 21 日上午 8 點至中午 12 點之間\n\n備註：\n洗碗機的所有零件享有三年保固。安裝將於送貨當天由本公司技師進行，大約需要兩小時。請確保現場有員工可以簽收貨品。如需修改訂單，請在送貨前至少 48 小時通知我們。","w":[652,578,573,522,506,702,723,624],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of this document?","o":["To confirm the details of a purchase","To request the repair of a dishwasher","To cancel a delivery","To advertise kitchen equipment"],"a":0,"ex":"標題是 ORDER CONFIRMATION（訂單確認），內容列出訂購品項、金額、付款方式和送貨時間，所以是確認一筆訂購的細節。文中沒有要求維修、打廣告或取消送貨。"},{"q":"What should Sunrise Café make sure of on August 21?","o":["That the invoice has already been paid","That the café is closed all day","That it has hired its own technician","That an employee is there to sign"],"a":3,"ex":"8 月 21 日是預定送貨日，文中說 Please ensure that a staff member is onsite to sign for the goods，也就是要有員工在現場簽收。發票是送貨後才寄出、30 天內付款；安裝由 Corwin 的技師負責，不用自己找人；也沒有要求整天停止營業。"},{"q":"What is indicated about the installation?","o":["It will take place on the delivery day","It is free of charge","It must be done by café staff","It takes about 48 hours"],"a":0,"ex":"Installation will be carried out on the day of delivery by one of our technicians and takes about two hours，所以安裝在送貨當天進行。安裝服務要 120 美元，不是免費；由技師安裝，不是咖啡廳員工；時間大約兩小時，48 hours 是修改訂單要提前通知的時間。"}]},
{"id":"r800-11","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Interview for Operations Analyst position","tx":"To: Jason Kim\nFrom: Olivia Grant, Personnel Department, Vantor Logistics\nSubject: Interview for Operations Analyst position\n\nDear Mr. Kim,\n\nThank you for applying for the position of Operations Analyst. After reviewing more than 80 applications, we have determined that your background meets our criteria, and we would like to invite you to an interview at our headquarters on Tuesday, July 8, at 10:00 A.M.\n\nThe interview will last about one hour. You will meet Mr. Alan Ford, who supervises the distribution team, and you will be asked to analyze a short set of delivery data. No prior preparation is needed for this task.\n\nPlease bring a photo ID and the contact details of two references. If the date is not convenient, let me know by Friday and I will arrange an alternative time.\n\nWe look forward to meeting you.\n\nBest regards,\nOlivia Grant","zh":"收件人：Jason Kim\n寄件人：Olivia Grant，Vantor Logistics 人事部\n主旨：營運分析師職位面試\n\nKim 先生您好：\n\n感謝您應徵營運分析師一職。在審閱超過 80 份申請之後，我們認定您的背景符合我們的標準，因此想邀請您於 7 月 8 日星期二上午 10 點到本公司總部面試。\n\n面試時間大約一小時。您將與負責管理配送團隊的 Alan Ford 先生見面，並且需要分析一小組配送資料。這項作業不需要事先準備。\n\n請攜帶附照片的身分證件，以及兩位推薦人的聯絡資料。如果這個日期不方便，請在星期五之前告訴我，我會另外安排時間。\n\n期待與您見面。\n\n謹致問候\nOlivia Grant","w":[697,505,566,669,504,682,624,525],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Ms. Grant write to Mr. Kim?","o":["To invite him to a job interview","To offer him a position","To ask him to review applications","To tell him his application was rejected"],"a":0,"ex":"we would like to invite you to an interview at our headquarters 說明這封信是邀請他來面試。目前只是面試，還沒有錄取；審閱申請書的是公司，不是他；他的背景 meets our criteria（符合標準），並沒有被拒絕。"},{"q":"What will Mr. Kim be asked to do during the interview?","o":["Examine some delivery data","Tour the distribution center","Give a presentation about his background","Take a written language test"],"a":0,"ex":"you will be asked to analyze a short set of delivery data，analyze 是「分析」，也就是要看一些配送資料並加以分析。做簡報、參觀配送中心、語言筆試文中都沒有提到。"},{"q":"What is suggested about the Operations Analyst position?","o":["Many people applied for it","It is a temporary job","It requires frequent travel","It is based overseas"],"a":0,"ex":"After reviewing more than 80 applications 表示公司收到超過 80 份申請，可見應徵的人很多。海外工作、經常出差、臨時職位在信中都沒有任何線索。"}]},
{"id":"r800-12","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"Scheduled System Maintenance","tx":"IT NOTICE: Scheduled System Maintenance\n\nTo enhance network security, the IT Department will install a major software update this weekend. The work will begin at 10:00 P.M. on Saturday, March 14, and is expected to finish by 6:00 A.M. on Sunday.\n\nDuring this period, e-mail, the shared file server, and the customer database will not be available. Remote login to the company network will also be suspended. The telephone system will not be affected.\n\nPlease save your work and log out before you leave the office on Friday. It may not be possible to retrieve files that are left open during the update.\n\nWe chose these hours to keep downtime to a minimum and to avoid disrupting normal operations. If you detect any problems on Monday morning, notify the help desk at extension 310.","zh":"資訊部公告：系統定期維護\n\n為了加強網路安全，資訊部將於本週末安裝一項重大的軟體更新。作業將於 3 月 14 日星期六晚上 10 點開始，預計在星期日早上 6 點前完成。\n\n在這段期間，電子郵件、共用檔案伺服器和客戶資料庫都無法使用，遠端登入公司網路的功能也會暫停。電話系統不受影響。\n\n星期五離開辦公室之前，請先儲存您的工作並登出。更新期間仍開啟的檔案可能無法救回。\n\n我們選擇這個時段，是為了盡量縮短停機時間，避免打亂正常營運。如果您在星期一早上發現任何問題，請撥分機 310 通知服務台。","w":[708,575,683,735,585,728,685,725],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main purpose of the notice?","o":["To introduce a new e-mail program","To warn staff of a planned system outage","To report a recent security problem","To announce new office hours for the IT Department"],"a":1,"ex":"標題 Scheduled System Maintenance 和內文 e-mail, the shared file server, and the customer database will not be available 說明這是通知員工系統將按計畫暫停服務。文中沒有介紹新的電子郵件程式，也沒有說發生了資安問題或要更改上班時間。"},{"q":"Which service will continue to work during the maintenance?","o":["The telephone system","E-mail","The shared file server","Remote login"],"a":0,"ex":"The telephone system will not be affected，not be affected 是「不受影響」，所以電話系統照常運作。e-mail 和 shared file server 是 will not be available（無法使用），remote login 是 will be suspended（暫停）。"},{"q":"Why did the IT Department choose these hours for the work?","o":["To reduce the cost of the software","To limit the effect on daily business","To allow staff to attend training","To meet a customer's request"],"a":1,"ex":"We chose these hours to keep downtime to a minimum and to avoid disrupting normal operations。downtime 是「停機時間」，disrupt 是「打亂」，選在週末深夜是為了盡量不影響日常營運。軟體費用、員工訓練、客戶要求文中都沒有提到。"}]},
{"id":"r800-13","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"memo","ti":"Fourth-floor renovation","tx":"MEMO\nTo: All fourth-floor staff\nFrom: George Whitman, Facilities Manager\nDate: January 6\nSubject: Fourth-floor renovation\n\nAs announced last month, the renovation of the fourth floor will be carried out in two phases.\n\nPhase 1 (January 20 to February 14): The east side will be closed. The marketing team will relocate temporarily to the conference rooms on the second floor.\n\nPhase 2 (February 17 to March 13): The west side will be closed, and the accounting team will move into the finished east side.\n\nThe old cubicles will be replaced with open desks, and two small meeting rooms will be added. Storage space will be limited during the transition, so please discard any documents you no longer need. Confidential papers must be placed in the locked bins beside the photocopier, not in the regular recycling.\n\nMoving boxes will be distributed on January 15. A detailed timeline is attached.","zh":"備忘錄\n收件人：四樓全體同仁\n寄件人：George Whitman，總務經理\n日期：1 月 6 日\n主旨：四樓整修\n\n如上個月所公告，四樓的整修工程將分兩個階段進行。\n\n第一階段（1 月 20 日至 2 月 14 日）：東側將關閉。行銷團隊將暫時搬到二樓的會議室。\n\n第二階段（2 月 17 日至 3 月 13 日）：西側將關閉，會計團隊將搬進已完工的東側。\n\n舊的辦公隔間將改為開放式辦公桌，並增設兩間小型會議室。過渡期間收納空間有限，請把不再需要的文件丟掉。機密文件必須放進影印機旁上鎖的回收箱，不可丟進一般的資源回收桶。\n\n搬家用的紙箱將於 1 月 15 日發放。詳細時程表如附件。","w":[563,549,717,568,548,701,643,583],"qs":[{"q":"What is the memo mainly about?","o":["The hiring of a facilities manager","A change in company ownership","New rules for booking conference rooms","A plan for remodeling part of an office"],"a":3,"ex":"主旨 Fourth-floor renovation 和第一句 the renovation of the fourth floor will be carried out in two phases 說明主題是四樓辦公室分兩階段整修的計畫，renovation 是「整修」。公司易主、會議室預約規定、招募經理都沒有提到。"},{"q":"Where will the marketing team work during Phase 1?","o":["On the east side of the fourth floor","On the second floor","On the west side of the fourth floor","In a building across the street"],"a":1,"ex":"Phase 1 寫到 The marketing team will relocate temporarily to the conference rooms on the second floor，relocate 是「搬遷」，所以行銷團隊會暫時搬到二樓的會議室。東側在第一階段會關閉，文中也沒有說他們搬到西側或別棟大樓。"},{"q":"The word \"discard\" in the memo is closest in meaning to","o":["put in order","print out","sign","throw away"],"a":3,"ex":"Storage space will be limited ... so please discard any documents you no longer need，因為收納空間有限，不需要的文件請「丟掉」，discard 就是 throw away。print out 是列印出來、put in order 是整理好、sign 是簽名。"}]},
{"id":"r800-14","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Now Hiring: Sales Associate","tx":"NOW HIRING: Sales Associate\nDelmar Home Furnishings\n\nDelmar Home Furnishings, a family-owned corporation with 14 stores, is recruiting a full-time Sales Associate for its Kingsport branch.\n\nResponsibilities:\n- Help customers choose furniture that fits their needs and budget\n- Process transactions and arrange deliveries\n- Check showroom inventory every week\n\nRequirements:\n- An enthusiastic and reliable personality\n- Availability to work two Saturdays per month\n- Prior retail experience is beneficial but not essential. All new staff receive a one-week orientation.\n\nWe offer a competitive salary plus commission on every sale, as well as paid vacation and a staff discount. Associates become eligible for health insurance coverage after three months.\n\nTo apply, send your résumé and the names of two references to our Personnel Department by October 31.","zh":"徵才：銷售人員\nDelmar Home Furnishings\n\nDelmar Home Furnishings 是一家擁有 14 家門市的家族企業，現正為 Kingsport 分店招募一名全職銷售人員。\n\n工作內容：\n- 協助顧客挑選符合需求和預算的家具\n- 處理交易並安排送貨\n- 每週清點展示間的庫存\n\n應徵條件：\n- 個性熱忱、可靠\n- 每個月可配合兩個星期六上班\n- 有零售業經驗者佳，但並非必要。所有新進員工都會接受為期一週的新進人員訓練。\n\n我們提供具競爭力的薪資，每筆銷售另有佣金，並享有有薪假和員工折扣。到職滿三個月後即可享有健康保險。\n\n意者請於 10 月 31 日前，將履歷及兩位推薦人的姓名寄至本公司人事部。","w":[559,664,507,632,633,516,530,608],"qs":[{"q":"What position is being advertised?","o":["A furniture designer","A store manager","A delivery driver","A salesperson at a furniture store"],"a":3,"ex":"標題 Sales Associate 是「銷售人員」，工作內容第一項是 Help customers choose furniture，所以是家具店的銷售人員。arrange deliveries 只是安排送貨，不是當司機；文中也不是徵店長或設計師。"},{"q":"What is stated about previous retail experience?","o":["It is helpful but not required","It replaces the orientation","It is required for all applicants","It must be at least one year long"],"a":0,"ex":"Prior retail experience is beneficial but not essential，beneficial 是「有幫助的」，not essential 是「不是必要的」，所以有經驗更好，但沒有也可以應徵。文中沒有規定年資，而且 All new staff 都要參加一週的 orientation（新進人員訓練）。"},{"q":"What is NOT mentioned as a benefit of the job?","o":["A discount for staff","A company car","Paid vacation","Commission on sales"],"a":1,"ex":"文中提到 commission on every sale（銷售佣金）、paid vacation（有薪假）和 a staff discount（員工折扣），這三項都有。公司配車沒有提到。"}]},
{"id":"r800-15","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"message","ti":"Flight delay and the Ellis meeting","tx":"Nina Petrov (2:05 P.M.): Bad news, Tom. My flight to Denver has been delayed three hours because of a safety inspection. I won't reach the client's office before 6:00.\nTom Becker (2:08 P.M.): That's a problem. The contract review with Ellis Corporation is at 4:30.\nNina Petrov (2:09 P.M.): Could you conduct the meeting without me? You know the proposal as well as I do.\nTom Becker (2:12 P.M.): I can outline the pricing, but they will want you to clarify the warranty clause. What if I ask them to move the meeting to tomorrow morning?\nNina Petrov (2:13 P.M.): Good idea. I'm free until 11:00.\nTom Becker (2:25 P.M.): Done. Their representative agreed to 9:00 A.M. tomorrow. She says that time actually suits them better.\nNina Petrov (2:26 P.M.): I'm so relieved. Thanks for resolving that so quickly.","zh":"Nina Petrov（下午 2:05）：Tom，壞消息。我飛往丹佛的班機因為安全檢查延誤了三個小時，6 點以前到不了客戶的辦公室。\nTom Becker（下午 2:08）：這下麻煩了。和 Ellis Corporation 的合約審閱會議是 4 點半。\nNina Petrov（下午 2:09）：你可以自己主持會議嗎？這份提案你跟我一樣熟。\nTom Becker（下午 2:12）：價格的部分我可以大致說明，但他們會希望由你來把保固條款講清楚。我請他們把會議改到明天早上怎麼樣？\nNina Petrov（下午 2:13）：好主意。我 11 點以前都有空。\nTom Becker（下午 2:25）：搞定了。對方的代表同意改到明天早上 9 點。她說那個時間其實對他們更方便。\nNina Petrov（下午 2:26）：我鬆了一口氣。謝謝你這麼快就解決了。","w":[738,710,602,671,522,586,722,678],"qs":[{"q":"What problem does Ms. Petrov report?","o":["She lost a contract","Her flight is behind schedule","A client rejected a proposal","Her hotel reservation was canceled"],"a":1,"ex":"My flight to Denver has been delayed three hours，delayed 是「延誤」，也就是她的班機比原定時間晚了三個小時。合約還要開會審閱，並沒有丟掉；飯店訂房和客戶拒絕提案都沒有提到。"},{"q":"When will the meeting with Ellis Corporation now take place?","o":["At 4:30 P.M. today","At 6:00 P.M. today","At 9:00 A.M. tomorrow","At 11:00 A.M. tomorrow"],"a":2,"ex":"Their representative agreed to 9:00 A.M. tomorrow，對方代表同意改到明天早上 9 點。4:30 是原本的開會時間，6:00 是她最快能到的時間，11:00 是她明天有空到幾點。"},{"q":"Why does Mr. Becker suggest changing the meeting time?","o":["He is unable to describe the pricing","He has another meeting at 4:30","The client will want Ms. Petrov to explain a clause","He has not had enough time to read the whole proposal"],"a":2,"ex":"他說 they will want you to clarify the warranty clause，clarify 是「說明清楚」，clause 是「條款」，客戶會希望由 Ms. Petrov 親自說明保固條款，所以他提議改時間。Ms. Petrov 說 You know the proposal as well as I do，他自己也說 I can outline the pricing，所以其他說法都不對。"}]},
{"id":"r800-16","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"Factory Cuts Electricity Use by a Fifth","tx":"Factory Cuts Electricity Use by a Fifth\n\nGREENFIELD — Halden Plastics, which manufactures food containers, has reduced its electricity consumption by 20 percent in one year, the company revealed on Tuesday.\n\nThe savings came from three measures. First, the firm replaced its old lighting with LED lamps. Second, it installed sensors that monitor each machine and switch it off automatically when it is not in use. Finally, solar panels on the roof now generate about a tenth of the plant's power.\n\nOperations manager Rita Collins acknowledged that the initial investment of $400,000 was significant. \"It was hard to justify at first,\" she said, \"but the project will pay for itself in four years.\"\n\nHalden intends to implement the same strategy at its second plant next spring. Ms. Collins added that greater efficiency has also enhanced the company's reputation among its customers.","zh":"工廠用電量減少五分之一\n\nGREENFIELD 訊 — 生產食品容器的 Halden Plastics 星期二透露，該公司在一年內把用電量減少了 20%。\n\n節省下來的電力來自三項措施。第一，公司把舊的照明設備換成 LED 燈。第二，安裝感應器監控每一台機器，機器沒有使用時會自動關閉。最後，屋頂上的太陽能板現在可以產生工廠大約十分之一的電力。\n\n營運經理 Rita Collins 坦承，40 萬美元的初期投資金額相當可觀。她說：「一開始很難說明這筆錢為什麼值得花，但這項計畫四年就能回本。」\n\nHalden 打算明年春天在第二座工廠實施同樣的策略。Collins 女士還說，效率提升也提高了公司在顧客心中的聲譽。","w":[739,535,687,599,736,668,684,676],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article mainly about?","o":["The opening of a new factory","A rise in the price of plastic containers","A shortage of solar panels","A company's cut in electricity use"],"a":3,"ex":"標題 Factory Cuts Electricity Use by a Fifth 和第一段 has reduced its electricity consumption by 20 percent 說明主題是這家公司成功減少用電，consumption 是「消耗量」。塑膠漲價和太陽能板短缺都沒提到；公司只是要在現有的第二座工廠採用同樣做法，並不是新開工廠。"},{"q":"How much of the plant's power comes from the solar panels?","o":["About one-half","About one-fifth","About one-tenth","Nearly all of it"],"a":2,"ex":"solar panels on the roof now generate about a tenth of the plant's power，a tenth 是「十分之一」。a fifth（五分之一，也就是 20%）是整體用電量減少的幅度，不是太陽能板的發電比例。"},{"q":"What is NOT one of the measures the company took?","o":["Buying new production machines","Installing sensors on machines","Changing the lighting","Adding solar panels"],"a":0,"ex":"三項措施是 replaced its old lighting with LED lamps（更換燈具）、installed sensors that monitor each machine（安裝感應器）和 solar panels on the roof（屋頂太陽能板）。文中沒有說公司購買新的生產機器。"}]},
{"id":"r800-17","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"letter","ti":"Replacement for your AirPure 200","tx":"Solvane Appliances\nCustomer Care Department\n\nNovember 3\n\nMs. Grace Huang\n77 Cedar Avenue\n\nDear Ms. Huang,\n\nThank you for returning your Solvane AirPure 200 air purifier to us. Our technicians have completed their inspection and determined that the fan motor was defective when it left the factory. We sincerely apologize.\n\nAs your purchase is still under warranty, you will not bear any cost. Unfortunately, the AirPure 200 is no longer manufactured, so we cannot send you an identical unit. As a substitute, we will ship you the AirPure 300, a newer model of equivalent size with a quieter motor. It should reach you within five business days.\n\nTo compensate you for the inconvenience, we have enclosed a voucher for two free filters, which can be redeemed at any Solvane store.\n\nSincerely,\nVictor Almeida\nCustomer Care Manager","zh":"Solvane Appliances\n客戶服務部\n\n11 月 3 日\n\nGrace Huang 小姐\nCedar Avenue 77 號\n\n黃小姐您好：\n\n感謝您將 Solvane AirPure 200 空氣清淨機寄回給我們。我們的技術人員已完成檢查，確定風扇馬達在出廠時就有瑕疵。我們誠摯地向您致歉。\n\n由於您購買的產品仍在保固期內，您不需要負擔任何費用。可惜 AirPure 200 已經停產，我們無法寄給您一模一樣的機型。作為替代，我們會寄給您 AirPure 300，這是比較新的機型，大小相同，馬達更安靜。應該會在五個工作天內送達。\n\n為了補償造成您的不便，我們隨信附上一張可兌換兩個免費濾網的兌換券，在任何一家 Solvane 門市都可以兌換。\n\n敬上\nVictor Almeida\n客戶服務部經理","w":[697,616,522,695,743,651,674,693],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the letter?","o":["To promote a new line of filters","To explain how a problem will be fixed","To refuse a warranty claim","To ask a customer to send back a broken item"],"a":1,"ex":"信中先說明檢查結果 the fan motor was defective（風扇馬達有瑕疵），再說 we will ship you the AirPure 300，所以目的是說明公司會怎麼處理這個產品問題。顧客已經把商品寄回了；濾網兌換券只是補償；產品 still under warranty，保固並沒有被拒絕。"},{"q":"Why will Ms. Huang receive a different model?","o":["She asked for a quieter machine","Her warranty has expired","The original model is no longer made","The newer model costs less"],"a":2,"ex":"the AirPure 200 is no longer manufactured, so we cannot send you an identical unit，manufacture 是「製造」，原本的型號已經停產，所以改寄 AirPure 300。信中沒有說她要求換機型，保固也還有效（still under warranty），文中更沒有比較價格。"},{"q":"What is suggested about the AirPure 300?","o":["Ms. Huang must pay extra for it","It is much larger than the AirPure 200","It is quieter than the AirPure 200","It will arrive the next day"],"a":2,"ex":"a newer model of equivalent size with a quieter motor，quieter 是「比較安靜」，所以新機型的噪音比較小。equivalent size 表示大小相同；you will not bear any cost 表示不用付任何費用；送達時間是 within five business days，不是隔天。"}]},
{"id":"r800-18","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"announcement","ti":"Lakeshore Small Business Expo: Call for Vendors","tx":"Lakeshore Small Business Expo: Call for Vendors\n\nThe Lakeshore Business Association will hold its tenth annual Small Business Expo on Saturday, September 19, at Pier Hall. Last year's event attracted more than 3,000 visitors, and we expect an even larger crowd this year thanks to a publicity campaign on local radio.\n\nLocal vendors are invited to reserve a booth to display their products and distribute samples. A booth costs $150, which includes a table, two chairs, electricity, and a listing in the printed event directory. Because space is limited to 80 booths, applications will be accepted in the order they arrive.\n\nNew this year: three free seminars on topics such as online marketing and financial planning.\n\nTo apply, submit the form on our website with your payment by August 15. No refunds will be granted after September 1.","zh":"Lakeshore 小型企業博覽會：攤商招募\n\nLakeshore 商業協會將於 9 月 19 日星期六在 Pier Hall 舉辦第十屆年度小型企業博覽會。去年的活動吸引了超過 3,000 名訪客，今年由於在地方電台進行宣傳活動，我們預期人潮會更多。\n\n歡迎在地商家預訂攤位，展示產品並發送試用品。每個攤位 150 美元，包含一張桌子、兩張椅子、電力，以及在活動紙本名錄上刊登資訊。由於場地僅能容納 80 個攤位，將依照申請送達的先後順序受理。\n\n今年新增：三場免費研討會，主題包括網路行銷和財務規劃等。\n\n報名請於 8 月 15 日前，在我們的網站上提交表單並完成付款。9 月 1 日之後恕不退費。","w":[540,512,577,720,584,538,644,737],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the announcement?","o":["To report a change of venue","To invite businesses to join an event","To find speakers for seminars","To thank visitors who came last year"],"a":1,"ex":"標題 Call for Vendors 是「徵求攤商」，內文說 Local vendors are invited to reserve a booth，目的是邀請商家報名參加博覽會。文中沒有感謝去年的訪客、徵求講師或更換場地。"},{"q":"What is included in the booth fee?","o":["A listing in the event directory","A parking space","Lunch for two people at the booth","Advertising on local radio"],"a":0,"ex":"A booth costs $150, which includes a table, two chairs, electricity, and a listing in the printed event directory。directory 是「名錄」，攤位費包含在活動名錄上刊登資訊。電台宣傳是主辦單位為整個活動做的，停車位和午餐都沒有提到。"},{"q":"What is suggested about booth applications?","o":["They must include product samples","They are accepted until the day of the expo, September 19","They cost nothing before August 15","Early applicants are more likely to get a booth"],"a":3,"ex":"Because space is limited to 80 booths, applications will be accepted in the order they arrive。攤位只有 80 個，而且按照送達的先後順序受理，所以越早申請越有機會。申請期限是 August 15；samples 是在攤位上發給訪客的，不是申請時要附的；攤位費一律是 150 美元。"}]},
{"id":"r800-19","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"review","ti":"Venue Review: Elmwood Conference Center","tx":"Venue Review: Elmwood Conference Center\nPosted by: Sandra Kowalski, Event Coordinator\nRating: 3 out of 5\n\nWe held our annual sales seminar at Elmwood last month for 150 employees. The main hall was spacious and well equipped, and the onsite technician resolved a projector problem within minutes. The catering was excellent too. The lunch buffet offered numerous choices, and nothing ran out.\n\nHowever, there were two significant problems. Parking was insufficient. The lot has only 60 spaces, so many of our staff had to park several blocks away. In addition, the air conditioning in the smaller workshop rooms was not adequate for a hot afternoon, and several participants complained.\n\nThe manager apologized and deducted 10 percent from our invoice, which I appreciated. I would consider Elmwood again for a smaller group, but it is not suitable for an event of our scale.","zh":"場地評論：Elmwood Conference Center\n發文者：Sandra Kowalski，活動統籌\n評分：5 分中的 3 分\n\n上個月我們在 Elmwood 為 150 名員工舉辦了年度業務研討會。主廳寬敞、設備齊全，駐場的技術人員幾分鐘內就解決了投影機的問題。外燴也很出色，午餐自助餐的選擇很多，而且沒有任何一道菜不夠。\n\n不過，有兩個重大的問題。停車位不足，停車場只有 60 個車位，所以我們很多同仁必須把車停在好幾個街區之外。此外，較小的幾間研習教室冷氣不夠強，應付不了炎熱的下午，有好幾位參加者抱怨。\n\n經理向我們道歉，並從發票金額中扣除了 10%，這一點我很感謝。如果是人數比較少的團體，我會考慮再選 Elmwood，但它並不適合我們這種規模的活動。","w":[655,678,576,612,636,613,691,527],"qs":[{"q":"What does the reviewer conclude about the venue?","o":["It is ideal for large companies","It should change its catering company","It is better suited to smaller events","It charges too much for parking"],"a":2,"ex":"最後一句 I would consider Elmwood again for a smaller group, but it is not suitable for an event of our scale，scale 是「規模」，她認為這個場地比較適合小型活動。外燴她很滿意（excellent）；停車的問題是車位不夠，不是收費太貴。"},{"q":"What problem did the group have with parking?","o":["The fee was too high","The entrance was hard to find","There were too few spaces","The lot was closed for repairs"],"a":2,"ex":"Parking was insufficient. The lot has only 60 spaces，insufficient 是「不足的」，150 人參加卻只有 60 個車位，所以是車位太少。收費、整修、入口難找文中都沒有提到。"},{"q":"What does the reviewer NOT praise?","o":["The main hall","The food","The technical support","The air conditioning"],"a":3,"ex":"她稱讚了 main hall（spacious and well equipped）、catering（excellent）和 onsite technician（幾分鐘內解決投影機問題）。冷氣則是 not adequate for a hot afternoon，adequate 是「足夠的」，這是她抱怨的地方。"}]},
{"id":"r800-20","lv":800,"p":7,"k":"form","ti":"Staff Development Day: Schedule","tx":"Northfield Retail Group\nStaff Development Day: Schedule\nFriday, October 9, Head Office, Room 3\n\n8:30 Registration and coffee\n9:00 Overview of this year's results (Diane Foster, Operations Director)\n9:30 Workshop: Resolving customer disputes (Paul Jensen)\n11:00 Break\n11:15 Seminar: Our online sales strategy (Maria Santos)\n12:30 Lunch (catering provided)\n1:30 Workshop: Keeping accurate inventory records (Paul Jensen)\n3:00 Closing remarks (Diane Foster)\n\nNotes:\nAttendance is mandatory for all branch managers. Assistant managers are welcome to attend if their branch has adequate staff coverage on that day. If you have special meal requirements, please notify Ms. Foster's office by October 2. Handouts will be distributed at registration. Parking is available behind the building, but spaces are limited, so please share a car if possible.","zh":"Northfield Retail Group\n員工進修日：議程表\n10 月 9 日星期五，總公司 3 號會議室\n\n8:30 報到及咖啡時間\n9:00 本年度業績概述（營運總監 Diane Foster）\n9:30 工作坊：化解顧客糾紛（Paul Jensen）\n11:00 休息\n11:15 研討會：我們的線上銷售策略（Maria Santos）\n12:30 午餐（提供外燴）\n1:30 工作坊：維持正確的庫存紀錄（Paul Jensen）\n3:00 結語（Diane Foster）\n\n備註：\n所有分店經理都必須出席。副理若所屬分店當天人手充足，也歡迎參加。如有特殊餐點需求，請於 10 月 2 日前通知 Foster 女士的辦公室。講義將在報到時發放。大樓後方可以停車，但車位有限，請盡量共乘。","w":[567,598,534,642,587,639,613,515],"qs":[{"q":"What kind of document is this?","o":["A program for a training day","A list of job openings","A report on sales results","A menu for a company lunch"],"a":0,"ex":"標題 Staff Development Day: Schedule 加上各時段的 Workshop、Seminar，可以知道這是員工訓練日的議程表。午餐只是其中一個時段，不是菜單；文中沒有職缺，也不是業績報告。"},{"q":"Who will lead the session on inventory records?","o":["Maria Santos","Paul Jensen","Diane Foster","A branch manager"],"a":1,"ex":"1:30 那一行是 Workshop: Keeping accurate inventory records (Paul Jensen)，inventory 是「庫存」，所以由 Paul Jensen 主講。Diane Foster 負責開場的概述和結語，Maria Santos 講的是線上銷售策略。"},{"q":"What is suggested about assistant managers?","o":["They must bring their own lunch","They will lead a workshop","They can come if their store has enough staff","They are required to attend both workshops and the seminar"],"a":2,"ex":"Assistant managers are welcome to attend if their branch has adequate staff coverage on that day，adequate 是「足夠的」，coverage 在這裡指「有人顧店」，也就是分店當天人手夠才可以來。必須參加（mandatory）的是 branch managers；工作坊由 Paul Jensen 主講；午餐有提供外燴。"}]},
{"id":"r800-21","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"email","ti":"Your subscription ends soon","tx":"To: Henry Clark\nFrom: Member Services, Business Insight Weekly\nSubject: Your subscription ends soon\nCustomer number: 20417\n\nDear Mr. Clark,\n\nYour subscription to Business Insight Weekly will end on June 30. To continue receiving the publication without interruption, please [1] ------- your subscription before that date.\n\nAs a loyal reader, you are [2] ------- for an exclusive rate of $79 per year, a saving of 20 percent on the regular price. You will also keep full access to our online library, which contains more than ten years of articles and market analysis.\n\nThe process is simple. Visit our website, enter the customer number shown above, and choose a payment method. [3] -------, you may call a customer representative at 555-0199 on weekdays between 9:00 A.M. and 5:00 P.M.\n\nThank you for your continued support.\n\nMember Services","zh":"收件人：Henry Clark\n寄件人：Business Insight Weekly 會員服務部\n主旨：您的訂閱即將到期\n客戶編號：20417\n\nClark 先生您好：\n\n您訂閱的 Business Insight Weekly 將於 6 月 30 日到期。為了讓您不間斷地收到本刊，請在該日期之前續訂。\n\n身為忠實讀者，您有資格享有每年 79 美元的專屬優惠價，比原價省下 20%。您也可以繼續完整使用我們的線上資料庫，裡面收錄了十多年來的文章和市場分析。\n\n手續很簡單：請上我們的網站，輸入上方所示的客戶編號，再選擇付款方式即可。或者，您也可以在週一至週五上午 9 點至下午 5 點之間，撥 555-0199 與客服代表聯絡。\n\n感謝您長期的支持。\n\n會員服務部","w":[565,724,608,630,543,511],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["renew","duplicate","suspend","decline"],"a":0,"ex":"訂閱 6 月 30 日到期，想要繼續收到刊物（To continue receiving the publication）就要「續訂」，renew a subscription 是固定搭配。suspend 是暫停、decline 是拒絕、duplicate 是複製，都和「繼續收到」的意思不合。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["capable","available","eligible","mandatory"],"a":2,"ex":"be eligible for 是「有資格享有…」，忠實讀者有資格享有專屬優惠價。capable 是「有能力的」，後面要接 of；available 是「可取得的、有空的」，不能用來說人有資格享受優惠；mandatory 是「強制的」，意思不通。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Alternatively","Nevertheless","Therefore","For example"],"a":0,"ex":"前一句說可以上網站辦理，這一句說也可以打電話，是兩種方式二選一，所以用 Alternatively（或者、另一個方法是）。Therefore 是因此、For example 是舉例來說、Nevertheless 是儘管如此，都接不上前後文。"}]},
{"id":"r800-22","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"notice","ti":"Parking Lot B closed August 3 to 7","tx":"NOTICE: Parking Lot B Closed August 3 to 7\nPosted July 27\n\nParking Lot B, behind the main building, [1] ------- from Monday, August 3, to Friday, August 7, while the surface is repaired and new lines are painted. For safety reasons, entry to the area will be restricted to the construction personnel.\n\nDuring this period, employees who normally use Lot B should park in Lot D on Franklin Street. A free shuttle bus will run between Lot D and the main entrance every fifteen minutes from 7:00 A.M. to 7:00 P.M. [2] -------\n\nPlease ensure that your vehicle is moved by 8:00 P.M. on Sunday, August 2. Any vehicles remaining after that time will be removed at the owner's expense.\n\nWe apologize for the [3] ------- and thank you for your cooperation. For further information, call extension 250.\n\nFacilities Department","zh":"公告：B 停車場 8 月 3 日至 7 日關閉\n公告日期：7 月 27 日\n\n主大樓後方的 B 停車場將於 8 月 3 日星期一至 8 月 7 日星期五關閉，以便修補路面並重新劃線。基於安全考量，該區域僅限施工人員進入。\n\n在這段期間，平常使用 B 停車場的員工請改停 Franklin Street 上的 D 停車場。免費接駁車將於上午 7 點至晚上 7 點之間，每十五分鐘一班，往返 D 停車場和大門口。或者，從 D 停車場走路過來大約十分鐘。\n\n請確保在 8 月 2 日星期日晚上 8 點前把車移走。逾時仍未移走的車輛將予以拖吊，費用由車主負擔。\n\n造成不便，敬請見諒，並感謝您的配合。如需進一步資訊，請撥分機 250。\n\n總務部","w":[670,528,702,580,653],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["has been closed","was closing","will be closed","closing"],"a":2,"ex":"公告日期是 July 27，停車場關閉是 8 月 3 日到 7 日，是未來的事，而且停車場是「被關閉」，所以用未來式被動 will be closed。has been closed 是現在完成式，表示已經關閉；was closing 是過去進行式；closing 不能單獨當句子的動詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["As a result, Lot D will also be closed that week.","Therefore, employees must pay the bus fare in cash.","Thank you for attending the opening ceremony.","Alternatively, the walk from Lot D takes about ten minutes."],"a":3,"ex":"前一句介紹了免費接駁車，接著補充另一個選擇「或者，從 Lot D 走路過來大約十分鐘」最通順。Lot D 是這一週的替代停車場，不可能也關閉；接駁車是 free（免費），不用付車資；文中沒有任何開幕典禮。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["precaution","inconvenience","compensation","circumstance"],"a":1,"ex":"We apologize for the inconvenience 是公告和信件裡常見的句子，意思是「造成不便，敬請見諒」。precaution 是預防措施、compensation 是補償、circumstance 是情況，都不是需要道歉的事。"}]},
{"id":"r800-23","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"memo","ti":"Annual performance reviews","tx":"MEMO\nTo: All department managers\nFrom: Susan Miller, Personnel Director\nSubject: Annual performance reviews\n\nThis year's performance reviews will be [1] ------- between November 2 and November 20. Each manager is expected to meet individually with every member of his or her team for about 45 minutes.\n\nBefore the meeting, ask each employee to complete the self-evaluation form, which is available on the company intranet. During the meeting, discuss the past year's results and agree on three [2] ------- objectives for next year, such as a sales figure or a completion date. Goals that are too general are difficult to measure.\n\nAll completed forms must reach my office by November 27. [3] ------- salary increases are based on these reviews, late forms may delay the changes to your team's pay.\n\nThank you for your cooperation.","zh":"備忘錄\n收件人：各部門經理\n寄件人：Susan Miller，人事總監\n主旨：年度績效考核\n\n今年的績效考核將於 11 月 2 日至 11 月 20 日之間進行。每位經理都應該和團隊的每一位成員個別面談，每次大約 45 分鐘。\n\n面談之前，請每位員工先填寫自我評量表，表單可在公司內部網路取得。面談時，請討論過去一年的成果，並共同訂出明年的三個具體目標，例如業績數字或完成日期。太籠統的目標很難衡量。\n\n所有填妥的表單必須在 11 月 27 日前送達我的辦公室。由於調薪是以這些考核為依據，表單遲交可能會延誤貴團隊的薪資調整。\n\n感謝您的配合。","w":[528,738,710,645,541,599],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["conducted","consulted","conveyed","consumed"],"a":0,"ex":"conduct a review 是「進行考核」，被動就是 reviews will be conducted。consumed 是消耗、conveyed 是傳達、consulted 是請教或查閱，都不能和「績效考核」搭配表示「舉行」。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["concrete","artificial","defective","overdue"],"a":0,"ex":"後面舉的例子是 a sales figure or a completion date（業績數字或完成日期），而且說 too general（太籠統）的目標很難衡量，所以要訂「具體的」目標，concrete objectives。artificial 是人造的、defective 是有瑕疵的、overdue 是逾期的。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Although","Whether","Because","Unless"],"a":2,"ex":"前半句「調薪是根據這些考核」是原因，後半句「表單遲交可能延誤調薪」是結果，所以用表示原因的 Because。Although 是雖然、Unless 是除非、Whether 是是否，邏輯都不對。"}]},
{"id":"r800-24","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"letter","ti":"Grant for the Riverside Youth Music Program","tx":"Clearwater Community Foundation\n45 Bridge Street\n\nFebruary 10\n\nMs. Elena Vargas\nDirector, Riverside Youth Music Program\n\nDear Ms. Vargas,\n\nOn behalf of the Clearwater Community Foundation, I am delighted to inform you that your program [1] ------- a grant of $15,000 for the coming year.\n\nOur committee received 62 applications and evaluated each one against strict criteria. Your proposal stood out because of its clear budget and its strong [2] ------- to offering free lessons to local children.\n\nThe funds will be transferred in two installments, in March and September. [3] ------- the second payment, we ask that you submit a short report by August 15 describing how the first half of the grant was used.\n\nCongratulations. We look forward to hearing about your progress.\n\nSincerely,\nThomas Reed\nChair, Grants Committee","zh":"Clearwater Community Foundation\nBridge Street 45 號\n\n2 月 10 日\n\nElena Vargas 女士\nRiverside Youth Music Program 主任\n\nVargas 女士您好：\n\n謹代表 Clearwater Community Foundation 很高興地通知您，貴計畫已獲得下一年度 15,000 美元的補助金。\n\n本會委員會共收到 62 份申請，並依照嚴格的標準逐一評估。您的提案之所以脫穎而出，是因為預算清楚，而且對於為在地兒童提供免費課程有很深的投入。\n\n補助款將分兩期撥付，分別在三月和九月。在撥付第二期款項之前，請您於 8 月 15 日前提交一份簡短的報告，說明前半筆補助金的使用情形。\n\n恭喜您。期待聽到您的進展。\n\n敬上\nThomas Reed\n補助委員會主席","w":[508,737,679,505,500,542,624],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["awarding","has been awarded","has awarded","will award"],"a":1,"ex":"主詞 your program 是「獲得」補助金的一方，所以要用被動語態 has been awarded a grant（獲頒補助金）。has awarded 和 will award 是主動，意思會變成貴計畫頒發補助金給別人；awarding 不能單獨當句子的動詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["commit","committed","commitment","commits"],"a":2,"ex":"空格前面有所有格 its 和形容詞 strong，所以要放名詞；commitment to + V-ing 是「對…的投入、承諾」。commit 和 commits 是動詞，committed 是過去分詞或形容詞，都不能放在形容詞 strong 後面當名詞用。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["In spite of","According to","As a result of","Prior to"],"a":3,"ex":"第二期款項在九月撥付，報告要在 8 月 15 日前交，也就是在第二次付款「之前」，所以用 Prior to（在…之前）。In spite of 是儘管、According to 是根據、As a result of 是由於，意思都不通。"}]},
{"id":"r800-25","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Bennett & Shaw Accounting","tx":"Bennett & Shaw Accounting: Let Us Handle the Numbers\n\nRunning a small business leaves little time for paperwork. If you are looking for a reliable partner, Bennett & Shaw can help. Our firm [1] ------- in accounting services for companies with fewer than 50 employees, from restaurants to design studios.\n\nOur team will prepare your invoices, process your payroll, and produce clear financial reports every month. Every client is assigned a [2] ------- accountant, so you will always speak with someone who knows your business well.\n\nOur fees are fixed and agreed in advance. [3] ------- That means no surprises when our invoice arrives.\n\nCall 555-0164 today to arrange a free one-hour meeting, or visit one of our three branches downtown.","zh":"Bennett & Shaw Accounting：數字的事交給我們\n\n經營小公司，實在沒有多少時間處理文書作業。如果您正在找一個可靠的夥伴，Bennett & Shaw 可以幫上忙。本事務所專門為員工少於 50 人的公司提供會計服務，客戶從餐廳到設計工作室都有。\n\n我們的團隊會為您開立發票、處理薪資，並且每個月製作清楚的財務報表。每位客戶都有一位專屬的會計師，所以您每次聯絡的都是熟悉貴公司業務的人。\n\n我們的收費固定，並且事先談定。絕不會另外收取超時費用。這表示您收到我們的帳單時不會有任何意外。\n\n今天就撥 555-0164 預約一小時的免費會談，或親臨我們在市中心的三家分所。","w":[617,661,573,644,635,582],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["provides","specializes","generates","supervises"],"a":1,"ex":"specialize in 是「專門從事、專精於」，空格後面有 in，只有 specializes 能接。provides（提供）、supervises（監督）、generates（產生）都是直接接受詞，後面不會加 in。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["compulsory","temporary","consecutive","dedicated"],"a":3,"ex":"a dedicated accountant 是「專屬的會計師」，所以客戶每次都能和了解自己公司的同一個人聯絡。temporary 是臨時的，和後面的 always 矛盾；consecutive 是連續的、compulsory 是強制的，都不能用來形容會計師。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Our office is closed on public holidays.","You will never be charged for extra hours.","We are currently recruiting two junior accountants.","Prices may change at any time without notice."],"a":1,"ex":"前一句說費用固定並且事先談好，後一句說收到帳單不會有意外，中間放「絕不會另外收取超時費用」最連貫。價格隨時變動和 fixed 互相矛盾；假日休息和徵人都和收費無關，接不上 That means no surprises。"}]},
{"id":"r800-26","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"announcement","ti":"Orbis Freight Appoints New Managing Director","tx":"Orbis Freight Appoints New Managing Director\n\nOrbis Freight announced today that Laura Jennings will [1] ------- the role of managing director on January 1. She replaces Richard Dunn, who is retiring after 22 years with the corporation.\n\nMs. Jennings joined Orbis eight years ago as a regional sales manager and [2] ------- the company's European operations since 2021. Under her leadership, revenue in that region has risen by 35 percent.\n\n\"Laura understands both our customers and our personnel,\" said Mr. Dunn. \"I am confident that the company will continue to thrive.\"\n\nIn her new role, Ms. Jennings intends to place greater [3] ------- on digital tracking services, which allow clients to follow their shipments at every stage of the journey.\n\nMs. Jennings will address employees at the headquarters on January 4.","zh":"Orbis Freight 任命新任總經理\n\nOrbis Freight 今天宣布，Laura Jennings 將於 1 月 1 日接任總經理一職。她接替的是 Richard Dunn，他在公司服務 22 年後即將退休。\n\nJennings 女士八年前加入 Orbis，擔任區域業務經理，並自 2021 年起掌管公司的歐洲業務。在她的帶領下，該地區的營收成長了 35%。\n\nDunn 先生表示：「Laura 既了解我們的客戶，也了解我們的員工。我有信心公司會繼續蓬勃發展。」\n\n上任後，Jennings 女士打算更加重視數位追蹤服務，這項服務讓客戶能掌握貨物在運送過程中每個階段的狀況。\n\nJennings 女士將於 1 月 4 日在總部對員工發表談話。","w":[731,561,669,533,590,730,529,744],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["convey","assume","deduct","dismiss"],"a":1,"ex":"assume the role of 是「接任…的職務」，assume 在這裡是「承擔、就任」的意思。dismiss 是解雇或駁回、convey 是傳達、deduct 是扣除，都不能和 role 搭配表示「上任」。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["has supervised","supervises","will supervise","was supervised"],"a":0,"ex":"句尾有 since 2021（從 2021 年到現在），要用現在完成式 has supervised。supervises 是現在簡單式，不能和 since 連用；will supervise 是未來式；was supervised 是過去被動，意思會變成她被監督。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["exposure","efficiency","capacity","emphasis"],"a":3,"ex":"place emphasis on 是固定搭配，意思是「把重點放在…、重視…」。exposure 是曝光或接觸、efficiency 是效率、capacity 是容量或產能，都不能和 place ... on 這樣搭配。"}]},
{"id":"r800-27","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"email","ti":"Inventory count this Sunday","tx":"To: All store staff\nFrom: Kevin Brandt, Store Manager\nSubject: Inventory count this Sunday\n\nHello everyone,\n\nOur twice-yearly inventory count will take place this Sunday, April 26, after the store closes at 6:00 P.M. Attendance is mandatory for everyone scheduled to work that evening. Please [1] ------- to the stockroom at 6:15 for instructions.\n\nCount carefully. Last time, the totals in several categories did not match our computer records, and it took three days to find the errors. [2] ------- figures help us order the right quantities and avoid running out of popular items.\n\nAny damaged or defective products that you find should be placed in the red bins near the back door. They [3] ------- on Monday morning after I have recorded them.\n\nDinner will be provided, and everyone will be paid at the overtime rate.\n\nThanks,\nKevin","zh":"收件人：全體門市同仁\n寄件人：Kevin Brandt，店長\n主旨：本週日庫存盤點\n\n大家好：\n\n我們半年一次的庫存盤點將在本週日 4 月 26 日晚上 6 點打烊後進行。當晚排班的同仁一律必須參加。請在 6 點 15 分前往倉庫聽取說明。\n\n請仔細清點。上一次有好幾個類別的總數和電腦紀錄對不上，花了三天才找出錯誤。正確的數字能幫助我們訂購適當的數量，避免熱門商品缺貨。\n\n如果發現任何損壞或有瑕疵的商品，請放進後門附近的紅色箱子裡。等我登記之後，這些商品會在星期一早上丟棄。\n\n當天會提供晚餐，所有人都會以加班費率計薪。\n\n謝謝\nKevin","w":[587,639,672,642,616,701],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["proceed","determine","obtain","notify"],"a":0,"ex":"proceed to + 地點 是「前往…」，請大家 6:15 前往倉庫聽取說明。notify（通知）、obtain（取得）、determine（決定）都是及物動詞，後面不能直接接 to the stockroom。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["Apprehensive","Accurate","Confidential","Controversial"],"a":1,"ex":"前面說上次的數字和電腦紀錄對不上，花了三天找錯誤，所以這裡強調「正確的」數字才能訂對數量，Accurate figures。Confidential 是機密的、Controversial 是有爭議的、Apprehensive 是憂慮的，都和訂貨數量無關。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["have discarded","will discard","will be discarded","were discarded"],"a":2,"ex":"They 指的是損壞或有瑕疵的商品，商品是「被丟棄」，時間是 on Monday morning（未來），所以用未來式被動 will be discarded。will discard 和 have discarded 是主動，而且後面沒有受詞；were discarded 是過去式，時間不對。"}]},
{"id":"r800-28","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"article","ti":"Tavero Releases Lightweight Travel Monitor","tx":"Tavero Releases Lightweight Travel Monitor\n\nElectronics maker Tavero Systems has released a portable computer monitor designed for business travelers. The Tavero Slim 14 weighs just 600 grams and is [1] ------- with most laptops and tablets through a single cable.\n\nAccording to product manager Irene Costa, the idea came from a customer [2] ------- conducted last year. More than half of the people who answered said that working on one small screen in a hotel room reduced their efficiency.\n\nThe Slim 14 costs $249 and comes with a protective cover and a two-year warranty. Tavero expects the product to boost its revenue in the portable device segment, where sales [3] ------- for the past two quarters.\n\nThe monitor is available now on the company's website and at major electronics stores.","zh":"Tavero 推出輕量型旅用螢幕\n\n電子產品製造商 Tavero Systems 推出了一款專為商務旅客設計的可攜式電腦螢幕。Tavero Slim 14 只有 600 公克重，用一條線就能與大多數筆電和平板電腦相容。\n\n產品經理 Irene Costa 表示，這個構想來自去年進行的一項顧客意見調查。超過半數的受訪者說，在飯店房間裡只用一個小螢幕工作會降低他們的效率。\n\nSlim 14 售價 249 美元，附保護套及兩年保固。可攜式裝置這個類別的銷售量在過去兩季持續下滑，Tavero 期望這款產品能提升該類別的營收。\n\n這款螢幕現在已經可以在該公司網站和各大電子產品賣場買到。","w":[748,620,594,536,747,590,502,746],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["compatible","exclusive","durable","eligible"],"a":0,"ex":"be compatible with 是「與…相容」，螢幕用一條線就能接上大多數筆電和平板。eligible 是有資格的（後面接 for）、durable 是耐用的、exclusive 是專屬的，都不會接 with most laptops。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["poll","clause","warranty","hazard"],"a":0,"ex":"後一句 More than half of the people who answered said... 說明這是一項有人回答的調查，a customer poll 是「顧客意見調查」。clause 是條款、warranty 是保固、hazard 是危險，都不是可以 conducted（進行）並且有人回答的東西。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["have declined","declining","will decline","are declined"],"a":0,"ex":"for the past two quarters（過去兩季以來）表示從過去持續到現在，要用現在完成式 have declined。will decline 是未來式，和 past 矛盾；decline 當「下降」時是不及物動詞，不用被動的 are declined；declining 不能單獨當動詞。"}]},
{"id":"r800-29","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"notice","ti":"Safety Notice: Storage of Cleaning Products","tx":"SAFETY NOTICE: Storage of Cleaning Products\n\nFollowing last week's safety inspection, all staff are reminded that cleaning products containing strong chemicals can be a serious [1] ------- if they are stored incorrectly.\n\nFrom now on, these products must be kept in the locked cabinet in the supply room, not under sinks or on open shelves. Each container must [2] ------- with its contents and the date it was opened. Never pour a product into an unmarked bottle.\n\nAs a further precaution, gloves and safety glasses are now available in the supply room. They must be worn [3] ------- you handle these products.\n\nIf a spill occurs, open the windows and notify the facilities supervisor immediately at extension 118. These measures will be enforced starting Monday, and supervisors will monitor each area regularly.","zh":"安全公告：清潔用品的存放\n\n上週安全檢查之後，在此提醒全體同仁：含有強烈化學物質的清潔用品如果存放不當，可能造成嚴重的危險。\n\n即日起，這類用品必須放在備品室上鎖的櫃子裡，不可放在水槽下方或開放式的架子上。每個容器都必須標示內容物和開封日期。絕對不要把清潔用品倒進沒有標示的瓶子裡。\n\n為了進一步預防意外，備品室現在備有手套和護目鏡。每次使用這些清潔用品時都必須配戴。\n\n萬一打翻，請打開窗戶，並立刻撥分機 118 通知總務主管。這些措施將自星期一起嚴格執行，各主管也會定期檢查各區域。","w":[531,579,554,532,725,599,699,736],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["merit","asset","prospect","hazard"],"a":3,"ex":"a serious hazard 是「嚴重的危險」，含有強烈化學物質的清潔用品如果存放不當會造成危險。merit 是優點、asset 是資產、prospect 是前景，都是正面的字，和 stored incorrectly 的情況不合。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["label","have labeled","labeling","be labeled"],"a":3,"ex":"助動詞 must 後面接原形動詞，而容器是「被貼上標籤」，所以用被動的 be labeled。label 和 have labeled 是主動，容器不會自己貼標籤；must 後面也不能接 labeling。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["although","unless","whereas","whenever"],"a":3,"ex":"手套和護目鏡是「每次」處理這些清潔用品時都要戴，所以用 whenever（每當）。although 是雖然、unless 是除非、whereas 是然而，放進去意思都不合理。"}]},
{"id":"r800-30","lv":800,"p":6,"k":"message","ti":"Reminder about the travel guidelines","tx":"From: Rachel Owens, Travel Coordinator\nTo: Sales team group chat\n\nHi everyone. Here is a quick reminder about the travel guidelines that we implemented on May 1.\n\n1. All flights and hotels must be booked through Skyway Travel, our official agency. It offers corporate rates that are not available on public websites.\n2. You need to [1] ------- written approval from your manager prior to booking any trip that costs more than $1,000.\n3. Keep every receipt. Any expense that is not supported by a receipt [2] ------- from your claim.\n\nThe agency's help line is open 24 hours a day, so you can get assistance even if a flight is canceled at night. The number is 555-0131.\n\n[3] ------- you have any questions about these rules, please message me directly. Have a safe trip!","zh":"寄件人：Rachel Owens，差旅統籌\n收件人：業務團隊群組\n\n大家好。在此簡單提醒各位我們 5 月 1 日開始實施的差旅規範。\n\n1. 所有機票和飯店都必須透過我們的指定旅行社 Skyway Travel 預訂。該旅行社提供一般網站上沒有的企業優惠價。\n2. 任何費用超過 1,000 美元的出差，訂票之前都必須先取得主管的書面核准。\n3. 請保留每一張收據。沒有收據佐證的費用，將從您的申請金額中扣除。\n\n旅行社的服務專線 24 小時開放，所以即使班機在半夜取消，您也能得到協助。電話是 555-0131。\n\n如果對這些規定有任何問題，請直接傳訊息給我。祝各位一路平安！","w":[544,676,572,631,709,624,691],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["qualify","restrict","notify","obtain"],"a":3,"ex":"obtain approval from 是「取得…的核准」，出差費用超過 1,000 美元要先取得主管的書面同意。restrict 是限制、notify 是通知（後面接人）、qualify 是使有資格，都不能接 written approval from your manager。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["deducting","has deducted","will deduct","will be deducted"],"a":3,"ex":"主詞 Any expense 是「被扣除」的對象，所以用被動語態 will be deducted from your claim（會從你的申請金額中扣除）。will deduct 和 has deducted 是主動，後面又沒有受詞；deducting 不能單獨當句子的動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Should","Would","Could","Might"],"a":0,"ex":"Should you have any questions 是 If you should have any questions 的倒裝，意思是「如果您有任何問題」，是商業書信的常見句型。Would、Could、Might 放在句首都不能這樣表示「如果」。"}]},
{"id":"r990-01","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Discrepancy on invoice 4471","tx":"To: Daniel Ortiz, Brightway Office Supply\nFrom: Mei-Ling Chen, Accounts Payable, Norland Freight\nSubject: Discrepancy on invoice 4471\n\nDear Mr. Ortiz,\n\nWhile reconciling our ledger for the third quarter, I noticed a discrepancy between invoice 4471 and the purchase order we issued on September 3. The purchase order authorized 40 ergonomic chairs at $185 each, whereas the invoice bills us for 48 chairs. Our warehouse records confirm that only 40 were delivered.\n\nI assume this is a simple oversight rather than a deliberate charge. Nevertheless, our internal policy obliges us to withhold payment on any invoice that deviates from the underlying purchase order. Accordingly, the outstanding balance of $8,880 will remain on hold until we receive a corrected invoice.\n\nOur external auditors begin their annual review on October 20, so a prompt reply would be appreciated. If a revised invoice reaches me by October 13, I can expedite the payment so that it is released within three business days instead of the usual thirty.\n\nPlease direct any further correspondence on this matter to me rather than to our procurement team.\n\nSincerely,\nMei-Ling Chen","zh":"收件人：Daniel Ortiz，Brightway Office Supply\n寄件人：Mei-Ling Chen，Norland Freight 應付帳款部\n主旨：第 4471 號發票金額不符\n\nOrtiz 先生您好：\n\n我在核對本公司第三季的總帳時，發現第 4471 號發票與我們 9 月 3 日開出的採購單有出入。採購單核准的是 40 張人體工學椅，每張 185 美元，但發票卻向我們請款 48 張。我們的倉庫紀錄確認只收到 40 張。\n\n我想這只是單純的疏忽，而不是刻意多收費用。不過，依照本公司內部規定，凡是與原始採購單不符的發票，我們都必須暫緩付款。因此，這筆 8,880 美元的未付款項將暫時保留，直到我們收到更正後的發票為止。\n\n本公司的外部稽核人員將於 10 月 20 日開始年度查核，因此希望您能盡快回覆。如果修正後的發票能在 10 月 13 日前寄達，我可以加速處理付款，讓款項在三個工作天內撥付，而不必等一般的三十天。\n\n關於此事的後續聯繫，請直接寄給我，不要寄給我們的採購團隊。\n\nMei-Ling Chen 敬上","w":[810,937,836,935,875,837,932,765],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Ms. Chen write the e-mail?","o":["To order additional chairs","To request a corrected invoice","To announce a new payment policy","To report damaged merchandise"],"a":1,"ex":"信中指出發票和採購單有 discrepancy（不一致），並說款項 will remain on hold until we receive a corrected invoice，可見目的是請對方重新開立正確的發票。信裡沒有要加訂椅子，也沒提到商品損壞；暫緩付款是公司原本就有的內部規定，不是在宣布新政策。"},{"q":"What will happen if a revised invoice arrives by October 13?","o":["The purchase order will be canceled","Payment will be released within three business days","The auditors will postpone their review","Eight more chairs will be delivered"],"a":1,"ex":"關鍵句是 If a revised invoice reaches me by October 13, I can expedite the payment so that it is released within three business days。expedite 是「加速處理」。稽核的日期沒有要延後，文中也沒說要補送椅子或取消採購單。"},{"q":"The word \"outstanding\" in paragraph 2 is closest in meaning to","o":["unpaid","excellent","estimated","noticeable"],"a":0,"ex":"outstanding balance 是固定搭配，指「尚未付清的款項」；前一句說公司必須 withhold payment（暫緩付款），所以這裡是 unpaid（未付的）。outstanding 雖然也有「傑出的」（excellent）、「顯著的」（noticeable）的意思，但用來形容 balance（餘額）說不通；estimated 是「估計的」，而 8,880 美元是確定的金額。"}]},
{"id":"r990-02","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"memo","ti":"Revised travel reimbursement rules","tx":"MEMO\n\nTo: All sales staff\nFrom: Karen Whitfield, Finance Director\nDate: March 2\nSubject: Revised travel reimbursement rules\n\nTravel expenditure rose 22 percent in the last fiscal year, far more than our budget can sustain. To curtail these costs without impeding client visits, the following rules will take effect on April 1.\n\nFirst, any trip expected to cost more than $1,500 must be authorized by your regional manager before tickets are purchased. Expenses incurred without prior approval will not be reimbursed. Second, claims must be submitted with itemized receipts within 14 days of your return; late claims will be paid only at the discretion of the finance department. Third, employees are expected to book economy fares on flights shorter than six hours. Staff traveling together with clients are exempt from this requirement.\n\nA recent audit found that nearly one in five claims lacked adequate documentation, so compliance with these rules will be monitored closely. Managers will be held accountable for every claim they approve.\n\nQuestions about the new rules should be directed to the finance department.","zh":"備忘錄\n\n收件人：全體業務人員\n寄件人：財務長 Karen Whitfield\n日期：3 月 2 日\n主旨：差旅費報帳規定修訂\n\n上一個會計年度的差旅支出增加了 22%，遠超過預算所能負擔的範圍。為了削減這些成本，同時又不妨礙拜訪客戶，以下規定將自 4 月 1 日起生效。\n\n第一，任何預估費用超過 1,500 美元的出差，都必須在購票前取得區域經理的核准。未經事先核准而產生的費用，一律不予報銷。第二，報帳申請必須在返回後 14 天內連同明細收據一併提出；逾期的申請是否給付，由財務部全權決定。第三，飛行時間少於六小時的航班，員工應訂經濟艙。與客戶同行的員工不受此項規定限制。\n\n最近一次稽核發現，將近五分之一的報帳申請缺少足夠的證明文件，因此公司將嚴格監督這些規定的遵守情況。主管必須為自己核准的每一筆申請負責。\n\n對新規定有任何疑問，請洽財務部。","w":[821,892,961,954,981,799,912,770],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main purpose of the memo?","o":["To announce a reduction in sales staff","To report the results of a client survey","To invite employees to a budget meeting","To explain new rules for travel expenses"],"a":3,"ex":"主旨是 Revised travel reimbursement rules，內文說 the following rules will take effect on April 1，接著列出三項關於差旅費的規定，所以目的是說明新的差旅費用規定。文中沒有提到裁減業務人員、預算會議或客戶調查。"},{"q":"Who does NOT have to book economy fares on flights under six hours?","o":["Employees traveling with clients","Finance department staff","Regional managers","Employees whose trips cost over $1,500"],"a":0,"ex":"文中說 Staff traveling together with clients are exempt from this requirement，exempt 是「免除的」，所以與客戶同行的員工不必訂經濟艙。區域經理負責核准出差、財務部負責處理報帳，超過 1,500 美元的出差只是需要事先核准，文中都沒有說這些人可以不訂經濟艙。"},{"q":"What is suggested about some past reimbursement claims?","o":["They lacked enough supporting documents","They were rejected by external auditors","They involved flights longer than six hours","They were paid twice by mistake"],"a":0,"ex":"依據是 A recent audit found that nearly one in five claims lacked adequate documentation，表示過去有些報帳申請的證明文件不足。文中沒有說這些申請被稽核人員退回、被重複付款，或是和六小時以上的航班有關。"}]},
{"id":"r990-03","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"Shareholders back Castell–Rhine merger","tx":"Shareholders Back Castell–Rhine Merger\n\nHARBOR CITY — Shareholders of Castell Logistics voted on Tuesday to approve a merger with Rhine Cargo, a smaller rival that specializes in refrigerated transport. The board had unanimously endorsed the deal in May, and more than 80 percent of the votes cast were in favor.\n\nUnder the terms disclosed last month, Rhine Cargo will become a subsidiary of Castell and will keep its own name for the foreseeable future. Castell's chairperson, Helen Navarro, said the two firms' networks are complementary: Castell is strong in long-distance road freight, while Rhine leads in cold-storage delivery within the region. She expects the resulting synergy to yield annual savings of about $12 million, chiefly by consolidating warehouses.\n\nNot everyone is convinced. Some analysts warn that integrating two separate tracking systems will entail considerable expense and could offset much of the projected saving during the first two years.\n\nThe transaction still requires clearance from regulators and is expected to close in early December. Rhine's chief executive, Paul Derrick, will remain in his post.","zh":"股東支持 Castell 與 Rhine 合併案\n\nHARBOR CITY 訊 — Castell Logistics 的股東週二投票通過與 Rhine Cargo 的合併案。Rhine Cargo 是規模較小的同業對手，專營冷藏運輸。董事會已在五月一致表態支持這項交易，而這次投票有超過八成的票數贊成。\n\n根據上個月公布的條件，Rhine Cargo 將成為 Castell 的子公司，並在可預見的未來保留原有名稱。Castell 董事長 Helen Navarro 表示，兩家公司的運輸網具有互補性：Castell 的強項是長途公路貨運，Rhine 則在區域內的低溫倉儲配送居於領先地位。她預期由此產生的綜效每年可省下約 1,200 萬美元，主要來自整併倉庫。\n\n不過，並非所有人都看好。部分分析師提醒，整合兩套各自獨立的貨物追蹤系統將需要可觀的費用，可能會抵銷頭兩年大部分的預期節省金額。\n\n這筆交易仍須取得主管機關核准，預計在十二月初完成。Rhine 執行長 Paul Derrick 將留任原職。","w":[834,761,917,964,805,841,942,990],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article mainly about?","o":["The opening of a new cold-storage warehouse","A dispute between regulators and a logistics firm","The resignation of a company's chairperson","The approval of a merger between two transport firms"],"a":3,"ex":"第一段說 Shareholders of Castell Logistics voted on Tuesday to approve a merger with Rhine Cargo，之後都在談這樁合併案的條件、效益和疑慮，所以主題是兩家運輸公司的合併案獲得通過。文中沒有董事長辭職、與主管機關的糾紛，也沒有新倉庫啟用。"},{"q":"According to Ms. Navarro, how will most of the savings be achieved?","o":["By reducing the number of drivers","By changing Rhine Cargo's name","By replacing the tracking systems","By combining warehouses"],"a":3,"ex":"Navarro 女士預期 annual savings of about $12 million, chiefly by consolidating warehouses。chiefly 是「主要」，consolidate 是「合併、整併」，也就是把倉庫合併起來。文中沒有提到減少司機；整合追蹤系統是分析師認為會花錢的地方，不是省錢的來源；Rhine Cargo 則會保留原名。"},{"q":"What is NOT stated about Rhine Cargo?","o":["It will keep its current name","It will relocate its headquarters","Its chief executive will stay on","It specializes in refrigerated transport"],"a":1,"ex":"文中寫到 specializes in refrigerated transport（專營冷藏運輸）、will keep its own name（保留原有名稱）、Paul Derrick will remain in his post（執行長留任），這三項都有提到。只有「搬遷總部」在文中完全沒有出現，所以是答案。"}]},
{"id":"r990-04","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"Elevator modernization at Kessler Tower","tx":"NOTICE TO ALL TENANTS OF KESSLER TOWER\n\nElevator Modernization\n\nBuilding management has engaged a licensed contractor to replace the control systems of all four passenger elevators. Work will commence on Monday, June 9, and is scheduled to finish by Friday, July 18.\n\nTo mitigate disruption, only one elevator will be taken out of service at a time. Tenants should nevertheless anticipate longer waits, particularly between 8:30 and 9:30 A.M. Intermittent noise is inevitable while the old equipment is being removed; the noisiest tasks have accordingly been restricted to the hours between 7:00 P.M. and 6:00 A.M.\n\nThe freight elevator at the rear of the premises will remain in operation throughout the project. In the interest of accessibility, it has been designated for visitors with limited mobility as well as for deliveries, so we ask other tenants to refrain from using it.\n\nCompanies planning to move furniture or large equipment during this period must notify the management office at least 48 hours in advance.\n\nThe new systems comply with the latest safety code and are expected to cut energy consumption by roughly 30 percent. We appreciate your patience.","zh":"KESSLER TOWER 全體租戶公告\n\n電梯更新工程\n\n大樓管理處已委託合格的承包商，更換全部四部客用電梯的控制系統。工程將於 6 月 9 日星期一開始，預定在 7 月 18 日星期五前完工。\n\n為了減輕對各位造成的不便，每次只會停用一部電梯。不過仍請租戶預期等候時間會拉長，尤其是上午 8:30 到 9:30 之間。拆除舊設備期間，難免會有斷斷續續的噪音；因此，最吵的作業已限定在晚上 7:00 到清晨 6:00 之間進行。\n\n位於大樓後方的貨梯在工程期間將照常運作。為了維持無障礙通行，除了送貨之外，這部貨梯也已指定供行動不便的訪客使用，因此請其他租戶不要搭乘。\n\n在此期間打算搬運家具或大型設備的公司，必須至少提前 48 小時通知管理處。\n\n新系統符合最新的安全規範，預計可減少約 30% 的耗電量。感謝您的耐心配合。","w":[766,974,966,904,865,758,977,926],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the notice?","o":["To introduce a new building manager","To announce an increase in rent","To inform tenants about upcoming elevator work","To report a recent safety violation"],"a":2,"ex":"公告一開始就說 a licensed contractor to replace the control systems of all four passenger elevators，並說明 Work will commence on Monday, June 9，後面都是工程期間的注意事項，所以目的是通知租戶即將進行電梯工程。文中沒有提到調漲租金、違反安全規定或新的大樓經理。"},{"q":"When will the loudest work be carried out?","o":["Only on weekends","During regular office hours","Between 7:00 P.M. and 6:00 A.M.","Between 8:30 and 9:30 A.M."],"a":2,"ex":"文中說 the noisiest tasks have accordingly been restricted to the hours between 7:00 P.M. and 6:00 A.M.，最吵的作業限定在晚上七點到清晨六點。上午 8:30 到 9:30 是等電梯會比較久的時段，不是施工時段；文中沒有說只在週末施工，安排在夜間正是為了避開上班時間。"},{"q":"The word \"mitigate\" in paragraph 2 is closest in meaning to","o":["schedule","predict","explain","lessen"],"a":3,"ex":"To mitigate disruption, only one elevator will be taken out of service at a time：一次只停用一部電梯，是為了「減輕」造成的不便，所以 mitigate 最接近 lessen（減少、減輕）。predict 是「預測」、explain 是「解釋」、schedule 是「安排時間」，都不是 mitigate 的意思。"}]},
{"id":"r990-05","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"advertisement","ti":"Procurement Manager wanted at Alder & Finch","tx":"Procurement Manager — Alder & Finch Foods\n\nAlder & Finch, an established producer of packaged snacks with a diversified clientele in twelve countries, is seeking a Procurement Manager for its Riverside headquarters.\n\nThe successful candidate will oversee a team of six buyers, negotiate contracts with suppliers of raw commodities such as wheat and sugar, and liaise with the logistics department to keep production lines supplied. Because commodity prices fluctuate sharply, the role demands sound judgment and the ability to assess risk under tight time constraints.\n\nApplicants must hold a degree in business or a related field and have at least five years of managerial experience in purchasing. Proficiency in a second language is desirable but not essential. Familiarity with food-safety legislation will be regarded as a considerable advantage.\n\nWe offer a competitive salary, performance-based incentives, and reimbursement of relocation costs up to $6,000.\n\nTo apply, submit a résumé and a letter outlining your credentials through the Careers page of our website by November 30. Shortlisted candidates will be invited to a preliminary video interview in mid-December; final interviews will be held onsite in January.","zh":"採購經理 — Alder & Finch Foods\n\nAlder & Finch 是一家信譽卓著的包裝零食製造商，客戶群多元，遍及十二個國家。本公司 Riverside 總部現正招募採購經理一名。\n\n錄取者將負責督導六名採購人員、與小麥和糖等原物料商品的供應商洽談合約，並與物流部門聯繫協調，確保生產線供料無虞。由於原物料價格波動劇烈，這個職位需要良好的判斷力，以及在緊迫的時間限制下評估風險的能力。\n\n應徵者必須具備商學或相關科系的學位，並有至少五年的採購管理經驗。精通第二外語者尤佳，但並非必要條件。熟悉食品安全法規者將大為加分。\n\n我們提供具競爭力的薪資、依績效發放的獎勵金，以及最高 6,000 美元的搬遷費用補助。\n\n有意應徵者，請於 11 月 30 日前透過本公司網站的「徵才」頁面，提交履歷及一封說明個人資歷的信函。進入候選名單者將受邀於十二月中旬參加初步的視訊面試；最終面試將於一月在公司現場舉行。","w":[824,806,923,986,918,842,775,988],"qs":[{"q":"What is indicated about Alder & Finch?","o":["It was founded twelve years ago","It grows its own wheat and sugar","It has customers in many countries","It recently moved its headquarters"],"a":2,"ex":"第一段說公司有 a diversified clientele in twelve countries，clientele 是「顧客群」，可知客戶遍布許多國家。twelve 指的是國家的數目，不是成立的年數；文中沒說總部最近搬遷；小麥和糖是向 suppliers（供應商）採購的，不是自己種的。"},{"q":"What is a requirement for the position?","o":["Familiarity with food-safety legislation","Proficiency in a second language","Managerial experience in purchasing","Previous work in the snack industry"],"a":2,"ex":"Applicants must ... have at least five years of managerial experience in purchasing，must 表示必要條件，所以採購方面的管理經驗是必備的。第二外語是 desirable but not essential（有更好，但非必要）；熟悉食品安全法規只是 a considerable advantage（加分項目）；文中也沒有要求零食業的工作經驗。"},{"q":"What is suggested about the interview process?","o":["All interviews will take place in December","The first round will be conducted by video","Final interviews will be held online","Candidates will be interviewed by six buyers"],"a":1,"ex":"最後一句說 a preliminary video interview in mid-December; final interviews will be held onsite in January。preliminary 是「初步的」，可見第一輪是視訊面試。最終面試在一月，而且是 onsite（到公司現場），所以「全部在十二月」和「最終面試在線上舉行」都不對；六名採購人員是這位經理要帶領的團隊，不是面試官。"}]},
{"id":"r990-06","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"message","ti":"Payroll software rollout: team chat","tx":"Ravi Menon (9:02 A.M.): Good morning. I brief the executives at 11:00, so I need a quick update. Where are we on the payroll software rollout?\n\nSofia Lindqvist (9:05 A.M.): The new system was deployed in the Denver and Austin offices over the weekend. Denver is running smoothly. Austin is reporting intermittent connectivity: users are logged out every twenty minutes or so.\n\nRavi Menon (9:07 A.M.): Is that our software or their network?\n\nTomas Vega (9:10 A.M.): Almost certainly their network. I spent an hour troubleshooting with their technician this morning. The application itself never crashed; the connection to the server simply drops. Their router has not been updated in years.\n\nSofia Lindqvist (9:12 A.M.): I agree. But until that is fixed, Austin cannot process Friday's payroll on the new system.\n\nRavi Menon (9:15 A.M.): Then let's be pragmatic. Austin goes back to the old system for this pay cycle. Tomas, please escalate the router issue to the infrastructure team and ask them to treat it as urgent. Sofia, postpone the Seattle rollout by a week so that we don't add to the backlog.\n\nTomas Vega (9:16 A.M.): Will do. You'll have a written summary by 10:30.","zh":"Ravi Menon（上午 9:02）：早安。我 11:00 要向高階主管做簡報，所以需要大家快速更新一下進度。薪資軟體的導入目前進行到哪裡了？\n\nSofia Lindqvist（上午 9:05）：新系統已在週末部署到 Denver 和 Austin 兩個辦公室。Denver 運作順利。Austin 則回報連線時斷時續：使用者大約每二十分鐘就會被登出一次。\n\nRavi Menon（上午 9:07）：是我們軟體的問題，還是他們網路的問題？\n\nTomas Vega（上午 9:10）：幾乎可以確定是他們的網路。今天早上我和他們的技術人員花了一個小時排查問題。應用程式本身從來沒有當機，只是和伺服器之間的連線會中斷。他們的路由器已經好幾年沒更新了。\n\nSofia Lindqvist（上午 9:12）：我同意。不過在修好之前，Austin 沒辦法用新系統處理星期五的薪資發放。\n\nRavi Menon（上午 9:15）：那我們就務實一點。這一期的薪資，Austin 先改回舊系統。Tomas，請把路由器的問題往上呈報給基礎設施團隊，並請他們列為緊急事項處理。Sofia，請把 Seattle 的導入時程延後一週，免得待處理的工作越積越多。\n\nTomas Vega（上午 9:16）：沒問題。10:30 前會給您一份書面摘要。","w":[753,784,971,904,771,943,950,804],"qs":[{"q":"What problem are the writers discussing?","o":["A technician did not arrive in Austin","Users in one office keep losing their connection","Employees in Denver were paid late","The payroll software has crashed several times"],"a":1,"ex":"Lindqvist 女士說 Austin is reporting intermittent connectivity: users are logged out every twenty minutes or so，也就是 Austin 辦公室的使用者連線一直中斷。Vega 先生明確說 The application itself never crashed（軟體沒有當機）；Denver 是 running smoothly；Austin 的技術人員有和 Vega 先生一起排查問題，文中沒有說技術人員沒到。"},{"q":"According to Mr. Vega, what is the most likely cause of the problem?","o":["A mistake made during the weekend installation","A shortage of trained technicians","A defect in the new software","Outdated network equipment in Austin"],"a":3,"ex":"Vega 先生說 Almost certainly their network，又說 Their router has not been updated in years（路由器好幾年沒更新），所以他認為原因是 Austin 老舊的網路設備。他說 The application itself never crashed，排除了軟體本身有缺陷的可能；文中也沒有提到週末安裝時出錯或技術人員不足。"},{"q":"What will most likely happen on Friday?","o":["Austin staff will be paid through the old system","The Denver office will return to the old system","Mr. Menon will travel to Austin","The Seattle office will start using the new software"],"a":0,"ex":"Lindqvist 女士說 Austin cannot process Friday's payroll on the new system，Menon 先生接著決定 Austin goes back to the old system for this pay cycle，所以星期五 Austin 的薪資會用舊系統發放。Seattle 的導入被延後一週；Denver 運作順利，沒有要改回舊系統；文中也沒有說 Menon 先生要去 Austin。"}]},
{"id":"r990-07","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"letter","ti":"Notice regarding your dormant savings account","tx":"Larkfield Community Bank\n218 Canal Street\n\nApril 4\n\nMr. Victor Lopez\n57 Birchwood Lane\n\nDear Mr. Lopez,\n\nOur records show that no deposits or withdrawals have been made on your savings account ending in 3306 since March of last year. Under current banking legislation, an account that shows no customer activity for twelve consecutive months must be classified as dormant.\n\nYour funds remain safe and will continue to accrue interest at the current rate. However, a provision in your account agreement entitles the bank to charge a monthly maintenance fee of $5 on dormant accounts, commencing 60 days from the date of this letter. In addition, if an account stays inactive for five years, we are required by law to close it and transfer the balance to the government's unclaimed-funds office.\n\nTo restore your account to active status, simply make a transaction of any amount or visit any branch with valid photo identification. No fee will be incurred if you do so before June 3.\n\nIf you believe this letter was sent in error, please contact us promptly at 555-0142.\n\nSincerely,\nGrace Okafor\nCustomer Accounts Manager","zh":"Larkfield Community Bank\n218 Canal Street\n\n4 月 4 日\n\nVictor Lopez 先生\n57 Birchwood Lane\n\nLopez 先生您好：\n\n本行紀錄顯示，您尾號 3306 的儲蓄帳戶自去年三月以來，沒有任何存款或提款紀錄。依現行銀行法規，連續十二個月沒有客戶交易往來的帳戶，必須列為靜止戶。\n\n您的存款依然安全，並會繼續依目前的利率累計利息。不過，依照帳戶約定書中的一項條款，本行有權自本函日期起 60 天後，開始對靜止戶每月收取 5 美元的帳戶管理費。此外，帳戶若連續五年沒有往來，本行依法必須將其結清，並將餘額移交政府的無人認領款項管理單位。\n\n如要恢復帳戶的正常狀態，只需進行一筆任何金額的交易，或攜帶有效的附照片身分證件至任一分行辦理即可。若您在 6 月 3 日前完成，就不會產生任何費用。\n\n如果您認為本函是誤寄，請盡快來電 555-0142 與我們聯絡。\n\n客戶帳戶經理\nGrace Okafor 敬上","w":[882,825,965,816,939,974,954],"qs":[{"q":"Why was the letter sent to Mr. Lopez?","o":["To request repayment of a loan","To warn him that his account is considered inactive","To confirm that his account has been closed","To announce a change in interest rates"],"a":1,"ex":"信中說他的帳戶超過十二個月沒有往來，must be classified as dormant（必須列為靜止戶），並提醒之後會開始收費，所以是通知他帳戶已被視為不活躍。帳戶並沒有被結清（要連續五年沒往來才會）；利息仍 at the current rate，利率沒變；信裡也沒提到貸款。"},{"q":"How can Mr. Lopez avoid the monthly fee?","o":["By signing a new account agreement","By making a transaction before June 3","By opening a second savings account","By writing to the unclaimed-funds office"],"a":1,"ex":"第三段說 simply make a transaction of any amount or visit any branch ... No fee will be incurred if you do so before June 3，只要在 6 月 3 日前進行一筆交易，就不會被收費。文中沒有要他另開帳戶或重簽約定書；unclaimed-funds office 是帳戶五年沒往來時餘額會被移交的單位，和免收管理費無關。"},{"q":"The word \"accrue\" in paragraph 2 is closest in meaning to","o":["owe","lose","accumulate","transfer"],"a":2,"ex":"Your funds remain safe and will continue to accrue interest：存款很安全，而且會繼續「累計」利息，accrue interest 是常見搭配，意思最接近 accumulate（累積）。lose 是「失去」，和 remain safe 的語意相反；owe 是「欠」；transfer 是「轉移」，都不是 accrue 的意思。"}]},
{"id":"r990-08","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"review","ti":"Review: Stratus Rise standing desk","tx":"Product review: Stratus Rise standing desk\nRating: 4 out of 5\nReviewed by Hannah Brooks, office manager\n\nWe bought twelve Stratus Rise desks when our firm refurbished its workstations last spring, and after eight months of daily use I can offer a fair appraisal.\n\nThe ergonomic design is the desk's foremost strength. The height adjusts quietly at the touch of a button, and the control panel is so intuitive that nobody on our staff needed the manual. Several colleagues say that alternating between sitting and standing has alleviated the discomfort of long hours at a desk. The steel frame feels solid, and the surface shows no scratches despite heavy use.\n\nMy reservations concern assembly and price. The printed instructions deviate from the parts actually supplied, and each desk took two people about ninety minutes to put together. At $640, it also costs considerably more than comparable models. On the other hand, the manufacturer's customer service was exceptional: when one motor failed in the fifth month, a replacement was dispatched within 48 hours at no charge.\n\nOverall, this is a sophisticated, durable product, provided you are willing to pay a premium and set aside an afternoon for assembly.","zh":"產品評論：Stratus Rise 升降桌\n評分：4 分（滿分 5 分）\n評論者：辦公室經理 Hannah Brooks\n\n去年春天公司翻新工作站時，我們買了十二張 Stratus Rise 升降桌。每天使用了八個月之後，我可以給出一個公允的評價。\n\n符合人體工學的設計是這張桌子最大的優點。只要按一個按鈕，桌面高度就能安靜地調整；控制面板非常直覺，我們沒有任何同事需要看說明書。好幾位同事說，坐著和站著交替工作，減輕了長時間坐在桌前的不適。鋼製桌架感覺很穩固，桌面雖然使用頻繁，卻沒有任何刮痕。\n\n我有所保留的地方是組裝和價格。紙本說明書和實際附的零件不一致，每張桌子要兩個人花大約九十分鐘才能組好。640 美元的售價也比同級產品貴上不少。不過另一方面，製造商的客服非常出色：第五個月時有一個馬達故障，替換品在 48 小時內就免費寄出了。\n\n整體來說，這是一款精密又耐用的產品，前提是你願意多付一些錢，並且空出一個下午來組裝。","w":[757,812,903,908,877,984,976,991],"qs":[{"q":"What does the reviewer consider the desk's greatest strength?","o":["Its detailed manual","Its low price","Its simple assembly","Its ergonomic design"],"a":3,"ex":"第二段第一句說 The ergonomic design is the desk's foremost strength，foremost 是「最重要的」，所以最大的優點是符合人體工學的設計。價格是 costs considerably more than comparable models（比同級產品貴）；組裝要兩個人花九十分鐘；說明書則和實際零件不符，這些都是缺點。"},{"q":"What happened in the fifth month of use?","o":["A desk was returned for a refund","A motor stopped working","The control panel was replaced","The surface became scratched"],"a":1,"ex":"文中說 when one motor failed in the fifth month, a replacement was dispatched within 48 hours，第五個月時有一個馬達故障。桌面是 shows no scratches（沒有刮痕）；被更換的是馬達，不是控制面板；廠商寄來的是替換品，沒有提到退貨退款。"},{"q":"What is NOT mentioned as a drawback of the desk?","o":["Noisy height adjustment","A relatively high price","Lengthy assembly","Inaccurate assembly instructions"],"a":0,"ex":"評論說 The height adjusts quietly（調整高度時很安靜），所以「調整高度很吵」不是缺點，是答案。其他三項文中都有提到：The printed instructions deviate from the parts actually supplied（說明書與零件不符）、costs considerably more than comparable models（價格偏高）、about ninety minutes to put together（組裝費時）。"}]},
{"id":"r990-09","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"announcement","ti":"Lakeshore Entrepreneurs' Forum returns in October","tx":"Lakeshore Entrepreneurs' Forum Returns in October\n\nThe Lakeshore Chamber of Commerce is pleased to announce that its ninth annual Entrepreneurs' Forum will convene on October 17 and 18 at the Marlowe Conference Center.\n\nThis year's theme, \"Growing Without Outside Capital,\" will be addressed by a panel of accomplished business owners. The keynote speaker is Irene Castillo, cofounder of the renowned bakery franchise Maple Oven, who will describe how she turned a single shop into a chain of sixty outlets without borrowing from a bank. Other sessions encompass topics ranging from cybersecurity for small firms to practical ways of monetizing an online audience.\n\nRegistration costs $180 for both days or $110 for a single day. Chamber members are entitled to a 20 percent discount, and full-time students may attend free of charge on presentation of valid identification. Seating is limited to 300, and last year's forum sold out three weeks in advance, so prompt registration is advised.\n\nAll proceeds will fund the Chamber's outreach program, which offers free mentoring to prospective business owners in the region.\n\nTo register, visit the Chamber's website or call 555-0177.","zh":"Lakeshore 創業家論壇十月再度登場\n\nLakeshore 商會很高興宣布，第九屆年度創業家論壇將於 10 月 17 日及 18 日在 Marlowe 會議中心舉行。\n\n今年的主題是「不靠外部資本也能成長」，將由多位成就卓越的企業主組成座談小組進行探討。主講人是知名烘焙連鎖加盟品牌 Maple Oven 的共同創辦人 Irene Castillo，她將分享自己如何在不向銀行借款的情況下，把一家小店發展成擁有六十家門市的連鎖體系。其他場次涵蓋的主題，從小型企業的資訊安全，到把線上觀眾變現的實用方法，應有盡有。\n\n兩日的報名費為 180 美元，單日為 110 美元。商會會員可享八折優惠，全職學生出示有效證件即可免費參加。座位限額 300 名，而去年的論壇在活動三週前就已售完，因此建議盡早報名。\n\n所有收益將用於贊助商會的外展計畫，該計畫為本地區有意創業的人士提供免費輔導。\n\n報名請上商會網站，或致電 555-0177。","w":[750,956,776,869,993,957,813,848],"qs":[{"q":"What is being announced?","o":["A two-day event for business owners","A change in chamber membership fees","The opening of a new bakery outlet","A mentoring program for students"],"a":0,"ex":"第一段說 its ninth annual Entrepreneurs' Forum will convene on October 17 and 18，entrepreneur 是「創業家」，convene 是「集會、召開」，所以宣布的是為期兩天、給企業主參加的活動。烘焙品牌只是主講人的背景；輔導計畫是收益的用途，對象是有意創業的人；文中沒有提到會費調整。"},{"q":"How much would a chamber member pay to attend both days?","o":["$110","$144","$88","$180"],"a":1,"ex":"兩天的報名費是 $180 for both days，而 Chamber members are entitled to a 20 percent discount，會員打八折：180 × 0.8 = 144 美元。180 美元是非會員的兩日費用，110 美元是非會員的單日費用，88 美元則是會員的單日費用（110 × 0.8）。"},{"q":"What is suggested about last year's forum?","o":["It was held at a different venue","It was free for chamber members","It lasted only one day","All of its seats were filled"],"a":3,"ex":"文中說 last year's forum sold out three weeks in advance，sold out 是「售完」，表示去年所有座位都被訂滿了，所以才建議 prompt registration（盡早報名）。文中沒有說去年在別的場地舉行、只辦一天，或是會員免費。"}]},
{"id":"r990-10","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"form","ti":"Consignment confirmation no. TR-58214","tx":"TRANSPACIFIC FREIGHT SERVICES\nConsignment Confirmation No. TR-58214\n\nShipper: Dalton Machine Parts, 9 Foundry Road\nRecipient: Kobe Precision Tools (Attention: Mr. Hiro Tanaka)\nContents: 14 crates of steel fittings, total weight 2,310 kg\nService: Standard ocean freight\nDate dispatched: August 6\nEstimated arrival: September 2\n\nCharges\nFreight: $3,420\nInsurance (declared value $58,000): $290\nCustoms documentation: $150\nTotal due: $3,860, payable within 30 days of dispatch\n\nTerms\n1. The estimated arrival date is provisional and may change owing to weather or port congestion.\n2. Our liability for loss or damage is limited to the declared value stated above.\n3. The shipper is accountable for ensuring that the contents match the specifications given on the customs declaration. Any fines or storage fees incurred as a result of a discrepancy will be charged to the shipper.\n4. Delivery may be expedited by transferring the consignment to air freight before it is loaded onto the vessel. An additional fee applies, and requests must be made in writing.\n\nPlease quote the confirmation number in all correspondence and inquiries.","zh":"TRANSPACIFIC FREIGHT SERVICES\n託運確認單　編號 TR-58214\n\n託運人：Dalton Machine Parts，9 Foundry Road\n收件人：Kobe Precision Tools（Hiro Tanaka 先生收）\n內容物：鋼製配件 14 箱，總重量 2,310 公斤\n服務類別：一般海運\n發送日期：8 月 6 日\n預計抵達日期：9 月 2 日\n\n費用\n運費：3,420 美元\n保險費（申報價值 58,000 美元）：290 美元\n報關文件費：150 美元\n應付總額：3,860 美元，須於發送後 30 天內付清\n\n條款\n1. 預計抵達日期為暫定日期，可能因天候或港口壅塞而變動。\n2. 本公司對貨物遺失或損壞的賠償責任，以上述申報價值為限。\n3. 託運人須負責確保內容物與報關單上所載的規格相符。若因兩者不符而產生任何罰款或倉儲費用，將向託運人收取。\n4. 貨物裝船前，可改以空運運送以加速送達。此服務須另外收費，且須以書面提出申請。\n\n來函或洽詢時，請一律註明確認單編號。","w":[832,991,900,835,856,809,810,932],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of this document?","o":["To cancel a freight booking","To request a customs inspection","To confirm the details of a shipment","To report goods damaged in transit"],"a":2,"ex":"標題是 Consignment Confirmation，consignment 是「託運的貨物」，表單列出託運人、收件人、內容物、費用和條款，所以用途是確認一批貨物的運送細節。文中沒有要求海關檢查、沒有回報貨物受損，也沒有取消訂艙。"},{"q":"What is the most the carrier would pay if the goods were lost?","o":["$58,000","$3,860","$290","$3,420"],"a":0,"ex":"條款 2 說 Our liability for loss or damage is limited to the declared value stated above，liability 是「賠償責任」，而上方保險一欄寫著 declared value $58,000，所以貨物遺失時最多賠償 58,000 美元。3,860 美元是應付總額，3,420 美元是運費，290 美元是保險費。"},{"q":"Who would be charged if the customs declaration proved inaccurate?","o":["Kobe Precision Tools","Dalton Machine Parts","Transpacific Freight Services","Mr. Tanaka"],"a":1,"ex":"條款 3 說 Any fines or storage fees incurred as a result of a discrepancy will be charged to the shipper，費用由 shipper（託運人）負擔。表單最上面寫著 Shipper: Dalton Machine Parts，所以是 Dalton Machine Parts。Kobe Precision Tools 和 Tanaka 先生是收件方，Transpacific Freight Services 則是運送業者。"}]},
{"id":"r990-11","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Provisional booking for your leadership retreat","tx":"To: Olivia Grant, Fenwick Pharmaceutical Group\nFrom: Marco Bellini, Events Manager, Pinecrest Lodge\nSubject: Provisional booking for your leadership retreat\n\nDear Ms. Grant,\n\nThank you for your inquiry about holding your managerial retreat at Pinecrest Lodge from May 14 to 16. I am pleased to confirm that I have placed a provisional hold on 24 guest rooms and the Lakeview meeting hall.\n\nOur lodge caters almost exclusively to a corporate clientele, and its setting, forty minutes from the nearest town, is conducive to focused discussion. The hall has state-of-the-art projection equipment, and breakfast and lunch are included in the quoted rate of $210 per person per night. Dinner can be arranged at an additional charge.\n\nPlease note that the hold will lapse on March 31 unless we have received a signed agreement and a deposit of 25 percent. The deposit is refundable in full for cancellations made before April 20; after that date it is forfeited.\n\nYou mentioned that some participants have limited mobility. All ground-floor rooms meet current accessibility standards, and I will gladly set those rooms aside for the guests concerned once you tell me how many are needed.\n\nKind regards,\nMarco Bellini","zh":"收件人：Olivia Grant，Fenwick Pharmaceutical Group\n寄件人：Marco Bellini，Pinecrest Lodge 活動經理\n主旨：貴公司主管共識營的暫定訂位\n\nGrant 女士您好：\n\n感謝您來信詢問 5 月 14 日至 16 日在 Pinecrest Lodge 舉辦主管共識營的事宜。很高興通知您，我已為您暫時保留 24 間客房及 Lakeview 會議廳。\n\n本旅館的客群幾乎全是企業客戶，而且地點距離最近的城鎮有四十分鐘車程，環境很適合專心討論。會議廳配有最先進的投影設備；報價為每人每晚 210 美元，已包含早餐和午餐。晚餐可另外付費安排。\n\n請留意，除非我們在 3 月 31 日前收到簽妥的合約及 25% 的訂金，否則這項暫定保留將會失效。若在 4 月 20 日前取消，訂金可全額退還；超過該日期，訂金將被沒收。\n\n您提到有幾位與會者行動不便。本旅館一樓的所有客房都符合現行的無障礙標準，只要您告訴我需要幾間，我很樂意為這幾位貴賓預留。\n\nMarco Bellini 敬上","w":[774,900,916,806,864,907,996,872],"qs":[{"q":"Why did Mr. Bellini write to Ms. Grant?","o":["To request payment of an overdue invoice","To cancel a reservation she made","To invite her to a hotel opening","To reply to her request about booking an event"],"a":3,"ex":"第一句是 Thank you for your inquiry about holding your managerial retreat at Pinecrest Lodge，inquiry 是「詢問」，接著說明暫定訂位、報價和訂金，可見是在回覆她詢問場地預訂的事。他是替她保留房間，不是取消訂位；文中沒有逾期未付的帳款，也不是邀請她參加開幕活動。"},{"q":"What must Pinecrest Lodge receive by March 31?","o":["Full payment for 24 rooms","A final list of participants","A signed agreement and a deposit","A choice of dinner menu"],"a":2,"ex":"第三段說 the hold will lapse on March 31 unless we have received a signed agreement and a deposit of 25 percent，也就是 3 月 31 日前要收到簽好的合約和訂金。訂金只有 25%，不是 24 間房的全額；文中沒有要求提供與會者名單或選擇晚餐菜單。"},{"q":"What would most likely happen if Ms. Grant canceled on April 25?","o":["A fee of $210 would be charged","The booking would be moved to June","The deposit would be refunded in full","Her company would lose its deposit"],"a":3,"ex":"The deposit is refundable in full for cancellations made before April 20; after that date it is forfeited。4 月 25 日已經超過 4 月 20 日，forfeit 是「喪失、被沒收」，所以公司拿不回訂金。全額退還只適用於 4 月 20 日之前取消；文中沒有提到改期到六月；210 美元是每人每晚的房價，不是取消的手續費。"}]},
{"id":"r990-12","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"Verlane Paper reports progress on emissions","tx":"Verlane Paper Reports Progress on Emissions\n\nVerlane Paper, one of the region's foremost packaging manufacturers, announced yesterday that it has cut carbon emissions at its three mills by 18 percent over the past two years, surpassing the 15 percent benchmark it set when it launched its sustainability initiative.\n\nThe company attributes most of the reduction to a $40 million upgrade of its energy infrastructure, including boilers that burn wood waste instead of natural gas. A smaller share came from optimizing delivery routes, which shortened the average truck journey by eleven kilometers.\n\nChief executive Laura Stein acknowledged that the remaining targets will be harder to attain. \"The easy savings are behind us,\" she said. \"Halving our emissions by the end of the decade will entail investment on an unprecedented scale.\" She added that the firm does not intend to buy carbon credits to offset its output, a practice she described as a way of postponing real change.\n\nStakeholders have responded favorably. An independent auditor has verified the figures, and two major retail clients have since extended their supply contracts with Verlane.","zh":"Verlane Paper 公布減排進展\n\n本地區首屈一指的包裝材料製造商之一 Verlane Paper 昨日宣布，過去兩年來，旗下三座紙廠的碳排放量已減少 18%，超越了當初啟動永續發展計畫時所訂下的 15% 基準。\n\n該公司表示，減排成果大部分要歸功於斥資 4,000 萬美元升級能源基礎設施，其中包括改用燃燒廢木料而非天然氣的鍋爐。另有一小部分來自配送路線的最佳化，使每趟貨車的平均行駛距離縮短了十一公里。\n\n執行長 Laura Stein 坦言，剩下的目標會更難達成。她說：「容易省的部分我們都已經做完了。要在這個十年結束前把排放量減半，將需要規模空前的投資。」她還表示，公司不打算購買碳權來抵銷排放量，並形容這種做法只是在拖延真正的改變。\n\n利害關係人的反應相當正面。一位獨立稽核人員已查證這些數據，而且有兩家大型零售客戶隨後與 Verlane 延長了供貨合約。","w":[760,945,752,829,782,998,823,930],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article mainly about?","o":["A new regulation on packaging waste","A paper company's plan to close a mill","An increase in natural gas prices","A manufacturer's progress in reducing emissions"],"a":3,"ex":"標題是 Verlane Paper Reports Progress on Emissions，第一段說它 has cut carbon emissions ... by 18 percent，全文都在講這家製造商減少排放的成果，emission 是「排放」。文中沒有提到包裝廢棄物的新法規、關閉紙廠，或天然氣漲價。"},{"q":"What accounted for most of the reduction?","o":["Shorter delivery routes","An upgrade of energy equipment","A decline in paper production","The purchase of carbon credits"],"a":1,"ex":"The company attributes most of the reduction to a $40 million upgrade of its energy infrastructure：attribute A to B 是「把 A 歸因於 B」，most 指大部分，所以主因是能源設備的升級。配送路線縮短只貢獻了 A smaller share（較小的一部分）；公司明說 does not intend to buy carbon credits（不打算買碳權）；文中沒有提到產量下降。"},{"q":"The word \"attain\" in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to","o":["explain","reach","lower","publish"],"a":1,"ex":"the remaining targets will be harder to attain：剩下的目標更難「達成」，attain a target 和 reach a target 意思相同，所以答案是 reach（達到）。lower 是「降低」、publish 是「公布」、explain 是「解釋」，都不是 attain 的意思。"}]},
{"id":"r990-13","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"memo","ti":"Pilot of flexible scheduling","tx":"MEMO\n\nTo: Customer Support team leaders\nFrom: Anita Rao, Vice President of Human Resources\nDate: September 8\nSubject: Pilot of flexible scheduling\n\nStaff turnover in Customer Support reached 31 percent last year, nearly double the company average. Exit interviews indicate that rigid shift patterns, rather than pay, are the underlying cause. The executive team has therefore authorized a six-month pilot of flexible scheduling, commencing October 1.\n\nUnder the pilot, agents may choose their own start time between 7:00 and 10:00 A.M., provided that each team maintains its required coverage. Team leaders will coordinate the schedules and will have full discretion to resolve conflicts within their respective teams.\n\nWe will gauge the results using three metrics: staff retention, average response time, and customer satisfaction scores. If response times deteriorate by more than 10 percent, the pilot will be suspended.\n\nIt is a common misconception that flexibility lowers productivity. Evidence from our Dublin subsidiary, where a similar scheme has operated since last year, suggests the opposite. Nevertheless, please report any adverse effects to me promptly.\n\nA briefing for team leaders will be held on September 22 in the boardroom.","zh":"備忘錄\n\n收件人：客服部各組組長\n寄件人：人力資源副總 Anita Rao\n日期：9 月 8 日\n主旨：彈性排班試辦計畫\n\n客服部去年的員工流動率達到 31%，幾乎是全公司平均的兩倍。離職面談顯示，根本原因是僵化的輪班方式，而不是薪資。因此，高階主管團隊已核准自 10 月 1 日起試辦彈性排班，為期六個月。\n\n試辦期間，只要各組維持規定的值班人力，客服人員可以在上午 7:00 到 10:00 之間自行選擇上班時間。組長將負責協調班表，並有完全的決定權處理各自組內的排班衝突。\n\n我們將以三項指標來評估成效：員工留任率、平均回覆時間，以及顧客滿意度分數。如果回覆時間惡化超過 10%，試辦計畫將會暫停。\n\n「彈性會降低生產力」是常見的錯誤觀念。我們的 Dublin 子公司自去年起實施類似的制度，當地的資料顯示情況正好相反。儘管如此，若有任何負面影響，仍請盡快向我回報。\n\n組長說明會將於 9 月 22 日在董事會會議室舉行。","w":[828,890,960,799,994,844,803,967],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the pilot being introduced?","o":["To reduce the number of employees who leave","To extend customer support hours","To lower payroll costs","To prepare for opening a Dublin office"],"a":0,"ex":"第一段說 Staff turnover ... reached 31 percent，turnover 是「員工流動率」，而 rigid shift patterns ... are the underlying cause，所以公司 has therefore authorized 這項試辦，目的是減少離職的人數。文中說原因 rather than pay（不是薪資），和薪資成本無關；客服時間沒有要延長；Dublin 子公司早已存在，只是被拿來當例子。"},{"q":"What would cause the pilot to be suspended?","o":["Scheduling conflicts among agents","Complaints from the Dublin subsidiary","A fall in the number of job applicants","A significant worsening of response times"],"a":3,"ex":"If response times deteriorate by more than 10 percent, the pilot will be suspended：deteriorate 是「惡化」，回覆時間明顯變差就會暫停試辦。排班衝突由組長自行處理（full discretion to resolve conflicts），不會因此暫停；應徵人數和 Dublin 子公司的抱怨，文中都沒有提到。"},{"q":"What is NOT listed as a measure of the pilot's results?","o":["Average response time","Staff retention","Customer satisfaction scores","Sales revenue"],"a":3,"ex":"文中列出 three metrics: staff retention, average response time, and customer satisfaction scores，metric 是「衡量指標」。員工留任率、平均回覆時間、顧客滿意度分數都在其中，只有 sales revenue（銷售營收）沒有被列入，所以是答案。"}]},
{"id":"r990-14","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"notice","ti":"Mandatory cybersecurity training","tx":"NOTICE: MANDATORY CYBERSECURITY TRAINING\n\nFollowing last month's attempted breach of our customer database, the IT Security Office is instituting annual cybersecurity training for every employee. No customer data was exposed in the incident, but our investigation revealed that the attackers had exploited a password that two staff members had shared by e-mail.\n\nThe training is a preemptive measure, not a punishment. It consists of a 45-minute online course, administered through the staff portal, followed by a short quiz. A score of at least 80 percent is required; those who fall short may retake the quiz as many times as necessary.\n\nIt is imperative that all staff complete the course by November 30. On December 1, the network credentials of anyone who has not done so will be suspended until the training is finished. Only employees on extended leave are exempt, and they must complete the course within two weeks of their return.\n\nContractors with access to company systems are also covered by this requirement. Their respective supervisors are accountable for ensuring compliance.\n\nQuestions may be directed to the IT Security Office at extension 4410.","zh":"公告：資訊安全訓練（全員必修）\n\n繼上個月有人企圖入侵本公司的客戶資料庫之後，資訊安全室即將建立制度，要求每位員工每年接受資訊安全訓練。這起事件中沒有任何客戶資料外洩，但調查發現，攻擊者利用了兩名員工透過電子郵件互傳的一組密碼。\n\n這項訓練是預防性的措施，而不是處罰。內容包括一堂 45 分鐘的線上課程，透過員工入口網站進行，課後有一份簡短的測驗。測驗成績必須達到 80% 以上；未達標者可以重考，次數不限。\n\n所有員工務必在 11 月 30 日前完成課程。自 12 月 1 日起，凡是尚未完成者，其網路登入憑證將被停用，直到完成訓練為止。只有請長假的員工可以免除，但必須在返回工作崗位後兩週內完成課程。\n\n可存取公司系統的外包人員同樣適用這項規定。他們各自的主管須負責確保規定確實遵守。\n\n如有疑問，請洽資訊安全室，分機 4410。","w":[833,854,997,934,902,919,881,775],"qs":[{"q":"Why is the training being introduced?","o":["Customer data was stolen last month","Someone recently tried to break into a company database","A new staff portal has been launched","New legislation requires it"],"a":1,"ex":"第一句說 Following last month's attempted breach of our customer database，breach 是「入侵、違反」，attempted 表示「企圖」，所以原因是最近有人試圖入侵公司的資料庫。文中說 No customer data was exposed（資料沒有外洩），所以「客戶資料被偷」不對；也沒有提到新法規或新推出的入口網站。"},{"q":"What will happen on December 1 to staff who have not finished the course?","o":["Their quiz scores will be lowered","They will have to pay a fine","Their network access will be suspended","They must attend a class in person"],"a":2,"ex":"第三段說 On December 1, the network credentials of anyone who has not done so will be suspended until the training is finished，credentials 在這裡是登入用的帳號憑證，被停用就無法使用公司網路。文中沒有罰款、實體課程或扣測驗分數的規定。"},{"q":"The word \"imperative\" in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to","o":["difficult","customary","optional","essential"],"a":3,"ex":"It is imperative that all staff complete the course by November 30，而且沒完成就會被停用登入憑證，可見這是「非做不可」的事，imperative 最接近 essential（必要的）。optional 是「可自由選擇的」，意思正好相反；difficult 是「困難的」；customary 是「慣例的」。"}]},
{"id":"r990-15","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"email","ti":"Re: Missing items in order 77-2093","tx":"To: Jonathan Park\nFrom: Elena Marsh, Customer Care, Corbin Kitchenware\nSubject: Re: Missing items in order 77-2093\n\nDear Mr. Park,\n\nThank you for your message of January 9. Please accept my apologies for the trouble you have had with your order.\n\nHaving looked into the matter, I can confirm that your consignment left our warehouse complete. The box, however, was damaged in transit, and we attribute the loss of two of the six saucepans to that damage. Although the courier disputes its liability, we do not believe that a customer should have to wait while that question is settled.\n\nI have therefore authorized two replacement saucepans, which will be dispatched tomorrow by express service at no cost to you. In addition, the $12 delivery fee you paid will be reimbursed to your credit card within five business days. As a gesture of goodwill, I have also attached a voucher for 15 percent off your next purchase.\n\nIf you would rather not receive replacements, you are entitled to a refund for the missing items instead; simply reply to this message by noon tomorrow.\n\nShould you have any further inquiries, please quote your order number in all correspondence.\n\nYours sincerely,\nElena Marsh","zh":"收件人：Jonathan Park\n寄件人：Elena Marsh，Corbin Kitchenware 顧客服務部\n主旨：回覆：訂單 77-2093 缺少商品\n\nPark 先生您好：\n\n感謝您 1 月 9 日的來信。對於這筆訂單給您帶來的困擾，謹此致上歉意。\n\n經過調查，我可以確認您的貨物離開本公司倉庫時是完整的。然而，箱子在運送途中受損，我們認為六個湯鍋中有兩個遺失，就是這個原因造成的。雖然貨運公司對自身的賠償責任有異議，但我們認為不該讓顧客等到這個問題解決為止。\n\n因此，我已核准補寄兩個湯鍋，明天將以快遞寄出，您不需負擔任何費用。此外，您支付的 12 美元運費將在五個工作天內退回您的信用卡。為了表達我們的誠意，我也附上一張下次購物可享八五折的優惠券。\n\n如果您不想收到補寄的商品，您也有權改為就缺少的商品辦理退款；只要在明天中午前回覆這封信即可。\n\n日後如有任何其他疑問，來信時請一律註明您的訂單編號。\n\nElena Marsh 敬上","w":[832,998,835,960,991,981,939,765],"qs":[{"q":"What is the main purpose of the e-mail?","o":["To explain how an order problem will be resolved","To ask a customer to return damaged goods","To notify a customer of a price increase","To confirm that an order arrived complete"],"a":0,"ex":"信中先說明原因，再說 I have therefore authorized two replacement saucepans，並退還運費、附上優惠券，可見目的是說明訂單問題將如何解決。信中沒有要顧客把商品寄回；她確認的是貨物 left our warehouse complete（出倉時是完整的），不是送達時完整；也沒有提到漲價。"},{"q":"According to Ms. Marsh, why were two saucepans missing?","o":["The order was sent to the wrong address","The items were out of stock","The warehouse packed too few items","The box was damaged during shipping"],"a":3,"ex":"The box, however, was damaged in transit, and we attribute the loss of two of the six saucepans to that damage：attribute A to B 是「把 A 歸因於 B」，in transit 是「運送途中」，所以原因是箱子在運送時受損。她說貨物出倉時是完整的，所以不是倉庫少裝；文中沒有提到地址錯誤或缺貨。"},{"q":"What is NOT offered to Mr. Park?","o":["Free delivery on future orders","Repayment of the delivery fee","Replacement saucepans","A discount voucher"],"a":0,"ex":"信中提供了 two replacement saucepans（補寄湯鍋）、the $12 delivery fee you paid will be reimbursed（退還運費）、a voucher for 15 percent off your next purchase（折價券）。只有「以後的訂單免運費」沒有提到，所以是答案。"}]},
{"id":"r990-16","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"review","ti":"Review: Tallyview Analytics for small shops","tx":"Tallyview Analytics\nReviewed by Owen Travers, owner of Travers Cycle Shop\nRating: 4.5 out of 5\n\nLike many small enterprises, my shop had years of sales records that nobody ever looked at. I subscribed to Tallyview ten months ago hoping to turn that accumulation of data into something useful, and on the whole it has delivered.\n\nIts chief merit is simplicity. I have no technical expertise, yet the intuitive dashboard took me under an hour to learn. Tallyview complements the accounting program I already use rather than replacing it, and it compiles a sales report automatically every morning. The forecasting tool has been invaluable: last spring it predicted a surge in demand for children's bicycles, and because I ordered extra stock in advance, sales in that category rose 30 percent.\n\nIt is not flawless. Reports cannot be customized as much as I would like, and the mobile app lacks some of the functionality of the desktop version. Support, though, is prompt: both of my inquiries were answered within a day.\n\nAt $49 a month, Tallyview is not the cheapest option, but for a business without a data specialist it is well worth the expenditure.","zh":"Tallyview Analytics\n評論者：Travers Cycle Shop 老闆 Owen Travers\n評分：4.5 分（滿分 5 分）\n\n和許多小型企業一樣，我的店裡累積了好幾年的銷售紀錄，卻從來沒有人去看。十個月前我訂閱了 Tallyview，希望把這些累積下來的資料變成有用的東西，而整體來說，它確實做到了。\n\n它最大的優點就是簡單。我沒有任何技術方面的專業知識，但這個直覺式的儀表板我不到一小時就學會了。Tallyview 是搭配我原本就在用的會計程式一起使用，而不是取代它，而且每天早上會自動彙整出一份銷售報告。預測工具更是幫了大忙：去年春天它預測兒童腳踏車的需求會激增，我因此提前多訂了貨，結果這個類別的銷售額成長了 30%。\n\n它並非毫無缺點。報表可以自訂的程度不如我的期望，而且手機 App 少了桌面版的部分功能。不過客服的回覆很迅速：我兩次詢問都在一天內得到答覆。\n\n每月 49 美元的 Tallyview 並不是最便宜的選擇，但對於沒有資料分析專員的店家來說，這筆支出非常值得。","w":[802,817,877,924,938,894,819,860],"qs":[{"q":"What does the reviewer regard as the software's main advantage?","o":["It is easy to use","It replaces his accounting program","It costs less than rival products","It allows full customization of reports"],"a":0,"ex":"第二段第一句說 Its chief merit is simplicity（最大的優點是簡單），接著說 the intuitive dashboard took me under an hour to learn，所以主要優點是容易使用。他說 Tallyview is not the cheapest option（不是最便宜的）；它是 complements ... rather than replacing（搭配而不是取代）會計程式；報表則 cannot be customized as much as I would like（自訂程度不夠）。"},{"q":"What happened after the software forecast higher demand?","o":["The shop ran out of stock","The shop sold more children's bicycles","The shop lowered its prices","The shop hired a data specialist"],"a":1,"ex":"it predicted a surge in demand for children's bicycles, and because I ordered extra stock in advance, sales in that category rose 30 percent：surge 是「激增」，他提前多訂貨，結果兒童腳踏車的銷售額成長了 30%。文中說這家店是 a business without a data specialist（沒有資料專員），也沒有提到降價或缺貨。"},{"q":"The word \"prompt\" in paragraph 3 is closest in meaning to","o":["automatic","costly","quick","polite"],"a":2,"ex":"Support, though, is prompt: both of my inquiries were answered within a day：冒號後面說兩次詢問都在一天內得到回覆，可見 prompt 是「迅速的」，最接近 quick。polite 是「有禮貌的」、automatic 是「自動的」、costly 是「昂貴的」，都和「一天內回覆」這個說明對不上。"}]},
{"id":"r990-17","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"letter","ti":"Notice concerning your cleaning services contract","tx":"Hartwell Property Management\n40 Mason Avenue\n\nFebruary 11\n\nMr. Stephen Doyle\nBrightSpan Cleaning Services\n\nDear Mr. Doyle,\n\nI am writing with respect to the cleaning contract for the Ridgeway Business Center that our two firms signed last July.\n\nOver the past three months, the standard of service has deteriorated markedly. Our inspections on December 4, January 8, and February 5 each found that the lobby floors had not been polished and that waste had been left uncollected on the third and fourth floors. These were not isolated oversights. They deviate from the specifications in section 3 of the agreement, and two tenants have made formal complaints.\n\nUnder section 9, either party may terminate the contract if the other fails to remedy a breach within 30 days of written notice. Please regard this letter as such notice. Should the problems be corrected by March 13, the contract will continue as before. Otherwise, your services will cease on March 31, and we will withhold payment for any work found deficient in the meantime.\n\nI would welcome a meeting to discuss how this matter might be resolved and am available any afternoon next week.\n\nYours sincerely,\nPatricia Nolan\nFacilities Director","zh":"Hartwell Property Management\n40 Mason Avenue\n\n2 月 11 日\n\nStephen Doyle 先生\nBrightSpan Cleaning Services\n\nDoyle 先生您好：\n\n本函是關於我們兩家公司去年七月就 Ridgeway Business Center 所簽訂的清潔合約。\n\n過去三個月來，服務水準明顯惡化。我們在 12 月 4 日、1 月 8 日和 2 月 5 日的檢查中，每次都發現大廳地板沒有打蠟拋光，三樓和四樓的垃圾也沒有清運。這些並不是偶發的疏忽。這些情況不符合合約第 3 條所訂的規格，而且已有兩家租戶提出正式申訴。\n\n依據第 9 條，若一方在收到書面通知後 30 天內未能改正違約情事，另一方得終止合約。請將本函視為該項書面通知。如果問題在 3 月 13 日前改善，合約將照常繼續。否則，貴公司的服務將於 3 月 31 日終止，而且在此期間凡經查驗不合格的工作，我們都將暫不付款。\n\n我很樂意安排會面，討論如何解決這件事；下週任何一天的下午我都有空。\n\n設施處長\nPatricia Nolan 敬上","w":[853,967,830,976,809,970,854,935],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the letter?","o":["To warn a contractor that its service must improve","To request a price quotation","To thank a company for its work","To renew a cleaning contract"],"a":0,"ex":"信中指出 the standard of service has deteriorated markedly（服務水準明顯惡化），並說 Please regard this letter as such notice，如果沒有在期限內改善，合約就會終止，所以目的是警告承包商必須改善服務。信裡沒有要續約、沒有要求報價，也不是感謝信。"},{"q":"What will happen if the problems are corrected by March 13?","o":["A new agreement will be signed","The contract will end on March 31","The contract will remain in effect","Payment will be withheld"],"a":2,"ex":"Should the problems be corrected by March 13, the contract will continue as before：如果問題在 3 月 13 日前改善，合約照常繼續，也就是維持有效。3 月 31 日終止服務和暫不付款，都是 Otherwise（沒有改善）才會發生的事；文中沒有提到簽新合約。"},{"q":"The phrase \"with respect to\" in paragraph 1 is closest in meaning to","o":["instead of","concerning","in honor of","in spite of"],"a":1,"ex":"I am writing with respect to the cleaning contract：with respect to 是正式書信用語，意思是「關於」，最接近 concerning。這裡的 respect 是「方面」，不是「尊敬」，所以不是 in honor of（為了向…致敬）；in spite of 是「儘管」；instead of 是「而不是」。"}]},
{"id":"r990-18","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"article","ti":"Local coffee roaster turns to franchising","tx":"Local Coffee Roaster Turns to Franchising\n\nWhen Marcus Bell opened Graystone Coffee Roasters in a converted garage eleven years ago, he did not imagine building a national brand. Today the entrepreneur runs nine company-owned cafés, and last week he announced plans to franchise the concept, with twenty franchised outlets to open over the next three years.\n\nMr. Bell said franchising was the only viable route to rapid growth. \"Opening a café costs us around $400,000,\" he explained. \"We could not raise that much capital for dozens of sites without handing a substantial share of equity to outside investors, and I was not willing to do that.\" Franchisees will instead bear the opening costs and pay Graystone 6 percent of their sales.\n\nDespite inflation in the price of coffee beans, the company's profitability has held up, a result Mr. Bell attributes to a loyal clientele and a diversified menu; food now accounts for a third of revenue.\n\nProspective franchisees must have at least five years of managerial experience in retail or hospitality. A shortlist of applicants will be drawn up in March, and those selected will undergo eight weeks of training at Graystone's roasting plant.","zh":"在地咖啡烘焙商改走加盟路線\n\n十一年前，Marcus Bell 在一間改建的車庫裡開設 Graystone Coffee Roasters 時，並沒有想過要打造全國性的品牌。如今，這位創業家經營九家直營咖啡店，上週他更宣布計畫開放加盟，預計在未來三年內開設二十家加盟店。\n\nBell 先生表示，加盟是快速成長唯一可行的途徑。他解釋：「我們開一家咖啡店大約要花 40 萬美元。要為幾十個據點籌措這麼多資本，就不得不把相當大比例的股權讓給外部投資人，而我不願意這麼做。」改採加盟後，開店成本將由加盟主負擔，加盟主並須將營業額的 6% 支付給 Graystone。\n\n儘管咖啡豆價格上漲，公司的獲利能力依然維持穩定，Bell 先生把這個成果歸功於忠實的顧客群和多樣化的菜單；目前餐點已占營收的三分之一。\n\n有意加盟者必須具備至少五年的零售業或餐旅業管理經驗。公司將在三月擬定申請人的候選名單，獲選者將在 Graystone 的烘焙廠接受八週的訓練。","w":[750,993,866,781,811,773,755,806],"qs":[{"q":"What is the article mainly about?","o":["A new training school for café managers","A sharp rise in coffee bean prices","The sale of a café chain to investors","A coffee company's plan to grow through franchising"],"a":3,"ex":"第一段說 he announced plans to franchise the concept, with twenty franchised outlets to open over the next three years，franchise 是「開放加盟」，全文都在談這項計畫，所以主題是咖啡公司打算透過加盟來擴張。咖啡豆漲價只是順帶一提；他正是不想把股權讓給投資人，並沒有出售公司；八週訓練是給加盟主的，文中沒有提到成立學校。"},{"q":"Why did Mr. Bell decide to franchise his business?","o":["He could not find suitable café sites","His customers asked for more locations","He did not want to give up much ownership","His company-owned cafés were losing money"],"a":2,"ex":"他說自己籌措資本就得 handing a substantial share of equity to outside investors, and I was not willing to do that：equity 是「股權」，他不願意把一大部分股權讓出去，所以選擇加盟。文中沒有說找不到店面；公司的 profitability has held up（獲利維持穩定），並沒有虧損；也沒有提到顧客要求多開分店。"},{"q":"What is NOT mentioned as something franchisees will do?","o":["Give Graystone a share of their sales","Complete eight weeks of training","Pay the cost of opening a café","Roast their own coffee beans"],"a":3,"ex":"文中提到加盟主要 bear the opening costs（負擔開店成本）、pay Graystone 6 percent of their sales（把營業額的 6% 付給 Graystone）、undergo eight weeks of training（接受八週訓練）。只有「自己烘焙咖啡豆」文中沒有提到，所以是答案。"}]},
{"id":"r990-19","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"message","ti":"Flight delay before the board meeting","tx":"Diane Foster (6:48 A.M.): Kenji, bad news. My flight from Portland is delayed at least three hours because of fog, and we have not even boarded yet. I will not make the 10:00 board meeting.\n\nKenji Watanabe (6:53 A.M.): Understood. The chairperson will not want to postpone, since two directors fly home tonight. Shall I ask to move your item to the end of the agenda?\n\nDiane Foster (6:55 A.M.): Even then I would miss it. I would rather you presented the acquisition proposal in my place. You compiled most of the figures, and you know the justification for the price as well as I do.\n\nKenji Watanabe (6:58 A.M.): I am comfortable with the figures, but the directors will ask about the implications for our debt. That is your area.\n\nDiane Foster (7:01 A.M.): Fair point. I will write a one-page note on that now and e-mail it before I board. If they need more, they can call me after I land, around 11:30.\n\nKenji Watanabe (7:03 A.M.): That works. I will inform the board secretary and make sure your absence is recorded in the minutes.\n\nDiane Foster (7:04 A.M.): Thanks. Let's debrief this afternoon.","zh":"Diane Foster（上午 6:48）：Kenji，有個壞消息。我從 Portland 出發的班機因為起霧，至少要延誤三個小時，我們到現在都還沒登機。10:00 的董事會我是趕不上了。\n\nKenji Watanabe（上午 6:53）：了解。董事長應該不會想延期，因為有兩位董事今晚就要搭機回去。要不要我去問問看，能不能把您的議案挪到議程的最後？\n\nDiane Foster（上午 6:55）：就算那樣我也趕不上。我希望由你代替我報告收購提案。大部分的數字都是你彙整的，而且這個價格的理由，你和我一樣清楚。\n\nKenji Watanabe（上午 6:58）：數字的部分我沒問題，但董事們一定會問到這對公司負債的影響。那是您的專長。\n\nDiane Foster（上午 7:01）：說得有道理。我現在就寫一頁關於這部分的說明，登機前用電子郵件寄給你。如果他們需要更多資訊，可以等我落地後打電話給我，大約是 11:30。\n\nKenji Watanabe（上午 7:03）：這樣可行。我會通知董事會秘書，並確認您缺席一事有記入會議紀錄。\n\nDiane Foster（上午 7:04）：謝謝。我們今天下午再來檢討一下。","w":[849,759,807,938,787,751,783,999],"qs":[{"q":"Why is Ms. Foster unable to attend the meeting?","o":["The meeting was moved to an earlier time","She is busy compiling figures","Her flight has been delayed","She has to fly home tonight"],"a":2,"ex":"Foster 女士說 My flight from Portland is delayed at least three hours because of fog ... I will not make the 10:00 board meeting，班機延誤，所以趕不上會議。今晚要搭機回去的是兩位董事；數字大多是 Watanabe 先生已經彙整好的；會議時間仍是 10:00，沒有提前。"},{"q":"What does Ms. Foster ask Mr. Watanabe to do?","o":["Book her a seat on another flight","Postpone the board meeting","Present a proposal on her behalf","Move her item to the end of the agenda"],"a":2,"ex":"她說 I would rather you presented the acquisition proposal in my place，in my place 是「代替我」，所以是請他代為報告提案。延期是董事長不會願意的事；把議案挪到最後是 Watanabe 先生自己的提議，她回答 Even then I would miss it，沒有採納；文中沒有提到改訂班機。"},{"q":"What will Ms. Foster most likely do next?","o":["Prepare a short document about debt","Lower the proposed purchase price","Telephone the chairperson","Record the minutes of the meeting"],"a":0,"ex":"被問到負債的問題後，她說 I will write a one-page note on that now and e-mail it before I board，that 指的是 the implications for our debt，所以她接下來會寫一份關於負債的簡短說明。她沒有說要打電話給董事長；會議紀錄是 Watanabe 先生要請秘書處理的事；文中也沒有提到要調降收購價格。"}]},
{"id":"r990-20","lv":990,"p":7,"k":"announcement","ti":"Thornbury Group names new chief operating officer","tx":"Thornbury Group Names New Chief Operating Officer\n\nThornbury Group is pleased to announce that Priya Raman has been appointed chief operating officer, effective July 1. She succeeds Gerald Hsu, who is retiring after 26 years with the company.\n\nMs. Raman joined Thornbury nine years ago as a logistics analyst and has led our Singapore subsidiary since 2021. Under her leadership, the subsidiary restructured its distribution network, cut delivery times by a fifth, and attained the highest customer retention rate of any unit in the group. Her pragmatic approach and her ability to foster cooperation between departments exemplify the qualities the board was seeking, and the directors voted unanimously in favor of her appointment.\n\nIn her new role, Ms. Raman will oversee manufacturing, procurement, and distribution in all eleven countries where Thornbury operates. Her foremost priority will be to consolidate the group's four regional warehouses in Europe into two by the end of next year.\n\nMr. Hsu will stay on in an advisory capacity until September 30 to facilitate the transition. A reception in recognition of his service will be held at headquarters on June 27, and all employees are welcome.","zh":"Thornbury Group 任命新任營運長\n\nThornbury Group 很高興宣布，Priya Raman 已獲任命為營運長，自 7 月 1 日起生效。她將接替 Gerald Hsu，Hsu 先生在公司服務 26 年後即將退休。\n\nRaman 女士九年前加入 Thornbury 擔任物流分析師，自 2021 年起領導本集團的新加坡子公司。在她的帶領下，該子公司重整了配送網路，將送貨時間縮短五分之一，並達到全集團各單位中最高的顧客留存率。她務實的作風，以及促進跨部門合作的能力，正是董事會所尋求特質的最佳典範，董事們一致投票贊成這項任命。\n\n就任新職後，Raman 女士將督導 Thornbury 在全部十一個營運國家的製造、採購和配送業務。她的首要任務是在明年年底前，把集團在歐洲的四座區域倉庫整併為兩座。\n\nHsu 先生將以顧問身分留任至 9 月 30 日，以協助交接順利進行。表彰他多年貢獻的茶會將於 6 月 27 日在總部舉行，歡迎全體員工參加。","w":[949,805,936,803,898,940,923,942],"qs":[{"q":"What is the purpose of the announcement?","o":["To announce a merger with another firm","To introduce a newly appointed executive","To invite employees to a training session","To report the closure of a subsidiary"],"a":1,"ex":"第一句說 Priya Raman has been appointed chief operating officer，接著介紹她的經歷和新職責，所以目的是介紹新任命的高階主管。文中沒有子公司關閉或與其他公司合併；最後提到的是表揚 Hsu 先生的茶會（reception），不是訓練課程。"},{"q":"What did the Singapore subsidiary achieve under Ms. Raman?","o":["It shortened its delivery times","It lowered its manufacturing costs","It doubled its number of warehouses","It expanded into eleven countries"],"a":0,"ex":"Under her leadership, the subsidiary ... cut delivery times by a fifth：在她的帶領下，子公司把送貨時間縮短了五分之一。倉庫的部分是她上任後要把歐洲的四座整併成兩座，不是增加；文中沒有提到製造成本；十一個國家是整個集團目前的營運範圍，不是子公司的擴張成果。"},{"q":"Which area is NOT mentioned as part of Ms. Raman's new responsibilities?","o":["Manufacturing","Marketing","Distribution","Procurement"],"a":1,"ex":"第三段說 Ms. Raman will oversee manufacturing, procurement, and distribution，oversee 是「督導」。製造、採購、配送都列在其中，只有 marketing（行銷）沒有提到，所以是答案。"}]},
{"id":"r990-21","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"email","ti":"Your first week at Calloway Engineering","tx":"To: New employees starting June 2\nFrom: Rachel Kim, Human Resources\nSubject: Your first week at Calloway Engineering\n\nDear new colleagues,\n\nWelcome to Calloway Engineering. To help you settle in quickly, we have prepared a comprehensive onboarding program that will occupy most of your first week.\n\nOn Monday morning, please report to the reception desk in the main lobby by 8:45, where you [1] ------- by a member of my team and issued a security badge. The morning session covers company policies, payroll procedures, and your leave entitlements. After lunch, each of you will be introduced to the mentor who has been [2] ------- to guide you through your first three months.\n\nTuesday through Thursday will be spent in your respective departments, where you will shadow experienced colleagues and learn the workflow. On Friday, all new staff will convene again for a short debrief with the managing director.\n\nPlease bring photo identification and your bank details on the first day. [3] -------, we will be unable to add you to the payroll in time for the June payment.\n\nIf you have any questions beforehand, do not hesitate to contact me.\n\nBest regards,\nRachel Kim","zh":"收件人：6 月 2 日到職的新進員工\n寄件人：人力資源部 Rachel Kim\n主旨：您在 Calloway Engineering 的第一週\n\n各位新同事好：\n\n歡迎加入 Calloway Engineering。為了幫助各位盡快適應，我們準備了一套完整的入職培訓計畫，將占去各位第一週的大部分時間。\n\n星期一早上，請在 8:45 前到大廳的接待櫃台報到，屆時我的團隊成員會在那裡迎接您，並發給您門禁識別證。上午的課程涵蓋公司政策、薪資作業流程，以及您應享有的休假權益。午餐後，我們會為每位新人介紹指定的輔導員，他們將在您到職的前三個月帶領您。\n\n星期二到星期四，各位將待在各自的部門，跟在資深同事身邊觀摩，並熟悉工作流程。星期五，所有新進員工會再次集合，與總經理進行簡短的檢討座談。\n\n第一天請攜帶附照片的身分證件及您的銀行帳戶資料。否則，我們將來不及把您加入薪資名單，趕不上六月的發薪。\n\n在此之前如有任何問題，歡迎隨時與我聯絡。\n\nRachel Kim 敬上","w":[880,814,753,831,977,868,754,956],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["are meeting","will be met","will meet","have met"],"a":1,"ex":"空格後面有 by a member of my team（由我的團隊成員），主詞 you 是「被迎接」的人，而且星期一還沒到，所以要用未來式被動 will be met；後面的 issued a security badge 也共用 will be，同樣是被動。will meet、have met、are meeting 都是主動，後面不能接 by a member of my team。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["depreciated","deterred","designated","disclosed"],"a":2,"ex":"the mentor who has been ------- to guide you：be designated to do 是「被指定去做某事」，designated（被指定的）最合適。depreciated 是「貶值的」、disclosed 是「被揭露的」、deterred 是「被嚇阻的」，放在這裡意思都不通。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Likewise","Meanwhile","Therefore","Otherwise"],"a":3,"ex":"前一句請新人帶證件和銀行資料，後一句說「我們將無法及時把您加入薪資名單」，這是「如果沒帶」的後果，所以用 Otherwise（否則）。Therefore 是「因此」，會變成「帶了所以無法加入」，邏輯相反；Likewise 是「同樣地」；Meanwhile 是「同時」。"}]},
{"id":"r990-22","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"memo","ti":"Changes to this year's performance appraisals","tx":"MEMO\n\nTo: All department heads\nFrom: Thomas Becker, Director of Human Resources\nSubject: Changes to this year's performance appraisals\n\nAnnual appraisals will commence on November 3. In response to feedback from last year, we are making two changes intended to make the process fairer and more transparent.\n\nFirst, managers will no longer rely [1] ------- on their own observations. Each appraisal will also draw on comments solicited from two of the employee's colleagues and, in the case of supervisors, from their subordinates.\n\nSecond, every rating must be supported by concrete examples. A rating given without [2] ------- may be perceived as arbitrary and will be returned to the manager for revision.\n\nCompleted forms are due by November 28. Because salary adjustments and incentive payments are calculated from the final ratings, any forms submitted after that date [3] ------- the December payroll for the entire department.\n\nManagers are accountable for the accuracy of every appraisal they sign. Training sessions on the new format will be held on October 20 and 22, and attendance is mandatory.","zh":"備忘錄\n\n收件人：各部門主管\n寄件人：人力資源處長 Thomas Becker\n主旨：今年績效考核的變更事項\n\n年度考核將於 11 月 3 日開始。因應去年收到的意見，我們將做兩項調整，目的是讓考核過程更公平、更透明。\n\n第一，主管不再只憑自己的觀察來評分。每一份考核還會參考向該員工的兩位同事徵詢而來的意見；如果受評者是主管，也會徵詢其下屬的意見。\n\n第二，每一項評等都必須有具體事例佐證。沒有正當理由的評等可能會被視為主觀武斷，並將退回給主管修改。\n\n填妥的表格須於 11 月 28 日前繳交。由於調薪和獎金都是根據最終評等計算，任何在該日期之後才交的表格，都會延誤整個部門十二月的薪資發放。\n\n主管必須為自己簽核的每一份考核的正確性負責。新格式的說明訓練將於 10 月 20 日及 22 日舉行，所有主管都必須參加。","w":[812,974,916,933,847,787,889,856],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["exclusively","unanimously","respectively","approximately"],"a":0,"ex":"rely exclusively on 是「完全只依賴」；下一句說 Each appraisal will also draw on comments ...（還會參考其他人的意見），可見以前是「只」靠主管自己的觀察，所以用 exclusively（專門地、僅僅）。respectively 是「分別地」、unanimously 是「全體一致地」、approximately 是「大約」，都不能用來修飾 rely on。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["justification","justifiably","justified","justify"],"a":0,"ex":"without 是介系詞，後面要接名詞，所以選 justification（正當理由）。justify 是動詞、justified 是形容詞或過去分詞、justifiably 是副詞，都不能單獨放在 without 後面。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["will delay","have delayed","delayed","delaying"],"a":0,"ex":"截止日 11 月 28 日還沒到，這句講的是「之後才交的表格將會延誤十二月的薪資」，是對未來的說明，所以用未來式 will delay。delayed 和 have delayed 表示過去或已經發生的事，時間不合；delaying 不是完整的動詞，句子會沒有主要動詞。"}]},
{"id":"r990-23","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"notice","ti":"Temporary closure of the east parking garage","tx":"NOTICE TO EMPLOYEES AND VISITORS\n\nTemporary Closure of the East Parking Garage\n\nThe east parking garage will be closed from Monday, August 4, through Friday, August 22, while a contractor resurfaces levels 1 to 3 and installs new lighting. The work, originally planned for the spring, [1] ------- because of a delay in obtaining a building permit.\n\nDuring the closure, staff are asked to use the west garage or the surface lot on Dover Street. To [2] ------- the shortage of spaces, the company will subsidize monthly transit passes for August and run a shuttle from Dover Street to the main entrance every fifteen minutes. To maintain accessibility, the spaces reserved for visitors with limited mobility have been moved to the front of the west garage.\n\nAny vehicle remaining in the east garage after 6:00 P.M. on Sunday, August 3, will be towed at the owner's expense. [3] -------, we urge you to move your car before the weekend.\n\nPlease expect intermittent noise near the east entrance of the premises while the work is under way. We apologize for the inconvenience and thank you for your cooperation.","zh":"員工及訪客公告\n\n東側停車場暫時關閉\n\n東側停車場將自 8 月 4 日星期一起關閉，至 8 月 22 日星期五為止，期間承包商將重鋪一至三樓的地面，並安裝新的照明設備。這項工程原定在春季進行，但因為建築許可證延遲核發而延期。\n\n關閉期間，請同仁改用西側停車場或 Dover Street 的平面停車場。為了緩解車位不足的情況，公司將補助八月份的大眾運輸月票，並安排接駁車，每十五分鐘一班，從 Dover Street 開往正門。為了維持無障礙通行，保留給行動不便訪客的車位已移到西側停車場的前方。\n\n8 月 3 日星期日下午 6:00 之後仍停在東側停車場的車輛，將被拖吊，費用由車主負擔。因此，我們呼籲您在週末前把車移走。\n\n施工期間，本場區東側入口附近預計會有斷斷續續的噪音。造成不便，敬請見諒，並感謝您的配合。","w":[766,984,972,872,913,904,758],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["postponed","was postponed","is postponing","has postponed"],"a":1,"ex":"主詞 The work（工程）是「被延期」的對象，而且延期是已經發生的事，所以用過去式被動 was postponed。postponed、is postponing、has postponed 都是主動用法，後面必須有受詞，而工程不會自己去延後別的東西。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["advocate","accumulate","authorize","alleviate"],"a":3,"ex":"alleviate the shortage 是「緩解短缺」；後面說公司補助月票、安排接駁車，都是為了減輕車位不足的問題，所以選 alleviate。accumulate 是「累積」、authorize 是「批准」、advocate 是「提倡」，和 shortage 搭配意思都不對。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Nevertheless","Similarly","Accordingly","Otherwise"],"a":2,"ex":"前一句說逾時未移的車會被拖吊，後一句呼籲大家週末前把車移走，後者是根據前者而來的結論，所以用 Accordingly（因此、相應地）。Nevertheless 是「然而」，表示轉折；Otherwise 是「否則」；Similarly 是「同樣地」，都接不上。"}]},
{"id":"r990-24","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"letter","ti":"Preliminary approval of your business loan","tx":"Summit Trust Bank\nCommercial Lending Department\n\nMay 19\n\nMs. Angela Rossi\nRossi Catering Ltd.\n\nDear Ms. Rossi,\n\nWe are pleased to inform you that your application for a business loan of $150,000 has received preliminary approval from our lending committee.\n\nThe loan will be secured by the kitchen equipment that you have offered as [1] -------. An independent appraisal has valued this equipment at $210,000, which is sufficient for the amount requested. Interest will accrue at a fixed annual rate of 6.2 percent, and the loan is to be repaid in monthly installments over five years.\n\nBefore final approval can be granted, you are required to [2] ------- any outstanding debts owed by your company and to provide audited financial statements for the last two fiscal years. These must reach us by June 6.\n\nOnce we [3] ------- these documents, a definitive decision will be issued within five business days. Please note that a provision in the loan agreement entitles the bank to review the interest rate if repayments are missed.\n\nShould you have any inquiries, please contact me directly.\n\nYours sincerely,\nEdward Lin\nSenior Lending Officer","zh":"Summit Trust Bank\n商業貸款部\n\n5 月 19 日\n\nAngela Rossi 女士\nRossi Catering Ltd.\n\nRossi 女士您好：\n\n很高興通知您，您申請的 150,000 美元企業貸款已獲得本行貸款審查委員會的初步核准。\n\n這筆貸款將以您提供作為擔保品的廚房設備作擔保。經獨立鑑價，這批設備的價值為 210,000 美元，足以支應您申請的金額。利息將以 6.2% 的固定年利率計算，貸款須在五年內按月分期償還。\n\n在最終核准之前，您必須揭露貴公司所有尚未清償的債務，並提供最近兩個會計年度經會計師查核的財務報表。這些文件必須在 6 月 6 日前送達本行。\n\n我們收到這些文件後，將在五個工作天內做出最終決定。請注意，依貸款合約中的一項條款，若有未按期還款的情形，本行有權重新審視利率。\n\n如有任何疑問，請直接與我聯絡。\n\n資深貸款專員\nEdward Lin 敬上","w":[863,846,812,965,922,875,891,816],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["correspondence","clientele","compliance","collateral"],"a":3,"ex":"offer ... as collateral 是「提供…作為擔保品」；前面說 The loan will be secured by the kitchen equipment（貸款以廚房設備作擔保），所以選 collateral（抵押品、擔保品）。clientele 是「顧客群」、compliance 是「遵守」、correspondence 是「通信」，都不能說成「提供設備作為…」。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["disclosing","disclose","disclosure","disclosed"],"a":1,"ex":"be required to 後面要接原形動詞，所以選 disclose（揭露）；後面的 and to provide 也是原形動詞，前後對稱。disclosure 是名詞、disclosed 是過去式或過去分詞、disclosing 是動名詞或現在分詞，都不能接在 to 後面構成不定詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["will receive","had received","have received","received"],"a":2,"ex":"Once（一旦）引導的時間子句講未來的事時，要用現在式或現在完成式代替未來式；主要子句是 will be issued，所以選 have received。will receive 不能用在 Once 子句裡；received 和 had received 是過去的時態，和後面的未來式不合。"}]},
{"id":"r990-25","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"article","ti":"Halden Stores posts stronger second quarter","tx":"Halden Stores Posts Stronger Second Quarter\n\nHalden Stores, the home-furnishings retailer, reported yesterday that second-quarter revenue rose 9 percent to $412 million, [1] ------- analysts' forecasts for the third consecutive quarter.\n\nChief executive Nora Fielding attributed the result to a surge in online orders and to the firm's decision last year to consolidate its two distribution centers, which reduced delivery costs. Profit margins, [2] -------, narrowed slightly as inflation pushed up the cost of imported timber.\n\nThe company said it does not intend to raise prices in the foreseeable future. Instead, it will seek to offset higher material costs by buying more of its products from domestic suppliers.\n\n[3] ------- The board has approved a dividend of 45 cents per share, up from 40 cents a year earlier, payable on September 15.\n\nHalden's shares closed 3 percent higher following the announcement. The retailer, which operates 140 stores, expects revenue for the full fiscal year to grow by between 6 and 8 percent.","zh":"Halden Stores 第二季業績走強\n\n居家家具零售商 Halden Stores 昨日公布，第二季營收成長 9%，達到 4.12 億美元，連續第三季超越分析師的預測。\n\n執行長 Nora Fielding 把這項成果歸功於線上訂單激增，以及公司去年決定整併兩座配送中心，因而降低了配送成本。不過，由於通貨膨脹推升了進口木材的成本，利潤率略為縮小。\n\n該公司表示，在可預見的未來不打算調漲售價。相反地，公司會設法向國內供應商採購更多產品，以抵銷上漲的原料成本。\n\n股東也將分享到業績改善的成果。董事會已核准每股配發 45 美分的股息，高於一年前的 40 美分，將於 9 月 15 日發放。\n\n消息公布後，Halden 的股價收盤上漲 3%。這家擁有 140 家門市的零售商預期，整個會計年度的營收將成長 6% 到 8%。","w":[945,998,992,942,755,867,990,808],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["deterring","curtailing","withholding","surpassing"],"a":3,"ex":"營收成長 9%，而且是 for the third consecutive quarter（連續第三季），surpass forecasts 是「超越預測」，所以用分詞 surpassing。curtailing 是「削減」、withholding 是「扣留」、deterring 是「嚇阻」，都不能和 analysts' forecasts 搭配來描述營收成長的結果。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["therefore","otherwise","however","moreover"],"a":2,"ex":"前面都是好消息（營收成長、配送成本降低），這一句卻說利潤率 narrowed slightly（略為縮小），語意轉折，所以用 however（然而）。therefore 是「因此」、moreover 是「此外」（用來補充同方向的資訊）、otherwise 是「否則」，都不表示轉折。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["Several stores are scheduled to close next month.","Shareholders will also share in the improved results.","Analysts had expected revenue to rise much more.","Customers have complained about slow deliveries."],"a":1,"ex":"下一句說 The board has approved a dividend of 45 cents per share, up from 40 cents（董事會核准提高股息），dividend 是發給股東的股息，所以前面應該是「股東也將分享到業績改善的成果」。文中沒有提到關店或顧客抱怨配送太慢；而「分析師原本預期營收成長更多」則和第一段的 surpassing analysts' forecasts（超越分析師預測）互相矛盾。"}]},
{"id":"r990-26","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"advertisement","ti":"The Aldgate Hotel: built for business","tx":"The Aldgate Hotel: Built for Business\n\nLocated two blocks from the financial district, the Aldgate Hotel has served a corporate clientele for more than forty years. Following a year-long renovation, we are proud to reopen with facilities designed around the way professionals actually work.\n\nEvery guest room now features an ergonomic desk, high-speed connectivity, and soundproofed windows, creating an environment [1] ------- to concentration. Our six meeting rooms accommodate between 8 and 120 people, and each [2] ------- with state-of-the-art presentation equipment. A dedicated events team will coordinate the logistics of your meeting, from catering to printing, so that you can focus on your agenda.\n\nWhen the working day is over, guests can relax in our rooftop restaurant or make use of the fitness center, which is open around the clock.\n\nGuests staying three nights or more are [3] ------- to complimentary airport transfers and late checkout. Rates start at $189 per night, and companies that book at least fifty room nights a year qualify for our corporate discount.\n\nTo make a reservation or to request a quotation for an event, call 555-0163 or visit our website.","zh":"Aldgate Hotel：為商務而生\n\nAldgate Hotel 距離金融區只有兩個街區，四十多年來一直服務企業客群。經過為期一年的整修，我們很榮幸重新開幕，所有設施都是依照專業人士實際的工作方式而設計。\n\n現在每間客房都備有符合人體工學的書桌、高速網路連線和隔音窗，營造出有助於專注的環境。我們的六間會議室可容納 8 到 120 人，每一間都配備最先進的簡報設備。專屬的活動團隊會為您協調會議的各項後勤事務，從餐飲到文件印製一手包辦，讓您可以專心在議程上。\n\n結束一天的工作後，房客可以到頂樓餐廳放鬆一下，或使用全天候開放的健身中心。\n\n住宿三晚以上的房客，可享有免費機場接送及延後退房。房價每晚 189 美元起，每年訂房達五十個房晚以上的公司，可享企業優惠價。\n\n如需訂房或索取活動報價，請致電 555-0163 或上我們的網站。","w":[806,903,771,864,907,921,797,939],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["contractual","comprehensive","conducive","considerable"],"a":2,"ex":"conducive to 是固定搭配，意思是「有助於…」；符合人體工學的書桌、隔音窗營造出「有助於專注」的環境，所以選 conducive。considerable 是「相當大的」、contractual 是「合約的」、comprehensive 是「全面的」，後面都不接 to concentration。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["has equipped","is equipped","equipping","equips"],"a":1,"ex":"be equipped with 是「配備有…」；主詞 each（每一間會議室）是「被配備」設備的對象，所以用被動 is equipped。equips 和 has equipped 是主動，後面要直接接受詞，不能接 with；equipping 不是完整的動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["entitled","entitlement","entitling","entitle"],"a":0,"ex":"be entitled to 是「有權享有…」；are 後面要用過去分詞 entitled 構成被動。entitle 是原形動詞，不能接在 are 後面；entitlement 是名詞（應得的權利），「房客是權利」說不通；are entitling 是主動進行式，後面要有受詞。"}]},
{"id":"r990-27","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"email","ti":"Update on your delayed order","tx":"To: Samuel Greene, Greene's Garden Center\nFrom: Lucy Hartmann, Customer Accounts, Tolland Tools\nSubject: Update on your delayed order\n\nDear Mr. Greene,\n\nI am writing to apologize for the delay in delivering your order of 200 pruning sets, which was due to reach you on April 10.\n\nAn unprecedented surge in spring orders, in conjunction with an equipment failure at our steel supplier's plant, has left us with a [1] ------- of more than 3,000 unfilled orders. Production returned to full capacity on Monday, and your order [2] ------- priority status. We now expect to dispatch the consignment by April 24. To expedite delivery, it will travel by air freight rather than by road, and we will bear the additional cost.\n\n[3] -------, we recognize that the delay may already have affected your own sales. We would therefore like to offer you a 10 percent reduction on this invoice.\n\nIf this arrangement is not acceptable, you may cancel the order without incurring any charge. Please let me know by Friday how you wish to proceed.\n\nWith apologies once again,\nLucy Hartmann","zh":"收件人：Samuel Greene，Greene's Garden Center\n寄件人：Lucy Hartmann，Tolland Tools 客戶帳務部\n主旨：您延遲訂單的最新進度\n\nGreene 先生您好：\n\n您訂購的 200 組修枝工具原本應於 4 月 10 日送達，卻延遲交貨，我特此來信致歉。\n\n春季訂單出現空前的激增，加上我們鋼材供應商的工廠設備故障，導致我們積壓了三千多筆尚未出貨的訂單。生產線已在星期一恢復全面運轉，您的訂單也已列為優先處理。我們目前預計在 4 月 24 日前發貨。為了加快送達速度，這批貨將改用空運而非陸運，額外的費用由我們負擔。\n\n儘管如此，我們明白這次延誤可能已經影響到您店裡的銷售。因此，我們願意為這張發票提供九折優惠。\n\n如果您無法接受這樣的安排，您可以取消訂單，不會產生任何費用。請在星期五前告訴我您希望如何處理。\n\n再次向您致歉。\nLucy Hartmann","w":[905,992,767,804,991,832,932,954],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["boardroom","blueprint","backlog","benchmark"],"a":2,"ex":"a backlog of ... unfilled orders 是「積壓的未出貨訂單」；訂單激增又遇到供應商設備故障，結果就是訂單堆積，所以選 backlog（積壓）。benchmark 是「基準」、blueprint 是「藍圖」、boardroom 是「董事會會議室」，都不能說成「一個…的未出貨訂單」。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["gave","has been given","has given","is giving"],"a":1,"ex":"主詞 your order（您的訂單）是「被給予」優先處理資格的對象，所以要用被動；而且這是到現在已經完成的事，用現在完成式被動 has been given。has given、is giving、gave 都是主動，會變成「訂單把優先權給了別人」，意思不通。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["For example","Consequently","In other words","Nevertheless"],"a":3,"ex":"前面說公司會改用空運並負擔費用，後面卻說「我們明白延誤可能已經影響您的銷售」，意思是「即使做了這些補救，影響還是造成了」，是讓步轉折，所以用 Nevertheless（儘管如此）。Consequently 是「因此」、For example 是「例如」、In other words 是「換句話說」，都不表示轉折。"}]},
{"id":"r990-28","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"announcement","ti":"Riverside Charity Run set for May 9","tx":"Riverside Charity Run Set for May 9\n\nHollis & Byrne Insurance is proud to sponsor the twelfth annual Riverside Charity Run, which will take place on Saturday, May 9. The run has become a prominent event in the city's calendar, [1] ------- more than 2,000 participants last year.\n\nAll [2] ------- from registration fees will go to the Riverside Literacy Project, an outreach program that provides free reading classes for adults.\n\nEmployees who wish to take part may register through the staff portal until April 24. The company will subsidize the $30 entry fee in full, and participants are entitled to leave work two hours early on the Friday before the race.\n\nVolunteers are also needed to hand out water along the route and to direct runners at the finish line. [3] ------- A short briefing will be given at 7:00 A.M. on the day of the race.\n\nThe renowned marathon runner Carla Voss, who has endorsed the run since its first year, will present the medals. For further details, contact Peter Aldana in Human Resources at extension 2215.","zh":"Riverside 慈善路跑 5 月 9 日開跑\n\nHollis & Byrne Insurance 很榮幸贊助第十二屆年度 Riverside 慈善路跑，活動將於 5 月 9 日星期六舉行。這項路跑已成為本市年度行事曆上的重要活動，去年吸引了超過 2,000 人參加。\n\n報名費的所有收益將捐給 Riverside Literacy Project，這是一項為成人提供免費閱讀課程的外展計畫。\n\n想參加的同仁可在 4 月 24 日前透過員工入口網站報名。公司將全額補助 30 美元的報名費，參加者並可在賽前的星期五提早兩小時下班。\n\n我們也需要志工在路線沿途發水，以及在終點線引導跑者。不需要任何相關經驗。比賽當天上午 7:00 會有簡短的行前說明。\n\n知名馬拉松選手 Carla Voss 從第一屆起就支持這項路跑，她將擔任頒獎人。詳情請洽人力資源部 Peter Aldana，分機 2215。","w":[878,813,848,972,939,869,964],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["attracting","attracted","attraction","attracts"],"a":0,"ex":"逗號前面已經是完整的句子（The run has become a prominent event），後面要用現在分詞 attracting 帶出補充說明，表示「（這項活動）去年吸引了兩千多人」。attracted 和 attracts 是一般動詞，前面沒有連接詞，不能直接接在逗號後面；attraction 是名詞，後面不能接 more than 2,000 participants 當受詞。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["minutes","premises","proceeds","credentials"],"a":2,"ex":"proceeds from ... will go to 是「…的收益將捐給」，proceeds 指活動的收益，和 registration fees（報名費）以及慈善活動的情境相符。premises 是「場所」、credentials 是「資歷證明」、minutes 是「會議紀錄」，都不是從報名費而來、可以捐出去的東西。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["No previous experience is necessary.","Registration closed at the end of March.","The race has been postponed until next year.","Runners must bring their own water."],"a":0,"ex":"前一句在徵求志工發水和引導跑者，後一句說當天早上會有 A short briefing（簡短的行前說明），中間最合理的是「不需要任何經驗」，因為到時會有人說明。其他三句都和文中內容矛盾：活動確定在 5 月 9 日舉行，並沒有延期；報名到 4 月 24 日才截止；志工會在沿途發水，跑者不必自己帶水。"}]},
{"id":"r990-29","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"memo","ti":"Spending measures for the second half of the year","tx":"MEMO\n\nTo: All department managers\nFrom: Linda Osei, Chief Financial Officer\nSubject: Spending measures for the second half of the year\n\nAs you know, first-half revenue fell 8 percent short of our forecast, leaving the company with a projected deficit of $2.4 million for the fiscal year. It is therefore imperative that we [1] ------- spending in every department without delay.\n\nThe following measures apply from July 1. All non-essential travel is suspended, and any expenditure above $2,000 must be authorized by my office. Hiring is frozen except for positions that generate revenue directly. In addition, the funds set aside for the office refurbishment [2] ------- to the product launch in September.\n\nI want to reiterate that these steps are not a first move toward downsizing. [3] -------, they are intended to protect jobs by restoring a surplus before the end of the year.\n\nManagers will be held accountable for staying within their revised budgets, which will be distributed on Friday. I appreciate your cooperation during this difficult period.","zh":"備忘錄\n\n收件人：各部門經理\n寄件人：財務長 Linda Osei\n主旨：下半年的支出管控措施\n\n如各位所知，上半年營收比預測少了 8%，使公司本會計年度預估將出現 240 萬美元的虧損。因此，我們務必立刻削減每個部門的支出。\n\n以下措施自 7 月 1 日起實施。所有非必要的出差一律暫停，凡是超過 2,000 美元的支出都必須經過我的辦公室核准。除了能直接創造營收的職位之外，人員招募全面凍結。此外，原本預留給辦公室整修的經費，將重新分配給九月的產品上市活動。\n\n我要重申，這些措施並不是裁員的前兆。相反地，這些措施是為了在年底前恢復盈餘，藉此保住大家的工作。\n\n各部門經理必須負責把支出控制在修訂後的預算之內，新預算將於星期五發給各位。感謝各位在這段艱難時期的配合。","w":[769,892,881,961,821,953,983,793],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["escalate","accrue","deteriorate","curtail"],"a":3,"ex":"前一句說公司預估會有 deficit（虧損），所以「務必要削減支出」，curtail spending 是「削減支出」。escalate 是「升高」，在虧損的情況下增加支出不合理；accrue 是「（利息、費用）累積產生」；deteriorate 是「惡化」，後面不接受詞，也不能和 spending 這樣搭配。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["will reallocate","will be reallocated","reallocating","have reallocated"],"a":1,"ex":"主詞 the funds（經費）是「被重新分配」的對象，要用被動；而且措施從 7 月 1 日才開始，是未來的事，所以用 will be reallocated。will reallocate 和 have reallocated 是主動，經費不會自己去分配別的東西；reallocating 不是完整的動詞。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["For instance","On the contrary","In addition","As a result"],"a":1,"ex":"前一句說這些措施 are not a first move toward downsizing（不是裁員的前兆），後一句說它們是為了 protect jobs（保住工作），前後意思相反，所以用 On the contrary（相反地）。In addition 是「此外」、As a result 是「結果」、For instance 是「例如」，都無法表達「不是…，恰恰相反…」的關係。"}]},
{"id":"r990-30","lv":990,"p":6,"k":"notice","ti":"Scheduled network maintenance this weekend","tx":"NOTICE FROM THE IT DEPARTMENT\n\nScheduled Network Maintenance This Weekend\n\nOver the past month, many of you have reported intermittent connectivity problems, particularly on the fourth floor. Our technicians have inspected every workstation and found no defects. The underlying cause is aging network equipment [1] ------- a fault in any individual computer.\n\nTo resolve the problem, new switches will be [2] ------- throughout the building this weekend. As a result, the network, including e-mail and the shared drives, will be unavailable from 8:00 P.M. on Friday until 6:00 A.M. on Monday. Staff who need to work during this period should copy the necessary files to their laptops before leaving on Friday.\n\nWe expect that all of the work [3] ------- by the time the office reopens on Monday. As a preemptive measure, however, two technicians will be onsite that morning to troubleshoot any remaining problems. If your connection is still unstable after the upgrade, please call the help desk at extension 3000 instead of restarting the equipment yourself.\n\nWe apologize for the disruption and thank you for your patience.","zh":"資訊部公告\n\n本週末網路例行維護\n\n過去一個月，許多同仁反映網路連線時斷時續，四樓的情況尤其明顯。我們的技術人員已經檢查過每一台工作站，並未發現任何故障。根本原因在於網路設備老舊，而不是哪一台電腦出了問題。\n\n為了解決這個問題，本週末將在整棟大樓部署新的交換器。因此，包括電子郵件和共用磁碟在內的網路，將從星期五晚上 8:00 起停止服務，到星期一早上 6:00 恢復。這段期間需要工作的同仁，請在星期五下班前把需要的檔案複製到筆記型電腦裡。\n\n我們預計所有工程會在星期一辦公室恢復上班前完成。不過，為了預防萬一，當天早上會有兩名技術人員在現場，協助排除任何殘留的問題。如果升級後您的連線仍然不穩定，請撥分機 3000 聯絡服務台，不要自行重新啟動設備。\n\n造成不便，敬請見諒，並感謝您的耐心配合。","w":[904,771,757,890,971,902,943],"qs":[{"q":"[1]","o":["in case of","as well as","rather than","because of"],"a":2,"ex":"前一句說檢查過每一台工作站都 found no defects（沒有故障），所以原因是「設備老舊，而不是個別電腦的問題」，用 rather than（而不是）。as well as 是「以及」，會變成電腦也有問題，和前一句矛盾；because of 是「因為」、in case of 是「萬一發生…時」，語意都不通。"},{"q":"[2]","o":["depreciated","deployed","disclosed","deterred"],"a":1,"ex":"deploy 是「部署（設備、系統）」，new switches will be deployed throughout the building 是「在整棟大樓部署新的交換器」。depreciated 是「折舊、貶值」、deterred 是「被嚇阻」、disclosed 是「被揭露」，都不能用來說明安裝網路設備。"},{"q":"[3]","o":["was completing","will have been completed","has completed","had been completed"],"a":1,"ex":"by the time the office reopens on Monday（到星期一辦公室恢復上班時）指的是未來的某個時間點，表示「到那時將已經完成」，要用未來完成式；主詞 the work 是被完成的對象，所以是被動 will have been completed。had been completed 是過去完成式，時間不合；was completing 和 has completed 是主動，時態也不對。"}]}];
